d":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf6-483","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
{"parentUuid":"06bdd011-17d1-4f27-8cc9-1180caf2c8ba","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a4fdab2f-a8e8-4d8b-94dc-8723c2dad09a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DK6vjLUSvmfNje3PYEvcyb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tcargo/caliper-docgen-core: minor\n3\tcargo/caliper-docgen: minor\n4\tcargo/caliper-docgen-napi: minor\n5\tnpm/caliper-docgen: minor\n6\tnpm/caliper-docgen-storybook: minor\n7\tnpm/caliper-docgen-napi: minor\n8\tnpm/caliper-docgen-vite-plugin: minor\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tLarge inherited sources are collapsed by default, wherever they are declared, and the checker's answer is collapsed the same way.\n12\t\n13\tBreaking for the Storybook addon: its default output changes. `collapseInheritedProps` now defaults to `'dependencies'` instead of `'none'`, so an inherited source too large to be an API (a dependency's DOM, ARIA or style-system set of more than 30 props, or any source of more than 200 props) is one inheritance layer of names instead of hundreds of Controls rows. A component's own props and the notable inherited ones are still listed. The props inside such a layer get no Controls row, and a story's `args` naming one shows it as undocumented: that is intended, and a later release adds the props stories and call sites use. Set `collapseInheritedProps: 'none'` to list every inherited prop as before.\n14\t\n15\tFor every consumer, the default `dependencies` mode now also collapses a source in the project's own code that declares more than 200 props (a design system's style props, such as Chakra's `SystemProperties` in Chakra's own repository); before, only dependency sources collapsed. With the checker on, the props a collapsed layer names are no longer also listed from the checker's answer: the checker's props follow the structural answer's layers, so both give the same layers.\n16\t"}]},"uuid":"11c0a02d-7d2e-48c5-9c87-ca90d4f732c2","timestamp":"2026-11-16T06:31:58.204Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8/.changeset/collapse-large-sources-by-default.md","content":"---\ncargo/caliper-docgen-core: minor\ncargo/caliper-docgen: minor\ncargo/caliper-docgen-napi: minor\nnpm/caliper-docgen: minor\nnpm/caliper-docgen-storybook: minor\nnpm/caliper-docgen-napi: minor\nnpm/caliper-docgen-vite-plugin: minor\n---\n\nLarge inherited sources are collapsed by default, wherever they are declared, and the checker's answer is collapsed the same way.\n\nBreaking for the Storybook addon: its default output changes. `collapseInheritedProps` now defaults to `'dependencies'` instead of `'none'`, so an inherited source too large to be an API (a dependency's DOM, ARIA or style-system set of more than 30 props, or any source of more than 200 props) is one inheritance layer of names instead of hundreds of Controls rows. A component's own props and the notable inherited ones are still listed. The props inside such a layer get no Controls row, and a story's `args` naming one shows it as undocumented: that is intended, and a later release adds the props stories and call sites use. Set `collapseInheritedProps: 'none'` to list every inherited prop as before.\n\nFor every consumer, the default `dependencies` mode now also collapses a source in the project's own code that declares more than 200 props (a design system's style props, such as Chakra's `SystemProperties` in Chakra's own repository); before, only dependency sources collapsed. With the checker on, the props a collapsed layer names are no longer also listed from the checker's answer: the checker's props follow the structural answer's layers, so both give the same layers.\n","numLines":16,"startLine":1,"totalLines":16}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"06bdd011-17d1-4f27-8cc9-1180caf2c8ba","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entr