see docs/adr/README.md). Facts you may rely on (verify against code/docs when unsure, do not invent): (1) collapse by default: `collapseInheritedProps` default 'dependencies' in the Storybook addon (was 'none'), a source of more than 200 props (ambient/DOM/ARIA/style sources more than 30) becomes one inheritance layer of names; own and notable props stay listed; Chakra median props per component 845 -> 139, Button Controls ~1141 -> ~146; this is a BREAKING change for the addon's default output: `Action:` set 'none' to keep every inherited prop; also: a prop the project itself declares next to React's types (`ComponentProps<'div'> & { className: 'mine' }`) stays listed, a collapsed layer never repeats a listed prop, and a source behind an unresolved `Omit` key set is not collapsed (PR 485). (2) memory: a checker extract of Chakra's own source took 42 GB on 0.11.0; now a type over 18,724 nodes is cut to its name and extraction stops asking the checker past a heap budget (60% of available memory, at most 8 GiB, cgroup-aware, including cgroup v1 comounted mounts), with a SEMANTIC_BACKEND warning. (3) the checker skips converting props held in collapsed layers (faster, memory down, output unchanged). (4) schema version 8: collapsed layers gain `used` (ambient members consumers pass or bodies read); consumers must read version 8 (Vite plugin, Storybook addon, scripts, oracle already do). (5) factory-built components (Chakra `chakra('div', {variants})`, `createLeafComponent`) gain own props: variant keys, render function annotation (props types, destructuring defaults, discriminated unions), only for proven render functions; Spectrum missing props 2216 -> 359, Chakra 13 -> 11. (6) structural answer: `ReactElement`/`JSX.Element` stay named; structural `Partial/Required/Pick/Omit` are NOT expanded (the checker answers them), type parameters and handler aliases as the existing changeset says; read the current file and keep only what is true on main (the expansion bullets were