{"attachment":{"command":"","content":"","durationMs":32,"exitCode":0,"hookEvent":"","hookName":"","stderr":"","stdout":"","toolUseID":"","type":"hook_success"},"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"mf6-483","isSidechain":false,"parentUuid":"0e88f655-80cb-4687-8d51-7179ee40102a","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano","timestamp":"2026-11-16T06:34:27.924Z","type":"attachment","userType":"external","uuid":"c30ba681-9d3a-4ea3-b9cd-bf3a69d7956e","version":"2.1.311"}
{"parentUuid":"053d0fcd-c64c-4e7d-8e5e-d67457d09a74","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"08d8dfa9-12ad-4625-aa58-11e91c631e1d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kfkk1o7gJUCPDZf8ZVHZCt","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"The weekly record: Caliper, react-docgen-typescript (RDT) and react-docgen on the five pinned corpora.\n\nFor each corpus it records, per tool, the wall time and peak RSS of one whole run (process start included), and for\nCaliper the canonical JSON's size. Recall is measured against RDT: of the components RDT reports with props, how many\nthe tool also reports (same file, same name), and of their props, how many it lists, split into the props `@types/react`\ndeclares and the rest. react-docgen follows imports to the file that declares a type but infers nothing, and lists none\nof React's props. With --oracle it also records how often TypeScript 7.1's checker contradicts each tool's prop types,\nover every prop the checker finds, and the headline of scripts/headline.py: how many of the props of the components Caliper\nreports are right. With --agent-eval it also asks a fixed list of questions about real components and scores what a\nreader of Caliper's output answers against the checker (scripts/agent_eval.py).\n\n--previous FILE compares with an earlier record (the last green run's artifact) and writes --issue FILE for the workflow\nto open or update one issue with, when a wrong type is above the gate or rises, a reader's question is answered\nsilent-wrong, or a whole run is over a budget (scripts/headline.py). Drift in time, memory and recall against RDT is\nlisted in the summary, not alarmed on.\n\nEvery measured command's exit status and wall time go to stderr, and --out is written after each corpus. A corpus whose\ncommand exits non-zero, dies of a signal or runs past STEP_TIMEOUT is recorded under `failed` (step, exit status, last\n20 lines of stderr) and the next corpus still runs; the exit status is 1 at the end if any failed. --enforce-budgets\nalso exits 1 when a whole run is over its corpus's budget: the `corpora-budget` job of the release pull request.\n\nUsage: scripts/weekly.py --bin BIN [--corpus NAME]... [--corpora DIR] [--work DIR] [--runs N] [--oracle] [--agent-eval]\n                         [--previous FILE] [--baseline-failed] [--enforce-budgets] [--out FILE] [--markdown FILE] [--issue FILE]\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport statistics\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport time\n\nimport agent_eval\nimport corpora\nimport headline\nimport oracle_data\nimport schema_version\nfrom corpora import ROOT, run_once, selected\n\nBASELINE_FAILED = \"The baseline download failed, so this run was not compared with last week's record.\"\nSLOWER = 1.10\nRECALL_DROP = 0.02\n# The rules that decide what the reference is: the exclusions and the pairing. Raise it when a change to them moves recall,\n# so that a record is never compared on recall with one made under other rules (a record without it is version 1).\nREFERENCE_VERSION = 3\n# The universe of the oracle's scores (`oracle.tools`): version 2 counts candidate components only, naming a default export\n# by its declaration; a record without it is version 1, which counted every function the checker takes for a component\n# and named a default export `default`. Version 3 pairs a checker component with Caliper's by file and export name\n# (ADR 0027) where version 2 paired by a normalised display name. Version 4 scores a prop whose checker type the oracle did\n# not evaluate as `not judged` where version 3 scored it identical, and classes a declaration's path by one rule\n# (apps/oracle/src/path-classes.json). Version 5 extracts with the checker, the default, where version 4 and earlier ran\n# `--no-checker`, so the oracle's props and verdicts are not the same measurement. Raise it when a change moves what the\n# oracle counts.\nUNIVERSE_VERSION = 5\n# No single measured command runs longer than this (seconds): a hung one is killed and its corpus recorded as failed.\nSTEP_TIMEOUT = 2400\n\naccuracy-rows/\nadr-0028/\nadr27p2-addon/\nadr27p2-save/\nadr27p2-save2/\nbigint-scratch/\ncaches/\ncallisto-0.20/\nchecker-default/\nci-corpora-budget-gate/\nclean-code/\ncleanup-patches/\ncollapse-default/\ncorpora/\ncrates-slice-1/\ncrates-slice-2/\nentire-0.13.2/\nentire-fix-backup/\nentire-probe/\nextract-speed/\nextractor-fix/\nfallback/\nfinal-perf/\nfirst-answer/\nfix417/\ngate-large/\nir-spike/\nlean-a-before/\nlive-demo/\nlogs/","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ef648e3d-3d0d-4bda-8a03-83058ca2fc0a","timestamp":"2026-11-16T06:34:30.750Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"The weekly record: Caliper, react-docgen-typescript (RDT) and react-docgen on the five pinned corpora.\n\nFor each corpus it records, per tool, the wall time and peak RSS of one whole run (process start included), and for\nCaliper the canonical JSON's size. Recall is measured against RDT: of the components RDT reports with props, how many\nthe tool also reports (same file, same name), and of their props, how many it lists, split into the props `@types/react`\ndeclares and the rest. react-docgen follows imports to the file that declares a type but infers nothing, and lists none\nof React's props. With --oracle it also records how often TypeScript 7.1's checker contradicts each tool's prop types,\nover every prop the checker finds, and the headline of scripts/headline.py: how many of the props of the components Caliper\nreports are right. With --agent-eval it also asks a fixed list of questions about real components and scores what a\nreader of Caliper's output answers against the checker (scripts/agent_eval.py).\n\n--previous FILE compares with an earlier record (the last green run's artifact) and writes --issue FILE for the workflow\nto open or update one issue with, when a wrong type is above the gate or rises, a reader's question is answered\nsilent-wrong, or a whole run is over a budget (scripts/headline.py). Drift in time, memory and recall against RDT is\nlisted in the summary, not alarmed on.\n\nEvery measured command's exit status and wall time go to stderr, and --out is written after each corpus. A corpus whose\ncommand exits non-zero, dies of a signal or runs past STEP_TIMEOUT is recorded under `failed` (step, exit status, last\n20 lines of stderr) and the next corpus still runs; the exit status is 1 at the end if any failed. --enforce-budgets\nalso exits 1 when a whole run is over its corpus's budget: the `corpora-budget` job of the release pull request.\n\nUsage: scripts/weekly.py --bin BIN [--corpus NAME]... [--corpora DIR] [--work DIR] [--runs N] [--oracle] [--agent-eval]\n                         [--previous FILE] [--baseline-failed] [--enforce-budgets] [--out FILE] [--markdown FILE] [--issue FILE]\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport statistics\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport time\n\nimport agent_eval\nimport corpora\nimport headline\nimport oracle_data\nimport schema_version\nfrom corpora import ROOT, run_once, selected\n\nBASELINE_FAILED = \"The baseline download failed, so this run was not compared with last week's record.\"\nSLOWER = 1.10\nRECALL_DROP = 0.02\n# The rules that decide what the reference is: the exclusions and the pairing. Raise it when a change to them moves recall,\n# so that a record is never compared on recall with one made under other rules (a record without it is version 1).\nREFERENCE_VERSION = 3\n# The universe of the oracle's scores (`oracle.tools`): version 2 counts candidate components only, naming a default export\n# by its declaration; a record without it is version 1, which counted every function the checker takes for a component\n# and named a default export `default`. Version 3 pairs a checker component with Caliper's by file and export name\n# (ADR 0027) where version 2 paired by a normalised display name. Version 4 scores a prop whose checker type the oracle did\n# not evaluate as `not judged` where version 3 scored it identical, and classes a declaration's path by one rule\n# (apps/oracle/src/path-classes.json). Version 5 extracts with the checker, the default, where version 4 and earlier ran\n# `--no-checker`, so the oracle's props and verdicts are not the same measurement. Raise it when a change moves what the\n# oracle counts.\nUNIVERSE_VERSION = 5\n# No single measured command runs longer than this (seconds): a hung one is killed and its corpus recorded as failed.\nSTEP_TIMEOUT = 2400\n\naccuracy-rows/\nadr-0028/\nadr27p2-addon/\nadr27p2-save/\nadr27p2-save2/\nbigint-scratch/\ncaches/\ncallisto-0.20/\nchecker-default/\nci-corpora-budget-gate/\nclean-code/\ncleanup-patches/\ncollapse-default/\ncorpora/\ncrates-slice-1/\ncrates-slice-2/\nentire-0.13.2/\nentire-fix-backup/\nentire-probe/\nextract-speed/\nextractor-fix/\nfallback/\nfinal-perf/\nfirst-answer/\nfix417/\ngate-large/\nir-spike/\nlean-a-before/\nlive-demo/\nlogs/","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"fe63fbd2-b989-4be7-bf12-8b0b037ef844","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","branch":"mf6-483","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxViolations":[],"sandboxed":true,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"053d0fcd-c64c-4e7d-8e5e-d67457d09a74","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf6-483","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
