{"parentUuid":"ef712565-9ef9-4ac8-a8b3-e3f2c272d10a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch69S8Tg9E88RmRr2t425","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The user-focused changesets are up as #488 (base `main`, trail 405).\n\n**What changed**\n- **Rewritten:** all ten pending changesets, to the AGENTS.md convention. I read the collapse one: bold lead-in, a separate `**Breaking:**` paragraph for the addon's new `collapseInheritedProps: 'dependencies'` default, an `**Action:**` line (set it to `'none'` to keep every inherited prop), and bullets with the Chakra numbers (845 → 139 median props, `Button` about 1,141 → about 146 Controls rows). Struct fields, cache schema numbers and ADR numbers are gone.\n- **New:** `keep-own-props-beside-collapsed-sources` (patch) for #485.\n- **Docs:** it fixed the stale default row in `docs/storybook-parity.md`.\n- **Checks (worker):** `just lint`, `just doc-check machete typos` and `just semver` all exit 0.\n\nI read only the collapse changeset in full. The other nine follow the same pattern according to the worker, but I haven't read them. Read them before the release PR.\n\n**Open from the alpha list**\n- The oracle run is in progress.\n- The \"Execute approved release\" failure and the corpora gate's first real run are untouched.\n- Docs: `STATUS.md` numbers, `MIGRATING.md` and the README limits.\n- Your three decisions: what \"alpha\" means, who the audience is, and whether the addon default flip ships in the first alpha.\n\nI'm waiting on your answers to the decisions, and I'll report the oracle run when it lands."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":425,"cache_read_input_tokens":738494,"output_tokens":530,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"e