{"parentUuid":"2b140350-f637-4408-b2f9-71cd50ef1513","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5b05b98d-d44f-4d67-93b5-bcbfb7aafe7f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R4V9M4rnh8M7YDhr8tZKc1","type":"tool_result","content":"/Users/gabe/.proto/shims/callisto\n{\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-16T07:10:12.460137Z\",\"level\":\"WARN\",\"message\":\"Failed to load the community plugins registry; continuing without it\",\"error\":\"FailedRequest { url: \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/moonrepo/proto/master/registry/data/community.json\\\", error: reqwest::Error { kind: Request, url: \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/moonrepo/proto/master/registry/data/community.json\\\", source: hyper_util::client::legacy::Error(Connect, TunnelUnsuccessful) } }\",\"target\":\"proto_core::loader\"}\ncallisto 0.5.0\n## Recover a failed release\n\nA release that stopped is picked up by the next push to `main` or the daily run, and `drain` chains any further unfinished ones. While one is unfinished, the release pull request is not refreshed, and a newer release pull request published first would release without any warning that the older version was never tagged. Finish the older release first.\n\nList what is unfinished, oldest first, with what is missing:\n\n```sh\ncallisto release pending --from 2daef9276b234fcc04d8994d91210eeccd88d7e8\n```\n\n`--from` is the `RELEASE_PENDING_FROM` value in `callisto-release.yml`. Without it, `release pending` reads the committed decision of the 10 newest release commits and stops with E166 on one whose decision no longer decodes. The pin is the 0.9.0 release commit (`2daef927`).\n\n0.9.0 was published before GitHub Releases were enabled, so `release pending` lists it as missing its GitHub Release. The first run after this flow lands finishes it: the build matrix rebuilds 0.9.0 from its release commit and Callisto creates the GitHub Release with five attested assets. Callisto adopts the crates, npm packages and tags that already landed (`docs/releasing.md` in `orin-dx/callisto`, \"Publication che\n\n- **A job failed:** \"Re-run failed jobs\". Callisto adopts the effects that already landed and does the rest.\n- **A release cannot finish:** dispatch it by hand with its release commit, `gh workflow run callisto-release.yml --ref main -f release_source_sha=<merged release commit>`. If it will never finish, skip it by moving `RELEASE_PENDING_FROM` to a newer release commit.\n- **E148, release PR snapshot changed:** the `version-pr` job planned from a release PR that changed before it applied the plan. Nothing was changed. Re-run the failed job, or push to `main` again.\n- **`ArtifactAssetDiffers`:** a rebuilt asset is not byte-identical to the one already on the draft Release. Delete the mismatched asset, then dispatch the workflow again with the release commit:\n\n  ```sh\n  gh release delete-asset \"cargo/caliper-docgen@x.y.z\" \"<asset>\" --yes\n  gh workflow run callisto-release.yml --ref main -f release_source_sha=<merged release commit>\n  ```\n<sandbox_violations>\ndeny network-outbound raw.githubusercontent.com:443 (not in this command's allowed_domains — re-run the command with this host listed if it needs it)\n</sandbox_violations>","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"38601bc1-709c-4252-b73c-05e6413dea75","timestamp":"2026-11-16T07:10:12.639Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"/Users/gabe/.proto/shims/callisto\n{\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-16T07:10:12.460137Z\",\"level\":\"WARN\",\"message\":\"Failed to load the community plugins registry; continuing without it\",\"error\":\"FailedRequest { url: \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/moonrepo/proto/master/registry/data/community.json\\\", error: reqwest::Error { kind: Request, url: \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/moonrepo/proto/master/registry/data/community.json\\\", source: hyper_util::client::legacy::Error(Connect, TunnelUnsuccessful) } }\",\"target\":\"proto_core::loader\"}\ncallisto 0.5.0\n## Recover a failed release\n\nA release that stopped is picked up by the next push to `main` or the daily run, and `drain` chains any further unfinished ones. While one is unfinished, the release pull request is not refreshed, and a newer release pull request published first would release without any warning that the older version was never tagged. Finish the older release first.\n\nList what is unfinished, oldest first, with what is missing:\n\n```sh\ncallisto release pending --from 2daef9276b234fcc04d8994d91210eeccd88d7e8\n```\n\n`--from` is the `RELEASE_PENDING_FROM` value in `callisto-release.yml`. Without it, `release pending` reads the committed decision of the 10 newest release commits and stops with E166 on one whose decision no longer decodes. The pin is the 0.9.0 release commit (`2daef927`).\n\n0.9.0 was published before GitHub Releases were enabled, so `release pending` lists it as missing its GitHub Release. The first run after this flow lands finishes it: the build matrix rebuilds 0.9.0 from its release commit and Callisto creates the GitHub Release with five attested assets. Callisto adopts the crates, npm packages and tags that already landed (`docs/releasing.md` in `orin-dx/callisto`, \"Publication che\n\n- **A job failed:** \"Re-run failed jobs\". Callisto adopts the effects that already landed and does the rest.\n- **A release cannot finish:** dispatch it by hand with its release commit, `gh workflow run callisto-release.yml --ref main -f release_source_sha=<merged release commit>`. If it will never finish, skip it by moving `RELEASE_PENDING_FROM` to a newer release commit.\n- **E148, release PR snapshot changed:** the `version-pr` job planned from a release PR that changed before it applied the plan. Nothing was changed. Re-run the failed job, or push to `main` again.\n- **`ArtifactAssetDiffers`:** a rebuilt asset is not byte-identical to the one already on the draft Release. Delete the mismatched asset, then dispatch the workflow again with the release commit:\n\n  ```sh\n  gh release delete-asset \"cargo/caliper-docgen@x.y.z\" \"<asset>\" --yes\n  gh workflow run callisto-release.yml --ref main -f release_source_sha=<merged release commit>\n  ```","stderr":"<sandbox_violations>\ndeny network-outbound raw.githubusercontent.com:443 (not in this command's allowed_domains — re-run the command with this host listed if it needs it)\n</sandbox_violations>","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"be3485c0-fd50-4ed9-ac2e-7d006c85832d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","branch":"mf6-483","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","platform":"macos"}},"toolResultRemedy":{"kind":"sandbox_violation"},"sandboxViolations":[{"kind":"network","host":"raw.githubusercontent.com","port":443}],"sandboxed":true,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2b140350-f637-4408-b2f9-71cd50ef1513","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf6-483","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
