ackages/storybook/src/options.ts) or a regression introduced by recent work (PR 469 collapse, 476 skip conversion, 485 own-props-beside-React keep, 483 `used`/`declaration_origin`, 480 factory)? Method: build the release binary from origin/main (own CARGO_TARGET_DIR under /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/diag/, rust 1.99.1 first on PATH /Users/gabe/.rustup/toolchains/1.99.1-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin; reuse /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/target/release/caliper-docgen (built from de016f69) if present: do not rebuild needlessly). On a SMALL project first (a tiny fixture with `export function Btn(props: React.ComponentProps<'button'> & {own?: string}) {}` and a `forwardRef` one, @types/react installed: use gate-large or a shadcn component from /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/corpora/shadcn-ui) run `extract --json` in the 4 combinations (checker on/off x htmlAttributes full/none/curated if the flag exists, collapse dependencies/none) and diff the props, inheritance layers and notableInherited; then do the same on the Chakra Button from the corpus Storybook demo (/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/sb-demo/, find how the addon is configured there: is `collapseInheritedProps` set explicitly in its .storybook/main config? check that FIRST: the demo was copied from an earlier harness that may pin 'none' or `htmlAttributes`), and read what the addon actually hands Storybook (packages/storybook/src/ provider/argtypes conversion: how a collapsed layer, notable props and DOM props become argTypes; whether the addon re-adds DOM props itself). Use `git log -S` / `git bisect`-style checks against the 0.11.0 tag and the commits above ONLY if needed to decide intended vs regression (for (B): does 0.11.0's checker lane drop them too?). Deliverable: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/diagnosis.md (short): for each symptom, the cause with file:line, whether intended by an ADR/doc (quote it) or a regression (name the commi