{"parentUuid":"b6daebc0-e191-42ce-9848-1ffde0c3cedd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch6ES6cdWdxynza96REWM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KW8cheD84GkWfR34TqQuPP","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/diagnosis.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2023,"cache_read_input_tokens":785605,"output_tokens":81,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2023,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":81,"cache_read_input_tokens":785605,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2023,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2023},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KW8cheD84GkWfR34TqQuPP":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/diagnosis.md"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"51a65e90-9ffc-4809-bc8c-bfe9595d2dd7","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch6ES6FoxJic8BuhEu1cZ","requestRef":"e8a30521-98ab-4dee-9067-a9463762b96b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"088df54d-6a6b-47c5-8370-dde6e3430a1d","timestamp":"2026-11-16T07:43:29.077Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf6-483","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
{"parentUuid":"088df54d-6a6b-47c5-8370-dde6e3430a1d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6483c60f-fcd1-4e62-a8ae-96fa3720a7b8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KW8cheD84GkWfR34TqQuPP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Diagnosis: 437 Controls rows (A) and the @types/react recall drop (B)\n2\t\n3\tBinary: the existing `oracle-run/target/release/caliper-docgen` (built from de016f69, not rebuilt). Source read at de016f69. Fixture: `sb-demo/src` itself (`Badge` = `ComponentProps<'span'> & {variant, asChild}`, `Button` = Chakra `ButtonProps & ComponentProps<'button'> & {...}`), `@types/react` and `@chakra-ui/react` installed in `sb-demo/node_modules`. Run: `extract --src sb-demo/src --json --no-cache` x checker on/off x `--html-attributes full|curated|none` x `--collapse-inherited-props dependencies|none` (12 runs, all exit 0).\n4\t\n5\tDemo config checked first: `sb-demo/.storybook/main.ts` sets only `srcDirs`, `semanticWaitMs`, `prefetchStories`. No `collapseInheritedProps` and no `htmlAttributes`, so the defaults apply: `dependencies` and `full` (`packages/storybook/src/options.ts:40,43` pass `undefined` through; `crates/core/src/types/options.rs:47,196`).\n6\t\n7\t## Measured (Button / Badge)\n8\t\n9\tRows = props + notableInherited, which is what `docgen_info` hands Storybook (`crates/core/src/pipeline/rdt.rs:63-72`). Layers are never expanded into rows.\n10\t\n11\t- off (structural), full, dependencies: Button 439 props (289 from @types/react), Badge 281 (279 from @types/react). SystemProperties is a layer (706 names).\n12\t- on (checker), full, dependencies: Button 150 props (0 from @types/react, 130 Chakra `Conditions`), Badge 2. The element layers `React.ComponentProps[button]` and `[span]` have `totalProps 0` and no members.\n13\t- on or off, curated, dependencies: Button 150 + 164 notable = 314 rows, Badge 2 + 159 notable = 161.\n14\t- none: Button 150, Badge 2. Collapse `none` changes only SystemProperties (Button 853 props); it never changes the DOM props.\n15\t\n16\tStorybook shows Button 437 and Badge 280. That is the structural full count (439 and 281) less `key`/`ref`/`children` that `arg-types.ts:12-20` and the RDT `children` rule drop. The CLI checker lane shows 150 and 2 for the same input. **The two checker lanes disagree on the same options.**\n17\t\n18\t## A. 437 rows in Storybook\n19\t\n20\t**Cause.** The session (Storybook) merge keeps every `@types/react` prop under `htmlAttributes: 'full'`. In `crates/core/src/react_types.rs:439-441`, `checker_prop_used` gives `HtmlAttributeMode::Full => true`, and it is applied in `crates/core/src/pipeline/semantic_hook.rs:338-341`. `react_props_wanted` (`react_types.rs:452-453`) asks the checker for all of them. Collapse never touches `@types/react`:\n21\t\n22\t- `options.rs:89-90`: \"A file in `node_modules` that is not a dependency's (`@types/react`, TypeScript's libraries) never collapses: React's attributes follow `htmlAttributes`.\"\n23\t- In the checker lane, `checker_sources` skips `react_declared` props (`crates/core/src/types/semantic.rs:715-716`).\n24\t\n25\tThe roughly 130 Chakra condition props (`_active`, `2xl`...) are listed because `Conditions` is not ambient by name (`crates/core/src/types/ambient.rs:101-105`: only `SystemProps`, `*StyleProps` and style prefixes). Its 130 props are under `LARGE_API_SOURCE` (200), so it is not collapsed (`options.rs:98-100`).\n26\t\n27\t**Intended or regression: intended.** It was already so in 0.11.0. `caliper-docgen-core@0.11.0` has the same `Full => true` at `react_types.rs:440`, and the earlier 0.11.0 demo showed 1,141 rows. The default is documented in `options.rs:17-19`: \"`Full`: actually resolve `@types/react`'s real ... interface chain, matching RDT's full ~250-300 attributes per element — the default.\" No recent PR (469, 476, 485, 483, 480) changed it. PR 469's collapse correctly removed the 705 SystemProperties rows (1,141 to 437).\n28\t\n29\tThe expectation \"the DOM source is one layer with 8 notable props under `dependencies`\" is not what any doc promises. The nearest mode, `curated`, keeps every `aria-*`, every non-Capture handler and the globals (`react_types.rs:415-418`), so it gives 164 notables, not 8.\n30\t\n31\t**Effect on a Storybook user.** About 290 DOM, ARIA and event rows bury the roughly 20 real props. Badge (two own props) shows 280 rows.\n32\t\n33\t**Smallest fix**, from smallest:\n34\t\n35\t1. Config only. Default `htmlAttributes` to `'curated'` in the addon (`packages/storybook/src/options.ts:40`, and its docs in `packages/storybook/src/index.ts:6-12`). Button goes to 314 rows (measured), Badge to 161. This is a small change but not the expected shape.\n36\t2. Contract fix (recommended). When collapse is not `none`, treat `@types/react`'s element attributes as the ambient layer they already are by `is_dom_file`. List only `notable_html_attrs(element)` (17 names for `button`) as `notableInherited`, and leave the rest to the element layer. Files:\n37\t   - `crates/core/src/types/options.rs`: drop the \"@types/react never collapses\" exemption at :89-90 and :102, or add a React clause.\n38\t   - `crates/core/src/react_types.rs`: `checker_prop_used` / `react_props_wanted` take the collapse mode.\n39\t   - `crates/core/src/pipeline/semantic_hook.rs`: `apply`, `target_of`.\n40\t   - The structural resolver's full-mode React expansion, so both lanes agree, plus a model test like `collapse_model.rs`.\n41\t\n42\t   Button would show about 150 + 17 = **about 167 rows** (146 to 150 Chakra and own props, including the 130 conditions, plus the button notables). Badge would show 2 + span notables.\n43\t\n44\t   Optionally, add Chakra's `Conditions` as a style source in `ambient.rs` (it is ambient, 130 > 30). Button would then drop to about 20 own + 17 notable = **about 37 rows**.\n45\t\n46\t## B. @types/react recall about 0% with the checker on (CLI, collapse `none`)\n47\t\n48\t**Cause.** The whole-project (CLI) merge drops every `react_declared` prop of a component that has any inheritance layer. In `crates/core/src/types/semantic.rs:429-437` (`apply_props`): `.filter(|prop| !prop.react_declared || (!layered && entry.props.contains_key(&prop.name)))`, followed by `Unanswered::Drop` (:439), which also removes the structural ones. The element layer is meant to \"stand for them\" (`crates/semantic/src/component.rs:33-37`). It ignores `htmlAttributes` and collapse, so `--collapse-inherited-props none` does not bring them back.\n49\t\n50\tAntd (23.9%) and Spectrum (86.8%) are higher because many of their components have no element layer, and the `!layered` branch keeps React props the structural pass listed.\n51\t\n52\t**Intended or regression: intended, and documented, since `d072b2ed` (2026-10-26, \"merge the checker's props by name and apply htmlAttributes once after the merge\").** That commit is in `caliper-docgen-core@0.8.0` through 0.11.0. 0.11.0 has the same filter at `semantic.rs:357-365`. B appeared in the weekly when 0.11.0 turned the checker on by default; it is not new in PRs 469 to 485. Docs that state it:\n53\t\n54\t- `docs/type-checker-integration.md:66`: \"Props `@types/react` declares are excluded by declaring file.\"\n55\t- `docs/type-checker-integration.md:203`: \"With the whole-project merge, `@types/react`'s props stay with the inheritance layers as for any component, so the CLI shows the component's own props.\"\n56\t- `docs/measurement.md:256`: \"`@types/react` props are counted apart (the whole-project checker pass leaves them out).\"\n57\t\n58\tThe weekly's \"@types/react props\" recall column (`docs/measurement.md:94`) was not adapted. It still counts listed props, so it measures a removed feature.\n59\t\n60\t**But it contradicts `htmlAttributes: 'full'`** (`options.rs:17-19`, \"matching RDT's full ~250-300 attributes\"). The layer that \"stands for\" them carries `totalProps: 0` and no member names, only `htmlElement`. A CLI JSON or `--format rdt` consumer therefore gets no DOM prop names unless it resolves the element itself. The session lane (A) does the opposite under the same option.\n61\t\n62\t**Effect on a Storybook user: none.** The addon goes through the session lane (`semantic_hook.rs`), not `apply_props`. The effect is on CLI and RDT-format consumers and on the weekly metric.\n63\t\n64\t**Smallest fix.** Pick one contract for both lanes; the one described under A, fix 2, settles both. On its own:\n65\t\n66\t- (a) Metric only: in `scripts/weekly.py`, count an `@types/react` RDT prop as recalled when the component has an element layer for that element (or report the column only for `--no-checker`). One file. No output change.\n67\t- (b) Output: make `apply_props` (`semantic.rs:429-437`) filter with `react_types::checker_prop_used(mode, ...)` as the session does. That restores full-mode recall to about 99%, and Chakra's CLI Button to 439. Files: `crates/core/src/types/semantic.rs` (`apply_props`, `merge_semantic` needs the mode), `crates/cli/src/commands/extract.rs:169` (passes it), and the CLI's target building so `react_wanted` is `None` under `full`.\n68\t\n69\tNot run: a bisect (not needed: the 0.11.0 tag has both policies), and the Chakra corpus Button in the CLI (the report already has 146 + layer there). No repo files changed.\n70\t"}]},"uuid":"a51a23ae-fdd0-4e9e-96a0-6ff4f2f88b2c","timestamp":"2026-11-16T07:43:29.146Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/diagnosis.md","content":"# Diagnosis: 437 Controls rows (A) and the @types/react recall drop (B)\n\nBinary: the existing `oracle-run/target/release/caliper-docgen` (built from de016f69, not rebuilt). Source read at de016f69. Fixture: `sb-demo/src` itself (`Badge` = `ComponentProps<'span'> & {variant, asChild}`, `Button` = Chakra `ButtonProps & ComponentProps<'button'> & {...}`), `@types/react` and `@chakra-ui/react` installed in `sb-demo/node_modules`. Run: `extract --src sb-demo/src --json --no-cache` x checker on/off x `--html-attributes full|curated|none` x `--collapse-inherited-props dependencies|none` (12 runs, all exit 0).\n\nDemo config checked first: `sb-demo/.storybook/main.ts` sets only `srcDirs`, `semanticWaitMs`, `prefetchStories`. No `collapseInheritedProps` and no `htmlAttributes`, so the defaults apply: `dependencies` and `full` (`packages/storybook/src/options.ts:40,43` pass `undefined` through; `crates/core/src/types/options.rs:47,196`).\n\n## Measured (Button / Badge)\n\nRows = props + notableInherited, which is what `docgen_info` hands Storybook (`crates/core/src/pipeline/rdt.rs:63-72`). Layers are never expanded into rows.\n\n- off (structural), full, dependencies: Button 439 props (289 from @types/react), Badge 281 (279 from @types/react). SystemProperties is a layer (706 names).\n- on (checker), full, dependencies: Button 150 props (0 from @types/react, 130 Chakra `Conditions`), Badge 2. The element layers `React.ComponentProps[button]` and `[span]` have `totalProps 0` and no members.\n- on or off, curated, dependencies: Button 150 + 164 notable = 314 rows, Badge 2 + 159 notable = 161.\n- none: Button 150, Badge 2. Collapse `none` changes only SystemProperties (Button 853 props); it never changes the DOM props.\n\nStorybook shows Button 437 and Badge 280. That is the structural full count (439 and 281) less `key`/`ref`/`children` that `arg-types.ts:12-20` and the RDT `children` rule drop. The CLI checker lane shows 150 and 2 for the same input. **The two checker lanes disagree on the same options.**\n\n## A. 437 rows in Storybook\n\n**Cause.** The session (Storybook) merge keeps every `@types/react` prop under `htmlAttributes: 'full'`. In `crates/core/src/react_types.rs:439-441`, `checker_prop_used` gives `HtmlAttributeMode::Full => true`, and it is applied in `crates/core/src/pipeline/semantic_hook.rs:338-341`. `react_props_wanted` (`react_types.rs:452-453`) asks the checker for all of them. Collapse never touches `@types/react`:\n\n- `options.rs:89-90`: \"A file in `node_modules` that is not a dependency's (`@types/react`, TypeScript's libraries) never collapses: React's attributes follow `htmlAttributes`.\"\n- In the checker lane, `checker_sources` skips `react_declared` props (`crates/core/src/types/semantic.rs:715-716`).\n\nThe roughly 130 Chakra condition props (`_active`, `2xl`...) are listed because `Conditions` is not ambient by name (`crates/core/src/types/ambient.rs:101-105`: only `SystemProps`, `*StyleProps` and style prefixes). Its 130 props are under `LARGE_API_SOURCE` (200), so it is not collapsed (`options.rs:98-100`).\n\n**Intended or regression: intended.** It was already so in 0.11.0. `caliper-docgen-core@0.11.0` has the same `Full => true` at `react_types.rs:440`, and the earlier 0.11.0 demo showed 1,141 rows. The default is documented in `options.rs:17-19`: \"`Full`: actually resolve `@types/react`'s real ... interface chain, matching RDT's full ~250-300 attributes per element — the default.\" No recent PR (469, 476, 485, 483, 480) changed it. PR 469's collapse correctly removed the 705 SystemProperties rows (1,141 to 437).\n\nThe expectation \"the DOM source is one layer with 8 notable props under `dependencies`\" is not what any doc promises. The nearest mode, `curated`, keeps every `aria-*`, every non-Capture handler and the globals (`react_types.rs:415-418`), so it gives 164 notables, not 8.\n\n**Effect on a Storybook user.** About 290 DOM, ARIA and event rows bury the roughly 20 real props. Badge (two own props) shows 280 rows.\n\n**Smallest fix**, from smallest:\n\n1. Config only. Default `htmlAttributes` to `'curated'` in the addon (`packages/storybook/src/options.ts:40`, and its docs in `packages/storybook/src/index.ts:6-12`). Button goes to 314 rows (measured), Badge to 161. This is a small change but not the expected shape.\n2. Contract fix (recommended). When collapse is not `none`, treat `@types/react`'s element attributes as the ambient layer they already are by `is_dom_file`. List only `notable_html_attrs(element)` (17 names for `button`) as `notableInherited`, and leave the rest to the element layer. Files:\n   - `crates/core/src/types/options.rs`: drop the \"@types/react never collapses\" exemption at :89-90 and :102, or add a React clause.\n   - `crates/core/src/react_types.rs`: `checker_prop_used` / `react_props_wanted` take the collapse mode.\n   - `crates/core/src/pipeline/semantic_hook.rs`: `apply`, `target_of`.\n   - The structural resolver's full-mode React expansion, so both lanes agree, plus a model test like `collapse_model.rs`.\n\n   Button would show about 150 + 17 = **about 167 rows** (146 to 150 Chakra and own props, including the 130 conditions, plus the button notables). Badge would show 2 + span notables.\n\n   Optionally, add Chakra's `Conditions` as a style source in `ambient.rs` (it is ambient, 130 > 30). Button would then drop to about 20 own + 17 notable = **about 37 rows**.\n\n## B. @types/react recall about 0% with the checker on (CLI, collapse `none`)\n\n**Cause.** The whole-project (CLI) merge drops every `react_declared` prop of a component that has any inheritance layer. In `crates/core/src/types/semantic.rs:429-437` (`apply_props`): `.filter(|prop| !prop.react_declared || (!layered && entry.props.contains_key(&prop.name)))`, followed by `Unanswered::Drop` (:439), which also removes the structural ones. The element layer is meant to \"stand for them\" (`crates/semantic/src/component.rs:33-37`). It ignores `htmlAttributes` and collapse, so `--collapse-inherited-props none` does not bring them back.\n\nAntd (23.9%) and Spectrum (86.8%) are higher because many of their components have no element layer, and the `!layered` branch keeps React props the structural pass listed.\n\n**Intended or regression: intended, and documented, since `d072b2ed` (2026-10-26, \"merge the checker's props by name and apply htmlAttributes once after the merge\").** That commit is in `caliper-docgen-core@0.8.0` through 0.11.0. 0.11.0 has the same filter at `semantic.rs:357-365`. B appeared in the weekly when 0.11.0 turned the checker on by default; it is not new in PRs 469 to 485. Docs that state it:\n\n- `docs/type-checker-integration.md:66`: \"Props `@types/react` declares are excluded by declaring file.\"\n- `docs/type-checker-integration.md:203`: \"With the whole-project merge, `@types/react`'s props stay with the inheritance layers as for any component, so the CLI shows the component's own props.\"\n- `docs/measurement.md:256`: \"`@types/react` props are counted apart (the whole-project checker pass leaves them out).\"\n\nThe weekly's \"@types/react props\" recall column (`docs/measurement.md:94`) was not adapted. It still counts listed props, so it measures a removed feature.\n\n**But it contradicts `htmlAttributes: 'full'`** (`options.rs:17-19`, \"matching RDT's full ~250-300 attributes\"). The layer that \"stands for\" them carries `totalProps: 0` and no member names, only `htmlElement`. A CLI JSON or `--format rdt` consumer therefore gets no DOM prop names unless it resolves the element itself. The session lane (A) does the opposite under the same option.\n\n**Effect on a Storybook user: none.** The addon goes through the session lane (`semantic_hook.rs`), not `apply_props`. The effect is on CLI and RDT-format consumers and on the weekly metric.\n\n**Smallest fix.** Pick one contract for both lanes; the one described under A, fix 2, settles both. On its own:\n\n- (a) Metric only: in `scripts/weekly.py`, count an `@types/react` RDT prop as recalled when the component has an element layer for that element (or report the column only for `--no-checker`). One file. No output change.\n- (b) Output: make `apply_props` (`semantic.rs:429-437`) filter with `react_types::checker_prop_used(mode, ...)` as the session does. That restores full-mode recall to about 99%, and Chakra's CLI Button to 439. Files: `crates/core/src/types/semantic.rs` (`apply_props`, `merge_semantic` needs the mode), `crates/cli/src/commands/extract.rs:169` (passes it), and the CLI's target building so `react_wanted` is `None` under `full`.\n\nNot run: a bisect (not needed: the 0.11.0 tag has both policies), and the Chakra corpus Button in the CLI (the report already has 146 + layer there). No repo files changed.\n","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":70}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"088df54d-6a6b-47c5-8370-dde6e3430a1d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf6-483","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
