{"parentUuid":"5f2b4b9f-a4f1-4e49-b3b5-80864e87f755","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch6w379m2UccJ66XVXsC9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015jrBj55PR9KjP5STsj5s9S","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"T4: list props by usage evidence in both lanes","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"Implement slice T4 of ADR 0028 (trail 405) on `origin/main` (`git fetch origin` first; if blocked use existing refs); branch `feat/list-props-by-usage`; commit locally in small commits; I push and open the PR. THE PRODUCT GOAL (the user's words, non-negotiable): 'produce the best results, not overwhelming massive numbers that are not useful to anyone': narrow what is listed BY USAGE. Today (measured at main de016f69, see /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/REPORT.md and diagnosis.md, read both) the Storybook Controls for Chakra `Button` show 437 rows and a plain `ComponentProps<'span'>` component `Badge` shows 280, because `htmlAttributes` defaults to `full` (every @types/react attribute is listed, ADR 0023, chosen for parity with react-docgen-typescript) and `@types/react` never collapses, and Chakra's ~130 `Conditions` props are under the 200 threshold; the CLI checker lane drops React props whenever an element layer exists (types/semantic.rs `apply_props` ~429-437, with the layer carrying no names), so the two lanes disagree (CLI Button 150, Badge 2). The evidence exists but no consumer applies it: crates/core/src/relevance/ (`decide`, `Member`, `Row`/`used`; ADR 0028 'Output'/'Owner defaults': props passed at call sites at a 20% floor, story args no floor, ambient members passed are typed rows even if ambient, JSDoc/literal unions alone do not promote an inherited prop, handed_on is unknown never guessed, NO name lists), T2 props_type, T3 forwarding, T6 call_sites, `relevance::apply` (the one sink), `InheritedLayer::used`, pipeline/semantic_hook.rs and types/semantic.rs (session and whole-project merges), react_types.rs (`checker_prop_used`, `react_props_wanted`, `notable_html_attrs`). Read ADR 0028 fully (docs/adr/0028-relevance-evidence-and-the-checker-scheduler.md: the T4 line of the slice plan, Output and Consequences), /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/shrink/findings-synthesis.md and the Pre-push gate in /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/worker-contract.md. Task: make the LISTING (props + notableInherited that become Controls rows / RDT-format props) follow the relevance rows `decide` already computes, in BOTH lanes through the one sink: a DOM/ARIA/event attribute, a Chakra condition prop or any member of a collapsed or ambient source is a listed typed row only when `decide` says so (passed or forwarded or read or named in a story arg at the floor, or named by the props type per the ADR defaults); otherwise it stays only in the layer's names (`members`, and `used` where applicable). The component's own props always stay listed. `htmlAttributes` keeps meaning 'which DOM attributes are KNOWN as data' (so `full` can stay the default input if that is how the ADR separates data from rows: decide and justify; if the cleanest result is to make the default `curated`/other, say so and why with numbers; amend ADR 0023/0028 via the adr skill for any change of contract) but it must no longer decide how many ROWS a user sees. Existing notable props (`notable_html_attrs`, a name list) are a rule the user rejected for new work: replace them by evidence where the ADR plans it (R9) or keep only as the fallback when there is NO usage evidence at all, and say which. When evidence is unavailable (no call sites, no stories, handed_on) the safe default must not hide a prop a consumer needs and must not dump hundreds: define it explicitly (e.g. own props + props named by the props type, not whole ambient sources) and test it. Acceptance, measure and report in the PR body: (1) Storybook Controls rows for Chakra Button and Badge in dev mode using the demo at /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/sb-demo/ (see sb-demo/serve.sh and setup-stories.sh; playwright MCP tools via ToolSearch select:mcp__playwright__browser_navigate,mcp__playwright__browser_evaluate,mcp__playwright__browser_wait_for) before 437/280 and after: target Button near its own-props count plus what stories/call sites actually use (a few dozen at most), Badge near 2 plus used ones; (2) CLI `extract` for the same components agrees with Storybook's rows; (3) five-corpus output sizes and medians before/after (median props per component: Chakra 139, Mantine 72, antd 14, shadcn 2, Spectrum 11 today with collapse): they must not grow, and the CLI JSON must still carry the layer names so no information is lost; (4) the oracle's headline must not get worse: run the weekly's oracle step on antd and shadcn only (scripts/weekly.py --oracle --corpus antd --corpus shadcn, see its usage; costs a little: this is authorised for these two corpora) and show wrong stays 0 (antd 1 today) and the right-rate does not fall; (5) timing/memory not worse on Chakra first/second run (release build; load is noisy: report load). Tests first, model-based: extend crates/core/tests/relevance_model.rs / relevance_watch_model.rs and crates/semantic/tests/collapse_model.rs so that for generated components with call-site/story evidence the listed rows equal `decide`'s rows in both lanes, the lanes agree, and the watch/lazy equals fresh after edits (an edit adding or removing a call site changes the listing; the lazy delta reports it: reuse the existing `layers_differ`/delta rule). Mutation-prove the guards. Apply the Pre-push gate (invariants, grammar sweep over the DOM-prop/ambient/layer forms, mutation proof, /code-review medium on your explicit SHA range awaited). Gates: `just lint doc-check machete typos`, nextest workspace (`cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked`; run `pnpm install --offline --ignore-scripts --frozen-lockfile` first), `just test-checker-lane` (symlink target/release in your worktree to your CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release), the TS/vitest suites for packages/storybook and the oracle (`just test-ts`), schema/doc snapshots, semver changeset in the user-focused convention of AGENTS.md. If the change alters output (listed props) it must bump what the repo requires (output schema/cache) with a snapshot update. Own CARGO_TARGET_DIR under /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/shrink/, rust 1.99.1 first on PATH (/Users/gabe/.rustup/toolchains/1.99.1-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin). Cap 120 tool calls; if you run out stop at a green commit and list what remains. Write the PR body to /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/pr/feat-list-props-by-usage.md (## What, ## Evidence with the before/after tables, ## Not verified, session URL line). Final message at most 90 words: SHA, Button/Badge rows before/after in Storybook and CLI, gates exit codes, what remains."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1326,"cache_read_input_tokens":805652,"output_tokens":4963,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2281},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1326,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4963,"cache_read_input_tokens":805652,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1326,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1326},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015jrBj55PR9KjP5STsj5s9S":{"description":"T4: list props by usage evidence in both lanes","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"Implement s