{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","id":"d416c6ad-ec24-4cd8-b197-40696204099f","timestamp":"2026-11-16T17:01:19.209Z","version":"2.1.311","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"9803daf85cbe48be5f6ca225f95dc13bf2e5a024e85e5325762dd209c1ad3e02","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"a8029a94-90e6-4d71-b3e5-1fc7eb3db39e","keep":1354,"tail":["822655521c89be4c0565f1d858bbfbdbe2279ee803d3e0d80fb435a5db7cf400","25c09da4680b57a57bb0b55e72964fcfb231038720c37ab7a0f4a569e35bc6e3","403241b25f27dc92da0b87c7f747256edd9a7d0c45bb14f07e2a22356b34e2d9"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1356,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"4f65e121ba4b543e3378fdaddd5644eae2fe5de12fb5953d2694c74c86aaa935"}
{"parentUuid":"c915299c-a6a7-47b1-8bf2-a9f650601f42","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch6xyR3R9wS9VERsNtrGY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"T4 is not pushable yet. The first pass cut the Controls rows sharply, but it isn't green, so I sent the worker back with a 100-call cap.\n\n**What it reported (head c5a267a6, local commits only)**\n\n| Component | Storybook rows, before → after | CLI checker rows, before → after |\n|---|---|---|\n| Chakra `Button` | 437 → 10 | 150 → 9 |\n| `Badge` | 280 → 3 (`children` comes from story args) | 2 → 2 |\n\nLint, doc-check, machete, typos and core nextest exit 0.\n\n**Why it isn't green**\n- **Workspace nextest:** 8 failures, 5 in `collapse_model`.\n- **A real lane mismatch:** a source with no structural `parent` gets a layer in the checker lane only. That breaks the one-owner rule, so it has to be fixed, not worked around.\n- **Not done yet:**\n  - The lane-agreement model test.\n  - The checker lane.\n  - The TypeScript and oracle tests.\n  - Mutation proofs.\n  - The oracle check on antd and shadcn.\n  - The `/code-review`.\n\n**What I added to its brief.** Narrowing must never hide a prop a consumer needs, and 10 rows for `Button` could mean it hides real props. So before the gates, the worker must:\n1. List `Button`'s 10 Storybook rows and 9 CLI rows. Compare them with the props Chakra's own props type declares (`variant`, `size`, `colorPalette`, `loading`, `spinner`, `disabled`, `asChild`, and so on).\n2. Run an old-versus-new differential on Chakra, Mantine, antd and shadcn `Button`. Any prop declared in the project's own source or the component's own props type that disappears is a bug in the rule, because own props must always stay listed.\n\nIt also writes the changeset in the user-focused convention and amends ADR 0023 or 0028 for any contract change, including the `full` default.\n\nI'll push nothing until the safety check, the full nextest run and the review are done. I'll report the own-props differential result with the row counts."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2565,"cache_read_input_tokens":816443,"output_tokens":704,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2565,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":704,"cache_read_input_tokens":816443,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2565},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"81066813-d70d-4378-a442-eec2a2be13bf","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch6xyQi4gDZmJiXPzRun2","requestRef":"d416c6ad-ec24-4cd8-b197-40696204099f","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"4b7c2a58-4fd3-4a78-8b98-598c5bc741f2","timestamp":"2026-11-16T17:01:24.589Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-aa49801b6d8a5a6c1","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
