{"parentUuid":"eb9a49a8-46f0-4aa3-891f-4edf25333dc8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"21c5cb8b-2147-40ac-910c-28fb083963c8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014hxUVjBptNZsQRWapYC3L4","type":"tool_result","content":"Five corpora, main de016f69 vs ce276f1a (checker on, `--load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies`, one run each, load 16 to 31):\n\n| Corpus | Median rows | Total rows | JSON | Layer names | First run |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Chakra | 139 → 139 | 84,386 → 81,914 | 49.6 → 49.1 MB | 406,765 → 576,322 | 3.84 s / 1,920 MiB → 4.23 s / 1,978 MiB |\n| Mantine | 72 → 72 | 20,873 → 20,294 | 57.2 → 57.3 MB | 0 → 73,100 | 1.09 s / 858 MiB → 1.15 s / 884 MiB |\n| antd | 8 → 8 | 10,241 → 5,557 | 5.5 → 4.8 MB | 0 → 16,303 | 1.75 s / 1,324 MiB → 1.75 s / 1,334 MiB |\n| shadcn | 2 → 2 | 33,249 → 8,738 | 5.5 → 5.3 MB | 6,615 → 388,181 | 1.47 s / 986 MiB → 1.56 s / 1,204 MiB |\n| Spectrum | 11 → 6 | 52,011 → 18,647 | 13.4 → 11.1 MB | 0 → 36,156 | 1.62 s / 845 MiB → 1.59 s / 840 MiB |\n\nNo median grew. Names that leave the listing stay in layers.\n\nOracle (`scripts/weekly.py --oracle --corpus antd --corpus shadcn`, exit 0):\n\n| Corpus | Correct | Wrong |\n|---|---|---|\n| shadcn | 98.7% (13,932 props) | 0 |\n| antd | 93.0% (4,127 props) | 0.02% (1) |\n\nBoth match the de016f69 report. The oracle measures the expanded view (collapse `none`).\n\nGates:\n\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked`: 1,645/1,645 pass, exit 0.\n- `just lint doc-check machete typos`: exit 0.\n- `just test-checker-lane`: exit 0.\n- `just test-ts`: exit 0 (66 + 114 + 229 pass).\n\nTests and mutation proofs:\n\n- New model test `the_ambient_members_put_forward_are_exactly_those_passed_at_the_floor_or_read` checks rows plus `used` against the model's own floor count over 12 generated projects.\n- New `watch_equals_fresh_when_relevance_narrows_the_listing`: watch, lazy and fresh agree under call-site edits, and the lazy delta reports them.\n- New `jsx_children_pass_children_at_a_call_site`.\n- New `a_member_of_a_mapped_type_over_keyof_an_interface_has_that_interface_as_parent`. Mutation-proven: dropping the parent fails it.\n- Tests that encoded the old listing now read the expanded view or expect layer names. Each commit message says why.\n\n`/code-review medium de016f69..89275198` returned 10 candidates.\n\nFixed in ce276f1a:\n1. `layers_differ` now compares the listing.\n2. An inline `Omit` over `keyof X` declined all narrowing. It now still narrows React's and the DOM's attributes; Mantine's median, which had risen to 73, is back to 72.\n3. An `Omit` behind an alias now declines the same way as one written in place.\n5. Pick key depth.\n6. CR and no-break-space in JSX whitespace.\n10. Line width.\n\nNot fixed:\n- 4: `key` in the CLI for an unlayered component whose structural answer lists it. The session keeps it as a structural prop and the CLI drops it.\n- 7: allocations in `narrow`.\n- 8: the unused `_mode` parameter on public functions. Removing it is a semver break.\n- 9: double alias walk.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"794d8b98-d623-4a1b-8950-8db8853a1c3f","timestamp":"2026-11-16T17:33:57.977Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Five corpora, main de016f69 vs ce276f1a (checker on, `--load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies`, one run each, load 16 to 31):\n\n| Corpus | Median rows | Total rows | JSON | Layer names | First run |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Chakra | 139 → 139 | 84,386 → 81,914 | 49.6 → 49.1 MB | 406,765 → 576,322 | 3.84 s / 1,920 MiB → 4.23 s / 1,978 MiB |\n| Mantine | 72 → 72 | 20,873 → 20,294 | 57.2 → 57.3 MB | 0 → 73,100 | 1.09 s / 858 MiB → 1.15 s / 884 MiB |\n| antd | 8 → 8 | 10,241 → 5,557 | 5.5 → 4.8 MB | 0 → 16,303 | 1.75 s / 1,324 MiB → 1.75 s / 1,334 MiB |\n| shadcn | 2 → 2 | 33,249 → 8,738 | 5.5 → 5.3 MB | 6,615 → 388,181 | 1.47 s / 986 MiB → 1.56 s / 1,204 MiB |\n| Spectrum | 11 → 6 | 52,011 → 18,647 | 13.4 → 11.1 MB | 0 → 36,156 | 1.62 s / 845 MiB → 1.59 s / 840 MiB |\n\nNo median grew. Names that leave the listing stay in layers.\n\nOracle (`scripts/weekly.py --oracle --corpus antd --corpus shadcn`, exit 0):\n\n| Corpus | Correct | Wrong |\n|---|---|---|\n| shadcn | 98.7% (13,932 props) | 0 |\n| antd | 93.0% (4,127 props) | 0.02% (1) |\n\nBoth match the de016f69 report. The oracle measures the expanded view (collapse `none`).\n\nGates:\n\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked`: 1,645/1,645 pass, exit 0.\n- `just lint doc-check machete typos`: exit 0.\n- `just test-checker-lane`: exit 0.\n- `just test-ts`: exit 0 (66 + 114 + 229 pass).\n\nTests and mutation proofs:\n\n- New model test `the_ambient_members_put_forward_are_exactly_those_passed_at_the_floor_or_read` checks rows plus `used` against the model's own floor count over 12 generated projects.\n- New `watch_equals_fresh_when_relevance_narrows_the_listing`: watch, lazy and fresh agree under call-site edits, and the lazy delta reports them.\n- New `jsx_children_pass_children_at_a_call_site`.\n- New `a_member_of_a_mapped_type_over_keyof_an_interface_has_that_interface_as_parent`. Mutation-proven: dropping the parent fails it.\n- Tests that encoded the old listing now read the expanded view or expect layer names. Each commit message says why.\n\n`/code-review medium de016f69..89275198` returned 10 candidates.\n\nFixed in ce276f1a:\n1. `layers_differ` now compares the listing.\n2. An inline `Omit` over `keyof X` declined all narrowing. It now still narrows React's and the DOM's attributes; Mantine's median, which had risen to 73, is back to 72.\n3. An `Omit` behind an alias now declines the same way as one written in place.\n5. Pick key depth.\n6. CR and no-break-space in JSX whitespace.\n10. Line width.\n\nNot fixed:\n- 4: `key` in the CLI for an unlayered component whose structural answer lists it. The session keeps it as a structural prop and the CLI drops it.\n- 7: allocations in `narrow`.\n- 8: the unused `_mode` parameter on public functions. Removing it is a semver break.\n- 9: double alias walk.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"1c85ca44-6804-484b-9fad-76c86e5f48d8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","branch":"mf-t4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxViolations":[],"sandboxed":true,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"eb9a49a8-46f0-4aa3-891f-4edf25333dc8","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
