{"parentUuid":"5ae5e12b-6224-46fe-884f-d5bff058ed24","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch74ABMHKb97qX7qJJ16z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79,"cache_read_input_tokens":835844,"output_tokens":3559,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":606},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":79,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3559,"cache_read_input_tokens":835844,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":79},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":4975,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"dd604218-1270-4820-8fbc-87a3e29436e9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch74AB2S9TAGmukvgTjSH","requestRef":"e66f7712-a703-4f3c-a999-94bda0c7716e","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5b7b6f6c-e34f-46bb-8014-ff889db16007","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:09:25.076Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
{"parentUuid":"5b7b6f6c-e34f-46bb-8014-ff889db16007","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch74ABMHKb97qX7qJJ16z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"There are three likely places, listed below with the evidence I have. I haven't profiled by phase, so I'm starting that now instead of guessing.\n\n**What we know**\n\n| Run | Peak RSS | Reading |\n|---|---|---|\n| Structural only (`--no-checker`) | 143–364 MiB | Our own parse, resolve and output. |\n| Second run (kept checker answer) | 129–476 MiB | Same as structural plus reading the kept answer. |\n| First run with the checker | 840–1,908 MiB | The checker's whole program adds roughly 0.6–1.5 GiB. |\n| Storybook dev server | 893 MiB | The same program held while the server runs. |\n\nEarlier measurements put a bare tsrs typecheck of Chakra at about 1.07 GiB. So the floor is the checker's own program, and most of the gap above structural is the checker's.\n\n**Where I'd expect savings, by size**\n1. **The checker loads far more than any one component needs.** It parses, binds and checks the whole program: our source, `node_modules` declarations, all of `@types/react`, and TypeScript's libs. We ask about components, not the whole program. Loading only the files each component reaches, or dropping program data after answering, could cut the largest share.\n2. **Memory held after it's no longer needed.** The CLI is one-shot, so conversion memos and the checker's type interning could be freed phase by phase. Peak RSS is what you see, so freeing before the next phase starts matters. Our own heap budget (60% of memory, at most 8 GiB) is a safety net, not a saving.\n3. **Our own structures.** Structural data for every file, the converted type trees (hundreds of thousands of layer names on Chakra), and the JSON being built and serialized (47–57 MB output). This is smaller than the checker's share, but the shadcn +22% from T4 shows our own allocations can matter.\n\nA profiling worker (Opus, 60 calls, no code changes) will break peak RSS down by phase on Chakra, shadcn and Mantine: parse and structural, checker program creation, conversion, merge, serialization. It will use allocator statistics and RSS sampling, find what the +22% on shadcn is, and rank the savings by size, effort and risk. I'll report the ranked list, not an opinion."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79,"cache_read_input_tokens":835844,"output_tokens":3559,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":606},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":79,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3559,"cache_read_input_tokens":835844,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":79},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"dd604218-1270-4820-8fbc-87a3e29436e9","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch74AB2S9TAGmukvgTjSH","requestRef":"e66f7712-a703-4f3c-a999-94bda0c7716e","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"08f1ecf7-4905-4aac-9ed4-264d2700dbcb","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:09:30.682Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
