 loading; (c) checker program creation (tsrs parse/bind of project + node_modules + libs: the number of files/bytes it loads: count them); (d) per-component checker work and conversion to our types (the memo, `convert.rs`, heap budget); (e) merge (`apply_props`, relevance `narrow`/`apply`, layering); (f) output interning + JSON serialization (peak while building the output string). Also try `dhat`-style allocation counts only if a dhat feature or `cargo-instruments` already exists; otherwise skip. (2) Explain the PR 490 +22% on shadcn: compare main vs the PR 490 head on shadcn: which phase and which structure grew (layer names 6,615 -> 388,181 on shadcn: the layers hold names as Strings? interned?). (3) Experiments to size each saving (scratch only): e.g. (i) how much RSS if the checker program loaded only files reachable from the component files (can you tell how many files tsrs loads vs how many components need: count with the existing diagnostics or by the tsrs API entry in crates/semantic), (ii) free/shrink phase data before the next phase (drop memos, clear the checker caches after the whole-project pass: is the process exiting right after? then dropping is useless for peak but a different order or streaming results may help), (iii) streaming output instead of building one 50 MB string and the whole ExtractionOutput, (iv) interning layer member names (Arc<str>/CompactString/shared tables: ADR 0018 already interns prop sets: check if layers use it), (v) a lower memory allocator setting (mimalloc options like MIMALLOC_PURGE_DELAY / arena settings, `eager_commit`/`reserve`), (vi) tsrs-side options that cut memory (type cache limits, skipping checking function bodies, `skipLibCheck`, lazy declaration loading) if exposed. Report for each: measured saving (MiB and %) on Chakra and shadcn, effort (S/M/L, files), risk (output change? semver?), and whether it helps the Storybook dev server (steady-state RSS 893 MiB) or only the one-shot CLI. Deliverable: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/memory-profile.md: (1) a table of peak RSS by phase for the four projects; (2) the +22% explanation; (3) the ranked savings table with the experiment evidence; (4) your recommendation of the top three to implement, with the expected total (e.g. 'Chakra 1.9 GiB -> X'), and what you could not measure. Do not change repo files or push; scratch builds under /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/mem/ only (own CARGO_TARGET_DIR there; rust 1.99.1 first on PATH /Users/gabe/.rustup/toolchains/1.99.1-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin). Cap 60 tool calls; run long commands in the background and poll. Final message at most 90 words: the phase with the most memory on Chakra, the cause of +22%, the top saving with its measured MiB.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper/ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba/tasks/ae3f305f76d56d9f5.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"dd604218-1270-4820-8fbc-87a3e29436e9","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","branch":"mf-t4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"31147df4-045f-4ca6-8527-63b867861f9a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba