{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","prNumber":490,"prUrl":"https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/490","prRepository":"orin-dx/caliper","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:21:19.426Z"}
{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","bridgeSessionId":"cse_013R2ytvK9B32ZaSUaSe6aAZ","lastSequenceNum":15975,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"65081455-4ad6-4279-ad27-537f1beb8d8b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch755FgxuRbK1iZN81ocm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Narrowing what the checker loads won't cut memory.** The program the checker reads is small, and the experiments say so. The memory is the checker session's working set while it answers components, and about 1.4 GiB of Chakra's peak is state the output doesn't need. The full report is at `~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/memory-profile.md`.\n\n**What the checker loads (measured)**\n\n| Project | Files read | Bytes read |\n|---|---|---|\n| Chakra | 2,291 | 6.6 MiB |\n| shadcn | 5,165 | 25.8 MiB |\n| Mantine | 1,393 | 6.3 MiB |\n\n- The TypeScript libs are embedded in tsrs, so they cost no disk reads.\n- The tsrs arena holds only 87–206 MiB at its peak.\n- `types: [\"react\"]` drops `@types/node` and removes about 220 files from Chakra's reads, with identical output and no RSS change (−12 MiB on Chakra, +5 on shadcn, both noise).\n- Splitting the component files into batches saves under 5%. At 4 or 8 batches the output changes, because a batch's program misses declarations the other files bring, so I'd reject it.\n- Allocator settings change nothing, and the output is already streamed.\n\n**Where the memory is on Chakra** (peak 1,866 MiB)\n- **After the structural pass:** 490 MiB.\n- **After all components are answered:** 1,604 MiB. That phase adds 1.1 GiB, mostly in the first second, when the 7 style-system components make about 4,000 checker requests each. It holds the tsrs type and relation caches plus our converter's memo and trees.\n- **Peak:** it lands in generic instantiation, in all four projects. That step builds a second whole program rooted at every file while both lane programs and their caches are still alive.\n- **The kept answer is only 32 MiB,** and the second run peaks at 476 MiB.\n\n**Ranked savings**\n1. **Generic instantiation builds a second whole program.** Deriving it from the live snapshot, or rooting it only at the generic components' files, is bounded at −262 MiB on Chakra (−14%), −231 on shadcn (−24%), −196 on Mantine (−23%). Output-preserving by design, medium effort, and it likely helps the dev server too.\n2. **Undo #490's retained data.** Its extra memory is data we keep: a per-component placement object and an un-interned `Vec<String>` of layer names. That's −164 MiB on Chakra and −213 MiB on shadcn. It's medium effort, with no output change if only the storage changes. This cause is partly unproven, because there's no allocation profile.\n3. **Share the converter's memo and cut oversized types before expanding them.** This is the only lever on Chakra's 1.1 GiB component phase, and its saving is unmeasured. It's a large change with a public type change.\n\n**Expected result.** With #1 and #2, Chakra goes from 1.87 to about 1.6 GiB, and shadcn with #490 from 1.2 to about 0.75 GiB. Getting Chakra below 1 GiB needs #3, which is a bigger job.\n\n**Not measured:** the Storybook dev server's 893 MiB, antd and Spectrum, the split between tsrs and converter memory inside the component phase, and a quiet machine. RSS isn't affected by load, but the times are.\n\nMy recommendation is to fix #2 before merging #490, since it's our own retained data and costs nothing in output. Then do #1. Treat #3 as the alpha's next memory slice if you want Chakra under 1 GiB. Want me to start #2 and #1 as workers?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8234,"cache_read_input_tokens":850144,"output_tokens":1230,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8234,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1230,"cache_read_input_tokens":850144,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8234,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8234},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ef04b6cc-15c0-488a-be75-beff0cedf434","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch755FP6kH3a3G3q1qtWF","requestRef":"f0b34297-d8d6-42d5-89c3-fd204cff0fed","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"fd5044fb-20f1-4952-bbbf-b38493841a9c","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:21:27.858Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
