{"parentUuid":"8c1221a0-7504-4a01-81da-080030603a37","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch75eieMYDVc1rr6TU4Kk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011xko8hYgrhA8aBBdpWHeVz","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"PR 490: stop retaining per-component placement and un-interned layer names","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"Cut the memory PR 490 added, on its own branch. Start from `origin/feat/list-props-by-usage` (PR 490; `git fetch origin` first; if blocked use existing refs); local branch `fix/list-props-memory`; commit locally; I push onto PR 490's branch. Read /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/worker-contract.md (incl. Pre-push gate) and /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/memory-profile.md (section 2 and ranked saving #2: measured causes; scratch instrumentation in /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/mem/ incl. instrument.pl, prof.sh, exp.sh: reuse them, do not commit instrumentation). Findings to fix: PR 490 added `relevance: Option<Arc<Placement>>` to every `ComponentEntry` (crates/core/src/types/output.rs:~143, not serialized, kept across merges) and element layers' member lists; `InheritedLayer.members` is a `Vec<String>` per component, not interned (only the JSON's `nameLists` are interned, ADR 0018). Measured on shadcn: `--no-checker` peak 357 -> 463 MiB (+30%), full first run 982 -> 1,195 (+22%); Chakra 1,866 -> 2,030; Mantine 871 -> 894; layer names on shadcn went 6,615 -> 388,181. Goal: bring PR 490's peak RSS back to within ~3% of main's (shadcn <= ~1,010 MiB, Chakra <= ~1,925, structural shadcn <= ~370) WITHOUT any change in output: canonical JSON byte-identical to PR 490's head on all five corpora (identity diff with the checker on, `--load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies`, `stats` stripped) and on gate-large, both lanes, watch/lazy results equal fresh (the existing relevance_watch_model/relevance_model tests). Approach (decide by measurement, smallest first): (1) do not keep a per-component `Arc<Placement>`: compute the listing and the `used` names where they are needed and drop the placement as soon as `narrow`/`apply` finish, or keep one shared placement per distinct evidence (many components share none/empty); only keep what the lazy delta (`layers_differ`) really needs, and prove that need with the model tests; (2) share layer member lists: components that name the same source layer (e.g. the 286 `button` attributes, SystemProperties' 705 names) must share ONE allocation (`Arc<[...]>` or an index into a table built once per source/element), not clone a Vec<String> per component; `InheritedLayer` is a public type: if its field type must change, do it with a semver-correct changeset (minor is fine in 0.x) in the user-focused convention of AGENTS.md and keep the serialized JSON identical; if a smaller change (e.g. `Arc<Vec<String>>` shared from a per-run table keyed by (source, element)) achieves it, prefer that; (3) check the structural pass clones: `session` clones per-file targets with placements (the profile says the component phase grew +130 MiB though checker requests fell): find with the instrumentation which structure grows and fix it. Measure before/after peak RSS (`/usr/bin/time -l`, 3 runs median) on shadcn, Chakra, Mantine, sb-demo, structural-only and full, and report a table in the PR note; report `uptime` (RSS is unaffected by load). Tests first where behaviour is guarded (identity and watch/lazy equality tests must stay green; add a test that two components naming the same source share the allocation if you introduce sharing). Pre-push gate: invariants, mutation proof for the sharing/drop (a test fails if broken), `/code-review medium` on your explicit SHA range awaited, one fix round. Gates: `just lint doc-check machete typos`, `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` (run `pnpm install --offline --ignore-scripts --frozen-lockfile` first), `just test-checker-lane` (symlink target/release in the worktree to your CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release), `just test-ts`, `just semver`. Own CARGO_TARGET_DIR under /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/shrink/, rust 1.99.1 first on PATH (/Users/gabe/.rustup/toolchains/1.99.1-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin). Cap 90 tool calls; if you run out, stop at a green commit and say what remains. Notes to /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/pr/fix-list-props-memory.md (## What, ## Evidence with the before/after RSS table, ## Not verified, session URL line). Final message at most 70 words: SHA, RSS before/after (shadcn, Chakra), identity result, exit codes."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":50,"cache_read_input_tokens":859608,"output_tokens":4207,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":561},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":50,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4207,"cache_read_input_tokens":859608,"cache_creation_input_tokens":50,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":50},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011xko8hYgrhA8aBBdpWHeVz":{"description":"PR 490: stop retaining per-component placement and un-interned layer names","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"Cut the memory PR 490 added, on its own branch. Start from `origin/feat/list-props-by-usage` (PR 490; `git fetch origin` first; if blocked use existing refs); local branch `fix/list-props-memory`; commit locally; I push onto PR 490's branch. Read /Users/gabe/Projects/cali