racle-run/memory-profile.md (ranked saving #1; scratch instrumentation in /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/mem/: instrument.pl, prof.sh, exp.sh: reuse, do not commit it), plus docs/type-checker-integration.md and crates/semantic/src/{lib.rs,rpc.rs,instantiate.rs,checker.rs}. Finding (measured): the process peak lands in generic instantiation (`instantiate::answer`) in all four projects (Chakra 1,866 MiB, shadcn 982, Mantine 868, sb-demo 230) because `Rpc::layered` (rpc.rs ~548) creates a fresh snapshot rooted at EVERY root file plus the synthetic files while both lane programs and their caches/the converter's memo are still alive; upper bound of the saving (peak minus the marker before that phase): Chakra -262 MiB (-14%), shadcn -231 (-24%), Mantine -196 (-23%). Goal: remove that peak WITHOUT changing output (canonical JSON byte-identical to origin/main on all five corpora, checker on, `--load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies`, `stats` stripped; and on gate-large; and Storybook session answers for generic components equal the batch ones: the existing semantic tests/gate harness determinism). Options, decide by measurement, smallest first: (a) derive the instantiation program from the live snapshot with `updateSnapshot` (as `beside` does) instead of a fresh snapshot; (b) root it only at the files of the generic components (and the synthetic files) rather than every root; (c) release lane 2's program/caches and the converter's memo before opening it (only if the memo is not needed after; check ownership); (d) run instantiation after the lanes finished and dropped. Measure peak RSS before/after (`/usr/bin/time -l`, 3 runs, median) on Chakra, shadcn, Mantine, sb-demo and antd, plus wall time (report load) and the Storybook dev-server RSS after answering a generic component if feasible with /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/sb-demo (skip if it needs more than a few calls: say so). Do not change the public API unless needed (semver changeset in the user-focused convention of AGENTS.md if you do; else a patch changeset: 'Extraction with the checker uses less memory: ...' with the measured numbers). Tests first where behaviour is guarded: the identity diff harness (script it in scratch under oracle-run/mem/, not committed) and the existing semantic tests; add a regression test only if it can pin 'one program for instantiation derived from the live snapshot' meaningfully (e.g. count of programs/roots in the fake binding's calls in crates/semantic/src/rpc.rs tests, which has a fake client: `updateSnapshot` assertions); mutation-prove it. Pre-push gate: invariants, mutation proof, `/code-review medium` on your explicit SHA range awaited, one fix round. Gates: `just lint doc-check machete typos`, `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` (run `pnpm install --offline --ignore-scripts --frozen-lockfile` first), `just test-checker-lane` (symlink target/release in the worktree to your CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release), gate_harness determinism and memory modes (checker/session code changed: see the contract), `just semver`. Own CARGO_TARGET_DIR under /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/shrink/, rust 1.99.1 first on PATH (/Users/gabe/.rustup/toolchains/1.99.1-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin). Cap 90 tool calls; if you run out, stop at a green commit and say what remains. Notes to /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/pr/perf-instantiation-without-second-program.md (## What, ## Evidence with the before/after RSS table, ## Not verified, session URL line). Final message at most 70 words: SHA, RSS before/after (Chakra, shadcn), identity result, exit codes.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper/ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba/tasks/a8954a6abcddbb7ce.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"1e267af9-53c2-492c-860d-ee90297a0400","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/