\": \"The `add` closure in `sources` calls `type_name.to_owned()` and `file_name.to_owned()` for every name, even when that source's key is already in the BTreeMap.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A component whose collapsed layers hold about 300 React DOM attributes from a few sources allocates about 600 throwaway Strings (long node_modules paths) just to build the grouping key, then drops them. `layer_members` in semantic.rs already avoids this with `BTreeMap&lt;(&amp;str, &amp;str), _&gt;`. Use borrowed keys and allocate only once per source when converting to the output Vec.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/core/src/types/semantic.rs\",\n    \"line\": 596,\n    \"summary\": \"`layer_members` and `relevance::sources` are the same grouping (BTreeMap of source to BTreeSet of names, then into `Vec&lt;((String, String), Box&lt;[Box&lt;str&gt;]&gt;)&gt;`), and the PR declares the same shape twice under two names (`SourceMembers` and `(Source, Box&lt;[Box&lt;str&gt;]&gt;)`).\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Two copies of the grouping and lookup logic for one representation: a later fix to ordering, dedup or lookup (such as a binary search by source) has to be made in both. Fix: one shared newtype (e.g. `BySource`) with `from_iter(name, type, file)`, `contains(name, type, file)` and `iter()`, used by both `Placement::left` and `LayerFacts::members`.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/core/src/types/semantic.rs\",\n    \"line\": 664,\n    \"summary\": \"`Layering::kept` flattens the newly grouped `facts.members` back into an FxHashSet of per-name `(name, type, file)` tuples on every call, so the grouping's benefit is lost on this path.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"For each checker target, `kept` builds a hash set with one entry per layer member (hundreds for DOM-heavy components) just to answer membership queries. The grouped Vec is sorted by source and by name, so `keeps` could look up the source and binary-search the name directly, with no rebuild and no extra memory each call.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/core/src/relevance/mod.rs\",\n    \"line\": 113,\n    \"summary\": \"`Placement::leaves` finds the source with a linear `.iter().find`, even though `left` comes from a BTreeMap and is already sorted by `(type_name, file_name)`.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"`narrow` calls `leaves` for every listed prop on every merge, so a component with many dependency/DOM sources pays O(props × sources) string comparisons, each comparing long file paths. `binary_search_by` on `(type_name, file_name)` uses the ordering the PR already guarantees and makes the lookup logarithmic.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/core/src/relevance/mod.rs\",\n    \"line\": 107,\n    \"summary\": \"`Placement::used` is still a `BTreeSet&lt;String&gt;` with one heap String per name, so the per-component memory the commit targets is only partly reduced.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"The commit's goal is to stop holding per-name facts on every ComponentEntry, but `used` still keeps an owned String for each used member of every component, duplicating names that `left` already holds. Since `used` names members of `left` (plus untyped and defaulted names), a per-source flag or `Box&lt;[Box&lt;str&gt;]&gt;` would finish the job; as it stands, a large design system still holds those per-name allocations for the whole run.\"\n  }\n]\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>65016</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>5</tool_uses><duration_ms>59684</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","reason":"absorbed_mid_turn","commandUuid":"79e579cc-70ac-4da4-a8ba-ccac36205746","deliveryId":"1a92228c-fe85-4ec2-b8bd-7eef57b7bbce"}
