{"parentUuid":"dfe5b4e7-ef7b-49f5-8b3b-72e88732003d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch78Vk7m5KvGNgWHFM5sJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56,"cache_read_input_tokens":880601,"output_tokens":1573,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":593},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1573,"cache_read_input_tokens":880601,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5263,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"a26b46b4-bc23-4c43-8630-de6a85934cc3","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch78VjnRKaquEzs8keoL8","requestRef":"a54ee7c0-f08d-4816-9b4f-e8ab12f0696d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ab6ade3d-481b-4dca-aa11-3f78bc9f1774","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:06:18.014Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
{"parentUuid":"ab6ade3d-481b-4dca-aa11-3f78bc9f1774","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch78Vk7m5KvGNgWHFM5sJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here are the top priorities, ordered by what blocks an alpha and what needs you.\n\n**1. Land the open PRs: #490, #491, #489.** These carry the alpha's visible improvement (Controls rows, memory, docs). Their CI and Entire reviews may still be running after the latest pushes, and I haven't checked them since. Two things block them:\n- **#490** needs your Spectrum decision on hiding `aria-*` and `id` by default (the SharedDom rule).\n- **I haven't read the diffs** of #490 or #491. I'll do that before telling you they're safe to merge.\n\n**2. Unblock publishing: the 0.11.0 release recovery.** It fails on every `main` push with E167, so nothing can publish until it's resolved. I need your choice: delete the mismatched asset and re-dispatch, or skip with `RELEASE_PENDING_FROM`. The corpora budget gate has also never run on a real release PR, and that gate is what would have caught the original 42 GB regression.\n\n**3. One clean measurement of the merged `main`.** After #490 and #491 land, run the oracle once on an idle machine. That gives the alpha's real first-run, second-run and Storybook dev numbers, and the `STATUS.md` refresh. Every earlier timing carried load 5–10 and up.\n\n**4. Make the weekly oracle trustworthy.** Three problems:\n- **Chakra:** it needs a larger Node heap, or it dies at about 4 GB. The CI weekly of 2026-11-15 also died with exit 143 on Chakra. It's worth confirming that the memory fixes make the weekly pass.\n- **\"Not judged\":** it reads as 75% on Chakra and 63% on Mantine, so those headlines say nothing about quality. The report should split it out, and I'd find out whether the size bound cuts those types.\n- **Recall metric:** it still counts `@types/react` props as \"recalled\" in a way T4 changes, because the element layer now carries names.\n\n**5. Memory, the converter memo (Chakra under 1 GiB).** This is the largest remaining saving, about 1.1 GiB in the component phase, and it's a large change to a public type. I'd plan it as its own slice once #490 and #491 are in, not before the alpha unless 1.7 GiB on Chakra is unacceptable to you.\n\n**Smaller items**\n- Sweep the docs for \"add-on\" wording, after you confirm what you meant.\n- Storybook dev mode: measure neighbour prefetch, and antd, which fails in Vite on a generated `./version` import. The head-to-head with react-docgen-typescript is also unmeasured.\n- Your two remaining alpha decisions: the audience, and whether the addon's default flip ships in the first alpha.\n\n**My suggested order:** 1 and 2 first (they need your answers), then 3, then 4, and treat 5 as post-alpha unless you say otherwise. Which of those do you want me to start on now?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56,"cache_read_input_tokens":880601,"output_tokens":1573,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":593},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1573,"cache_read_input_tokens":880601,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a26b46b4-bc23-4c43-8630-de6a85934cc3","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch78VjnRKaquEzs8keoL8","requestRef":"a54ee7c0-f08d-4816-9b4f-e8ab12f0696d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3921b664-f012-4621-9eab-51017cc08d1c","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:06:24.821Z","a