{"parentUuid":"62b37160-0926-4606-ae00-10743da56c2a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch78YTYBwMJpnrUijnNwz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":72,"cache_read_input_tokens":882230,"output_tokens":1008,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":303},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":72,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1008,"cache_read_input_tokens":882230,"cache_creation_input_tokens":72,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":72},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2744,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"09ec85d3-2546-4089-b9ab-a0214de1fae1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch78YTCbuJDkMj6jB7BTa","requestRef":"37cfc346-4e0c-410a-81b3-5d58fa35eed2","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2c26bc02-3f5f-4903-8737-0a5b5e40fbae","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:06:52.412Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
{"parentUuid":"2c26bc02-3f5f-4903-8737-0a5b5e40fbae","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch78YTYBwMJpnrUijnNwz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes. That is #490, \"list props by usage\", and it's item 1.\n\n**What it does today (measured on the demo)**\n- Chakra `Button` goes from 437 Controls rows to 10, and `Badge` from 280 to 3. The CLI gives the same names.\n- A DOM attribute, a Chakra condition prop or any member of a large dependency source becomes a row only when evidence says it matters. That means it's passed at call sites, named in a story arg, read in the component body, forwarded to another component, or named by the props type. Everything else stays in the layer as a name, so no information is lost.\n- The component's own props always stay listed. The differential found none missing on Chakra, Mantine, antd or the demo.\n- `Button` ends up with its real props (`variant`, `size`, `loading`, and so on), plus `children` from the story args.\n\nThe collapse-by-default work that's already merged is the other half: sources over 200 props, or over 30 for DOM, ARIA and style sources, become one layer of names. #490 builds on it, so the two together are what removes the massive prop counts.\n\n**What it does not cover**\n- **Your own project's large sources.** Only sources outside the project are narrowed by usage. A source in your own code keeps the size-based collapse rule. That's why Chakra's own `Button`, measured in Chakra's own repository, stays at 147 rows.\n- **No usage evidence at all.** With no call sites or stories, the listing is own, picked, overriding, required and defaulted props. A whole DOM source is never listed.\n- **Spectrum:** 972 components lose `aria-*`, `id` and similar props by default, because their declaring file is classed as ambient. That's the decision I need from you.\n- **Untested on real consumers.** I verified it on the demo and four corpora, with story args or few call sites. I haven't seen it on a real app with many call sites per component, where I'd expect more props to qualify as used.\n\nSo the first priority isn't a new optimization. It's getting #490 reviewed and merged, with your Spectrum answer, since that is the change that fixes what you asked about. Should I read its diff now and check how it behaves when a component has many call sites?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":72,"cache_read_input_tokens":882230,"output_tokens":1008,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":303},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":72,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1008,"cache_read_input_tokens":882230,"cache_creation_input_tokens":72,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":72},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"09ec85d3-2546-4089-b9ab-a0214de1fae1","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch78YTCbuJDkMj6jB7BTa","requestRef":"37cfc346-4e0c-410a-81b3-5d58fa35eed2","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"36a9e9d8-af5f-4490-b6d4-28209b29c0cf","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:06:57.983Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
