{"parentUuid":"140cc760-c4c2-4d92-b180-478a50da7fb5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch78i6d8fEpcrM2tHuwzY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1481,"cache_read_input_tokens":893550,"output_tokens":2286,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1376},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1481,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2286,"cache_read_input_tokens":893550,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1481,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1481},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":15936,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"9f3452cf-c9b5-4326-b7c0-c748581dd121","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch78i6LkxPnvX3WCYspwM","requestRef":"4db509c6-ec35-40d2-bc6f-201ed2814ac2","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5e98bcee-c6d9-46c6-bd04-34fce6520b59","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:09:16.408Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
{"parentUuid":"5e98bcee-c6d9-46c6-bd04-34fce6520b59","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch78i6d8fEpcrM2tHuwzY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No, it doesn't include all of them. I checked by running #490's build on the demo, and some of the component's own API props are hidden.\n\n**The demo `Button` isn't Chakra's `Button`.** It's a component whose props are `ButtonProps & ComponentProps<'button'>` plus five it declares itself (`tone`, `fresh`, `size`, `kind`, `extra`). Its two stories pass only `children` and `tone`.\n\n**What the 10 rows are.**\n- The five props the demo declares itself.\n- `variant`, `loading`, `spinnerPlacement` and `recipe`, from Chakra's `ButtonProps`.\n- `children`, which Storybook adds from the story args.\n\nI couldn't tell from the output why those four `ButtonProps` members are listed when no story passes them.\n\n**What's hidden.** Chakra's `ButtonProps` is split into small sources, and its members are now only layer names:\n\n| Source | Members hidden |\n|---|---|\n| `ButtonLoadingProps` (2) | `loadingText`, `spinner` |\n| `PolymorphicProps` (2) | `as`, `asChild` |\n| `UnstyledProp` (1) | `unstyled` |\n| `JsxStyleProps` (1) | `css` |\n| `HtmlProps` (5) | `htmlContent`, `htmlHeight`, `htmlSize`, `htmlTranslate`, `htmlWidth` |\n| `Conditions` (130) | `_active`, `2xl`, … |\n| `SystemProperties` (706) | style props |\n| `React.ComponentProps` (286) | DOM attributes |\n\nThe last three should be narrowed. But `loadingText`, `spinner` and `asChild` are part of what a button's API is, and they're hidden because no story passes them.\n\n**Why my own check missed it.** The own-props differential covered only props declared in the project's own source. Props inherited from a dependency's small API interface were outside that check by construction. So \"nothing own was lost\" was true but didn't answer your question.\n\n**The cause, and the fix I'd make.** #490 narrows every dependency source by usage, however small it is. That wasn't the intent: the noise is in large sources (a 130-prop `Conditions`, 286 DOM attributes, 706 style props), not in a 2-prop interface that carries the component's API. The fix is by size, not by name. A dependency source at or under a small threshold, say 30 members, is listed in full. Only larger or ambient sources are narrowed by usage. `Button` would then show about 10 more rows, with the useful API props and none of the noise. It matches the thresholds collapse already uses.\n\nI'd make this change on #490 before it merges. Want me to start it, with the check extended to dependency-declared props this time?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1481,"cache_read_input_tokens":893550,"output_tokens":2286,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1376},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1481,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2286,"cache_read_input_tokens":893550,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1481,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1481},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"9f3452cf-c9b5-4326-b7c0-c748581dd121","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch78i6LkxPnvX3WCYspwM","requestRef":"4db509c6-ec35-40d2-bc6f-201ed2814ac2","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"dfc1caeb-32d1-4fce-aff3-82922d03f6ab","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:09:17.543Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Proj