{"parentUuid":"8401d3f8-9379-43d0-98bf-6b064c08887a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch792ndggp7He8cqwnQxY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":116,"cache_read_input_tokens":897317,"output_tokens":6726,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2693},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":116,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6726,"cache_read_input_tokens":897317,"cache_creation_input_tokens":116,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":116},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":22933,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"c269bd78-ca09-4614-84c8-2f08bb2a0bd1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch792nL5P97sWQ59MTdCT","requestRef":"16c87d94-25e1-42ed-bce2-5422587a5a46","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"97d99a1b-8a59-4f12-8e7c-0a3a045eddaf","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:13:37.525Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
{"parentUuid":"97d99a1b-8a59-4f12-8e7c-0a3a045eddaf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch792ndggp7He8cqwnQxY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, that makes sense, and I misread it. I took \"used\" to mean used by stories and call sites. You mean what the component itself uses, plus the whole of its main props whether or not anything passes them.\n\n**The rule, as I now understand it**\n1. **Main props: everything.** Every member of the component's props type from its API sources is listed, whether or not a story or call site passes it. For `Button` that means all of Chakra's `ButtonProps`: `variant`, `size`, `colorPalette`, `loading`, `loadingText`, `spinner`, `spinnerPlacement`, `asChild`, `as`, `unstyled` and the rest, plus the five the demo declares.\n2. **What the component uses directly.** A member from any source, including a DOM or ambient one, is listed when the component's body reads it, destructures it, or passes it to something explicitly. If the body does `<button {...props} />`, that's a spread onto a DOM tag and counts as no evidence, as before. A spread onto another component resolves to that component's props (T3).\n3. **Big generated sources stay as names in a layer.** That covers the 286 DOM attributes, 706 style props and 130 condition props. They're the noise, and they're not the button's API.\n\n**What changes in #490**\n- Story args and call-site frequency stop being the thing that decides what's shown. A prop passed in a story can still be promoted, which is cheap and makes Controls match the story. But nothing in the main props depends on it.\n- #490 narrowed even a 2-prop interface like `ButtonLoadingProps`. That reverses: small API sources are listed in full.\n- Telling `Conditions` (130, generated) from a real 100-prop API source can't be done by size alone, because collapse only collapsed sources above 200. I'd decide it by structure: a source whose members are a mapped type over `keyof` of a large key set is generated style-system noise. It isn't decided by name.\n\nI'm starting the change on #490's branch (Opus, 100 calls, no push). It has to show, as measured evidence:\n- **Demo `Button`:** all of `ButtonProps`' members plus the five own props, and none of the 286, 706 or 130 noise members.\n- **A component that reads `props.onClick`, or destructures `className`,** lists it even though DOM declares it.\n- **Mantine, antd, shadcn and Spectrum `Button`:** before and after row counts, with no member of a component's declared main props missing. The check this time includes props inherited from a dependency's own API interfaces, which my first differential skipped.\n\nIt keeps the memory fixes and the model tests, and runs the pre-push gate."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":116,"cache_read_input_tokens":897317,"output_tokens":6726,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2693},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":116,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6726,"cache_read_input_tokens":897317,"cache_creation_input_tokens":116,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":116},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c269bd78-ca09-4614-84c8-2f08bb2a0bd1","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch792nL5P97sWQ59MTdCT","requestRef":"16c87d94-25e1-42ed-bce2-5422587a5a46","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c3057d56-4da7-4ac2-9977-7b6f062aada3","timestamp":"2026-11-16T19:13:44.037Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
{"parentUuid":"c3057d56-4da7-4ac2-9977-7b6f062aada3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch792ndggp7He8cqwnQxY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012rXV7rj2bokR9y5awbim2t","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"PR 490: list the main props in full plus what the component uses itself","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"Rework what PR 490 (`origin/feat/list-props-by-usage`, head 24438c48; `git fetch origin` first; if blocked use existing refs) lists, because I (the lead) misread the user's meaning of 'use'. Branch `fix/list-main-props`; commit locally; I push onto PR 490's branch. Read /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/worker-contract.md (incl. Pre-push gate), docs/adr/0028-relevance-evidence-and-the-checker-scheduler.md (incl. the A2 section PR 490 added), the PR body /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/pr/feat-list-props-by-usage.md and /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/pr/fix-list-props-memory.md (keep its memory wins: peak RSS shadcn ~976 MiB, Chakra ~1,825; do not regress them), crates/core/src/relevance/ (`decide`, `Placement`, `narrow`, `apply`), pipeline/semantic_hook.rs, types/semantic.rs, react_types.rs. THE USER'S EXACT WORDS (the product rule, non-negotiable): 'We want to make sure we're providing everything in the main props even if the story doesn't use them. And anything that the actual Button component uses directly. ... It seems like you understood the use to mean used in the story but that is not what I meant.' And earlier: 'produce the best results, not the overwhelming massive numbers that are not useful to anyone'. THE RULE to implement, in BOTH lanes through the one sink: (1) MAIN PROPS ARE LISTED IN FULL: every member of the component's props type that comes from the component's API sources is a listed row, regardless of any story or call site: the props type's own members, members of project sources (collapse still applies to project sources above 200), and members of dependency sources that are API-sized interfaces (e.g. Chakra `ButtonLoadingProps` (loadingText, spinner), `PolymorphicProps` (as, asChild), `UnstyledProp` (unstyled), `JsxStyleProps` (css), `HtmlProps`, the recipe props variant/size/colorPalette/loading/spinnerPlacement). (2) WHAT THE COMPONENT USES DIRECTLY: a member from ANY source, including DOM/ambient/large ones, is a listed typed row when the component's body reads it, destructures it (including with defaults), or passes it explicitly to a child (the T1/T3 body facts: `BodyFacts.reads`, `elements`/attributes, forwarding), never through a spread onto a DOM tag (a DOM spread is no evidence; a spread onto a component resolves to that component's non-ambient props, T3); an unknown body (`handed_on`) is unknown: it does not promote anything and does not hide anything that rule (1) lists. (3) BIG GENERATED / AMBIENT SOURCES STAY AS LAYER NAMES unless (2) promotes a member: the 286 `@types/react` button attributes, `SystemProperties` (706), Chakra `Conditions` (130 `_active`, `2xl`...). Distinguish generated from API by STRUCTURE and PROVENANCE, never by name lists: ambient by declaring path (existing `Origin`), large by the existing collapse thresholds (more than 30 ambient / 200 other), and a source whose members come from a homomorphic mapped type over `keyof` a large interface (Conditions: PR 490's commit 89275198 gives such a member its key's interface as parent) is generated style-system noise: define that rule precisely, justify it, and test it; if a size-only variant gives the same results on the corpora, prefer the simplest. (4) Story args and call-site frequency are NO LONGER the criterion for the main props: keep them ONLY as an additional promotion for members of the noise sources (a story arg naming a collapsed prop makes it a row so the Control shows the arg; call-site floor evidence stays in `decide` as a secondary promotion; if keeping the call-site floor makes the output harder to explain, drop it and say so: simplest correct design wins; amend ADR 0028 A2 via the adr skill with the exact new rule and why (the owner's clarification)). `htmlAttributes` remains 'which DOM attributes are KNOWN'. `collapseInheritedProps: none` still lists everything. Acceptance, measure and put in the PR note: (a) demo sb-demo Button (/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/sb-demo/src/Button.tsx: `ButtonProps & React.ComponentProps<'button'> & { tone, fresh, size, kind, extra }`, body `<button {...props}/>`) lists ALL of Chakra ButtonProps' non-noise members (loadingText, spinner, asChild, as, unstyled, css, variant, size, colorPalette, loading, spinnerPlacement, recipe, html* ...: enumerate which ones exist in the installed @chakra-ui/react types and show them) plus the five own props and children from args, and NOT the 286/706/130 noise members; show the exact row list before (10 rows) and after, in CLI (`extract --src sb-demo/src --json ...`, decode the interned `props`/`propSets`/`nameLists` with a script kept in scratch under /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/ not the repo) and in Storybook dev mode rows (sb-demo/serve.sh; playwright MCP tools via ToolSearch select:mcp__playwright__browser_navigate,mcp__playwright__browser_evaluate,mcp__playwright__browser_wait_for); (b) a component whose body reads `props.onClick` / destructures `{ className = 'x' }` / passes `onFocus={props.onFocus}` to a child lists those DOM props as rows even from the 286-attribute source, and one that only spreads onto `<button>` lists none of them (new tests, both lanes, model-based: extend relevance_model.rs); (c) the main-props DIFFERENTIAL, this time INCLUDING props inherited from dependencies' API interfaces: for every component on gate-large, chakra-only, Mantine, antd, shadcn and Spectrum, the set of members that sit in sources of at most 30 members (any origin except ambient DOM/React/shared-DOM) plus all members