`api` is then true for every one of them and all of them become rows. Before this change, a non-ambient member with no evidence followed the collapse rule.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/core/src/extractor/body_facts.rs\",\n    \"line\": 316,\n    \"summary\": \"`BodyFacts::handed_on` is still computed at about 10 sites, stored in `types/collected.rs` and serialized into the cache, but nothing reads it any more since `Forwarding::handed_on` and `Body::handed_on` were removed.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Dead state that is computed, cached and tested (body_facts/tests.rs asserts it about 15 times). The module docs at body_facts.rs:25-30 still say `reads` is complete only while `handed_on` is false, which misleads the next reader about a contract nothing enforces. Remove the field (bumping CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION) or note that it is unused.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/core/src/relevance/mod.rs\",\n    \"line\": 43,\n    \"summary\": \"The new comment says the resolver collapses a style system 'past `LARGE_API_SOURCE` members', but this code path's notion of large is COLLAPSE_THRESHOLD, and an ambient dependency style system collapses past COLLAPSE_THRESHOLD.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A reader trusts the comment and assumes the cut-off is 200. In fact relevance treats anything over 30 as large and the resolver collapses ambient dependency style sources over 30. The threshold mismatch in the second finding is hidden by this wrong comment.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/core/src/relevance/mod.rs\",\n    \"line\": 5,\n    \"summary\": \"The module docs still describe four outcomes ('a typed row, a name in its collapsed layer's `used` list, left in that layer, or unknown because the body says nothing'), but `Shown` now has only `rows` and `collapsed`.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"The documented contract of `decide` no longer matches its output. A maintainer looking for the 'unknown' path, or for ambient-read members going to `used`, finds neither.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/core/src/relevance/forwarding/tests.rs\",\n    \"line\": 97,\n    \"summary\": \"The test helper `inherited()` was changed to `large: true`, so the unresolved-spread and handed-on tests (still named `..._is_unknown`) now cover only large sources. No test covers a non-ambient dependency source of 31 to 200 members behind an unresolved spread, the case where the behaviour regressed.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"`a_spread_onto_a_tag_that_does_not_resolve_is_unknown` and `a_component_whose_props_did_not_resolve_is_unknown` now assert `collapsed`, so the regression in the first finding is locked in as expected behaviour, and the test names contradict their assertions.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/core/src/relevance/mod.rs\",\n    \"line\": 272,\n    \"summary\": \"An ambient member the signature defaults (`{ className = 'x' }`), or that the body only reads, is now a full typed row in `props` instead of a `used` name in the DOM layer.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Every component that destructures `className`, `children`, `style` or `onClick` with or without a default now gets typed Controls rows for those DOM attributes, as the snapshot growth shows. Under the old ADR Combination rule these stayed layer names. If the decision intends only body-'used' members, this increases the rows for most shadcn-style components.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nI accidentally ran `git checkout 2f234371` in this worktree, which detached HEAD. I switched back to `fix/list-main-props` right away; it is the same commit. The worktree has an uncommitted change to `crates/core/src/relevance/mod.rs` that I did not make and did not touch. It was outside the review range, so I did not review it.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>84081</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>9</tool_uses><duration_ms>115876</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","reason":"absorbed_mid_turn","commandUuid":"44d91847-81d4-4c1a-9ec5-e9404d227e86","deliveryId":"cd280186-7e97-4a4c-b