{"parentUuid":"5ac2295d-f689-4c3e-8043-ef4b78c51810","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Ci9XiiwiPZVVPP8iVZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":85,"cache_read_input_tokens":914975,"output_tokens":4219,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1394},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":85,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4219,"cache_read_input_tokens":914975,"cache_creation_input_tokens":85,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":85},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":11745,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"8917260b-ed7f-4054-a58b-ff5604896637","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch7Ci8d9fCw9uVgashD7z","requestRef":"99b8634d-45ac-4d55-be84-0d6e6be9c46b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7b2595a4-7556-4e48-83f4-095ea9def107","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:01:40.230Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
{"parentUuid":"7b2595a4-7556-4e48-83f4-095ea9def107","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Ci9XiiwiPZVVPP8iVZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Noted: `colorPalette` stays hidden, and I won't special-case it.\n\n**Will this work for other components?** In principle yes, because the rule decides by provenance and structure and never by name. But I've only proven it on seven corpora and one demo component, so I don't know yet. The 0-violation differential shows no main prop got hidden. It doesn't show that the right things are hidden, or that the patterns we haven't looked at behave.\n\n**Patterns where it could break**\n- **Main props from a large source.** A library whose API sits in one interface over 200 members, or in a mapped copy over `keyof`. Collapse already treats it as generated.\n- **Style-system props that are API.** Chakra's `colorPalette` and `bg`, Mantine's `c` and `p`, and Panda's props live in the generated style source. You've accepted hiding them, but a pattern-level view should show how many such props there are.\n- **Polymorphic `as` components.** Their props depend on a type parameter, and only the checker can see them.\n- **Components that pass props through a hook** (`useButton(props)`). The body is \"handed on\", so no usage evidence, and only the main-props rule applies.\n- **Compound components, `forwardRef` and `memo` wrappers, and factory-built ones.**\n\n**What I'm starting now.** A read-only evaluation (Opus, 80 calls, no code changes) across the repo's roughly 20 validated fixture libraries: shadcn, Radix, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, antd, ariakit, ark-ui, base-ui, blueprint, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, panda and more. For each library it reports:\n- **Rows per component** on `main` versus #490, with medians.\n- **What's hidden:** the top hidden prop names per library, so we can see which patterns lose useful props. It classifies each hidden member as generated style noise, DOM or ambient, or a real API prop.\n- **Pattern buckets:** which of the patterns above each library falls into, with a representative component and what it shows.\n- **A verdict and proposed rule fixes** where a pattern is wrong, so we fix patterns, not components.\n\nI'll bring back the table and anything that needs a rule change before #490 merges."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":85,"cache_read_input_tokens":914975,"output_tokens":4219,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1394},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":85,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4219,"cache_read_input_tokens":914975,"cache_creation_input_tokens":85,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":85},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8917260b-ed7f-4054-a58b-ff5604896637","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch7Ci8d9fCw9uVgashD7z","requestRef":"99b8634d-45ac-4d55-be84-0d6e6be9c46b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0a06aeec-4e27-4101-a249-8e9252881062","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:01:45.741Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
{"parentUuid":"0a06aeec-4e27-4101-a249-8e9252881062","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Ci9XiiwiPZVVPP8iVZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015saUdnrNCr11XTFMNPzgcp","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Evaluate the listing rule across the ~20 fixture libraries by pattern","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"EVALUATE, do not fix or push. Question from the user: does PR 490's new listing rule (`origin/feat/list-props-by-usage` at d884334e: main props listed in full; a member from any source listed when the component's body reads/destructures/passes it explicitly, not through a DOM spread; big generated/ambient sources (a source over 200 members, ambient by declaring path, or a mapped copy of `keyof` over 30 members) stay as names in a layer; story args and call-site floor are secondary promotions) work well for OTHER components and libraries, 'we are not trying to one-off this work, we want to address the patterns'? Read /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/pr/feat-list-props-by-usage.md (the rule and evidence), docs/adr/0028-relevance-evidence-and-the-checker-scheduler.md (A2), /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/worker-contract.md, docs/rdt-coverage.md and docs/STATUS.md (they name the ~20 real-world fixture libraries the project validates against: shadcn, Radix, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, antd, ariakit, ark-ui, base-ui, blueprint, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, panda, react-final-form, react-resizable... find where they live: `git grep -n \"ariakit\" -- 'scripts/*' 'docs/*.md' | head`, /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/corpora/ (five installed) and any fixtures dir with the rest, e.g. `ls tests/fixtures`, apps/oracle, scripts/corpora.py; use whichever are installed locally; do NOT fetch or reinstall large corpora unless a small one is missing and cheap: say which you could not run). Build both binaries: origin/main de016f69 or later (reuse /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/target/release/caliper-docgen) and PR 490's head (reuse /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/shrink/lpm/target/release/caliper-docgen if it is d884334e or later: check `git log` of its source; else build into your own CARGO_TARGET_DIR under /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval/, rust 1.99.1 first on PATH /Users/gabe/.rustup/toolchains/1.99.1-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin). For each available library run `extract --json --load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies --no-cache` with both binaries (checker on) and decode the interned output (a decoder script kept in scratch under oracle-run/pattern-eval/, NOT in the repo: component props are `propSets`/`props`/`nameLists` hash-interned; inspect the JSON and the existing /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/ scripts such as counts.py). Report per library: components, median and p95 rows (props + notableInherited) main vs 490; count of components whose rows grew by more than 30 or fell by more than 90%; for hidden members (names in layers that were rows on main or that sit in API-sized sources): classify each as (a) DOM/ARIA/event ambient noise, (b) generated style-system noise (names like style props, conditions, `_hover`), (c) a REAL API prop of the component (declared in the component's own props type or a small dependency API interface) hidden by mistake, (d) other; count them per library and list the TOP 15 hidden names per library with their declaring source, so the lead can eyeball real APIs among them. Pattern buckets: assign each component to one pattern and report counts and 2 representative examples (rows listed, rows hidden) per pattern: own props type only; wrapper over a design-system props type with DOM spread (`<button {...props}/>`); polymorphic `as`; forwardRef/memo wrapper; compound/namespace component (Menu.Item); hook-driven (`useX(props)` handed_on); factory-built (chakra('div'), createLeaf); component with props from a generic/conditional (checker-only); component re-exporting a dependency component. Then check the RULE'S FAILURE MODES with targeted probes (small synthetic components in scratch, both lanes): (i) body reads a DOM prop in a nested closure / event handler / useEffect / template; (ii) body passes `{...rest}` after destructuring some props onto a child COMPONENT (T3 forwarding: the child's non-ambient props are used: are they listed?) vs onto a DOM tag; (iii) props accessed only via `props['x']` or aliases `const p = props`; (iv) a default-exported anonymous arrow; (v) a prop declared in a >200-member project source (collapse) that the body reads; (vi) a component with 40 API props in ONE dependency interface (is a mid-size real API source (31-200 members) fully listed? it must be); (vii) a props type that is a union/discriminated union; (viii) a wrapper that renames props. Deliverable: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval.md: tables per library and per pattern, the failure-mode probe results (pass/fail with the output), the top hidden real-API candidates, an honest verdict per pattern ('works', 'works with caveat', 'broken') and proposed RULE-LEVEL changes (not per-component fixes) with the expected effect, plus what you could not run. Do not change repo files or push. Cap 80 tool calls; run long commands in the background and poll. Final message at most 90 words: libraries covered, the worst pattern, any real-API prop hidden by mistake (count), and the path."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":85,"cache_read_input_tokens":914975,"output_tokens":4219,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1394},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":85,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"in