interned; inspect the JSON and the existing /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/ scripts such as counts.py). Report per library: components, median and p95 rows (props + notableInherited) main vs 490; count of components whose rows grew by more than 30 or fell by more than 90%; for hidden members (names in layers that were rows on main or that sit in API-sized sources): classify each as (a) DOM/ARIA/event ambient noise, (b) generated style-system noise (names like style props, conditions, `_hover`), (c) a REAL API prop of the component (declared in the component's own props type or a small dependency API interface) hidden by mistake, (d) other; count them per library and list the TOP 15 hidden names per library with their declaring source, so the lead can eyeball real APIs among them. Pattern buckets: assign each component to one pattern and report counts and 2 representative examples (rows listed, rows hidden) per pattern: own props type only; wrapper over a design-system props type with DOM spread (`<button {...props}/>`); polymorphic `as`; forwardRef/memo wrapper; compound/namespace component (Menu.Item); hook-driven (`useX(props)` handed_on); factory-built (chakra('div'), createLeaf); component with props from a generic/conditional (checker-only); component re-exporting a dependency component. Then check the RULE'S FAILURE MODES with targeted probes (small synthetic components in scratch, both lanes): (i) body reads a DOM prop in a nested closure / event handler / useEffect / template; (ii) body passes `{...rest}` after destructuring some props onto a child COMPONENT (T3 forwarding: the child's non-ambient props are used: are they listed?) vs onto a DOM tag; (iii) props accessed only via `props['x']` or aliases `const p = props`; (iv) a default-exported anonymous arrow; (v) a prop declared in a >200-member project source (collapse) that the body reads; (vi) a component with 40 API props in ONE dependency interface (is a mid-size real API source (31-200 members) fully listed? it must be); (vii) a props type that is a union/discriminated union; (viii) a wrapper that renames props. Deliverable: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval.md: tables per library and per pattern, the failure-mode probe results (pass/fail with the output), the top hidden real-API candidates, an honest verdict per pattern ('works', 'works with caveat', 'broken') and proposed RULE-LEVEL changes (not per-component fixes) with the expected effect, plus what you could not run. Do not change repo files or push. Cap 80 tool calls; run long commands in the background and poll. Final message at most 90 words: libraries covered, the worst pattern, any real-API prop hidden by mistake (count), and the path.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper/ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba/tasks/a664ef066cde44793.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8917260b-ed7f-4054-a58b-ff5604896637","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","branch":"mf-t4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4477da52-e954-4e1c-b7d7-a98e9e1c1e69","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessio