{"parentUuid":"45d95ebe-1f3d-4ecc-a7e7-e5bde130a7de","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7DM87v6V9MsivoEZiXk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017Q5opC7DqvHk14e4UiWGut","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":723,"cache_read_input_tokens":923164,"output_tokens":82,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":723,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":82,"cache_read_input_tokens":923164,"cache_creation_input_tokens":723,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":723},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017Q5opC7DqvHk14e4UiWGut":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval.md"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"56777f77-02eb-462b-8b2f-1f44aa8f5bf9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch7DM6MWDHFoQrtzLAouA","requestRef":"29ec7dc6-4410-4882-8039-16f56e57a9db","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"603f3223-0805-4b37-96b4-457fc8721d58","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:09:50.642Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
{"parentUuid":"603f3223-0805-4b37-96b4-457fc8721d58","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a783a593-d77b-401d-ab4d-5832f479cd0f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Q5opC7DqvHk14e4UiWGut","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Pattern evaluation: PR 490's listing rule (feat/list-props-by-usage, d884334e) vs main\n2\t\n3\tQuestion: does the rule (main props in full; any member the body reads, destructures or passes by name, but not through a DOM spread; generated or ambient sources stay layer names) work for other components and libraries as a pattern, not as a one-off?\n4\t\n5\tShort answer: **mostly yes.** It removes DOM, ARIA and event noise across every library, keeps every own-props component unchanged, and both lanes agree on every probe. It has five rule-level gaps, and four of them hide real API:\n6\t1. Ambient is decided by file path. React Aria's API interfaces that live in `@react-types/shared/src/dom.d.ts` are therefore hidden.\n7\t2. A member that @types/react also declares is hidden, even when a small API interface declares it.\n8\t3. The generated rule does not apply to project sources, so Chakra's own repo still lists 130 condition names on Button.\n9\t4. Reads do not promote members of collapsed or >200-member sources.\n10\t5. The mapped-type rule hides a real 40-key API.\n11\t\n12\t## Setup\n13\t\n14\t- **Main:** `oracle-run/target/release/caliper-docgen`, built 2026-11-15 22:37, 6 minutes after de016f69 (the first-parent tip at the time). I took it to be de016f69 and did not re-verify it by rebuild.\n15\t- **PR 490:** `shrink/list-main-props/target/release/caliper-docgen`. It was built 2026-11-16 11:36 from worktree `agent-af9171696…` at d884334e, 2 minutes after the commit. Note: `shrink/lpm` is the fix-list-props-memory build (PR 490's \"before\"), not d884334e, so I did not use it.\n16\t- **Flags:** `extract --json --quiet --no-cache --load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies`, checker on.\n17\t- **Runs reused:** the PR 490 listed and expanded (`none`) runs on the five corpora are reused from `oracle-run/list-main-props/runs/*.after.json` and `*.expanded.json`. That is the same binary with the same flags.\n18\t- **Runs made here:**\n19\t  - main on the five corpora\n20\t  - main and PR 490 on the repo's `fixtures/`\n21\t  - PR 490 expanded on `fixtures/`\n22\t- **Libraries covered:**\n23\t  - 5 installed corpora: Chakra (`packages/react/src`), Mantine (`@mantine/core`), antd (`components`), shadcn (`apps/v4`), React Spectrum (`packages`)\n24\t  - 19 of the 20 `fixtures/` libraries (vendored files, @types/react resolved, other deps mostly unresolved): ariakit, ark-ui, base-ui, blueprint, chakra, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, mantine, mui, panda, radix, react-aria, react-final-form, react-resizable-panels, shadcn, storybook-emotion, tanstack-table, antd, plus rdt-compat\n25\t- **Scratch** (not in the repo), under `oracle-run/pattern-eval/`:\n26\t  - `run.sh` (runs)\n27\t  - `eval.py` (rows, hidden classes, patterns)\n28\t  - `mixed.py` (multi-declaration and SharedDom audit)\n29\t  - `patterns.out`\n30\t  - `probes/` (probe project, `run.sh`, `show.py`, `show.out`)\n31\t  - `<lib>.out`\n32\t\n33\t**Definitions:**\n34\t- **Rows:** `props` + `notableInherited`.\n35\t- **Hidden members** are the union of two sets:\n36\t  - members that are rows on main and not on PR 490;\n37\t  - names in PR 490 layers whose source (from the expanded run) is non-ambient and has at most 200 members.\n38\t- **Classes:**\n39\t  - (a) DOM, ARIA or event, declared under @types/react or `@react-types/shared` `dom.d.ts`\n40\t  - (b) generated: csstype, `_`-prefixed, a source over 200 members, or a System/Conditions-like source\n41\t  - (c) real API, declared by the component's own type or by a small (≤200) non-ambient source\n42\t  - (d) other\n43\t\n44\t## Per library (components present in both runs)\n45\t\n46\tEach entry gives rows main → 490 as median, p95 and total; how many components grew by more than 30 rows or fell by more than 90%; and the hidden members by class.\n47\t\n48\t**Corpora:**\n49\t- **Chakra repo:** 629 components.\n50\t  - Rows: median 139 → 139; p95 154 → 150; total 84,386 → 81,972\n51\t  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 7\n52\t  - Hidden: a 2,521, b 0, c 0, d 0\n53\t- **Mantine:** 348 components.\n54\t  - Rows: median 72 → 72; p95 107 → 106; total 20,873 → 20,348\n55\t  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 1\n56\t  - Hidden: a 592 (incl. `ref` ×11), b 0, c 0, d 0\n57\t- **antd:** 254 components.\n58\t  - Rows: median 14 → 13; p95 148 → 61; total 9,114 → 4,975\n59\t  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 7\n60\t  - Hidden: a 4,219, b 0, c 0, d 0\n61\t- **shadcn:** 1,901 components.\n62\t  - Rows: median 2 → 3; p95 51 → 19; total 33,249 → 11,142\n63\t  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 75\n64\t  - Hidden: a 23,527 (515 of them SharedDom API-named), b 0, c 34, d 0\n65\t- **React Spectrum:** 1,415 components.\n66\t  - Rows: median 11 → 6; p95 112 → 55; total 52,011 → 18,739\n67\t  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 100\n68\t  - Hidden: a 33,298 (4,584 of them SharedDom API-named), b 0, c 102, d 0\n69\t\n70\t**Fixtures:**\n71\t- **ark-ui:** 2 components.\n72\t  - Rows: median 174.5 → 37; p95 313 → 37; total 349 → 74\n73\t  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 0\n74\t  - Hidden: a 276, nothing in b, c or d\n75\t- **react-resizable-panels:** 1 component.\n76\t  - Rows: median 288 → 14; total 288 → 14\n77\t  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 1\n78\t  - Hidden: a 274, nothing in b, c or d\n79\t- **chakra (vendored styled-system):** 8 components.\n80\t  - Rows: median 863.5 → 864.5; p95 884 → 885; total 6,943 → 6,951\n81\t  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 0\n82\t  - Hidden: none (the project source is not narrowed)\n83\t- **The 16 other fixture libraries:** ariakit, base-ui, blueprint, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, mantine, mui, panda, radix, rdt-compat, react-aria, react-final-form, shadcn, storybook-emotion, tanstack-table and antd, with 1 to 12 components each.\n84\t  - Rows change by 0 to +3 per component.\n85\t  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 0\n86\t  - Hidden: none\n87\t- **zendesk-garden:** no component matched in both runs.\n88\t\n89\t**What the class (c) numbers contain:**\n90\t- **shadcn (34):**\n91\t  - The aria `Item` (`registry/bases/aria/ui/item.tsx`): 8 members (onBlur, onFocus, onKeyDown, onKeyUp, autoFocus, onClick, slot, style). They come from 1 to 3-member React Aria interfaces (`FocusEvents`, `KeyboardEvents`, `PressEvents`, `FocusableProps` in `@react-types/shared/src/events.d.ts`; `SlotProps`, `StyleRenderProps` in react-aria-components `utils.d.ts`). They are hidden on main too, so they break the \"API source in full\" rule rather than being a 490 regression.\n92\t  - `excludeFromTabOrder` ×26.\n93\t- **Spectrum (102):**\n94\t  - `excludeFromTabOrder` ×55\n95\t  - `routerOptions` ×47\n96\t- **Where they are declared:** `excludeFromTabOrder` and `routerOptions` are not DOM attributes. They are React Aria API declared in `@react-types/shared/src/dom.d.ts` (`FocusableDOMProps`, `LinkDOMProps`), and that file is ambient by path. They were rows on main and are hidden by 490.\n97\t- **Total:** 136 component rows across 10 distinct names.\n98\t- **Debatable, counted in (a):** `id`, `aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`, `aria-describedby` and `aria-details` in React Aria's `DOMProps` and `AriaLabelingProps`. They are documented Spectrum API that happen to be DOM-named. 4,584 component rows on Spectrum and 515 on shadcn are hidden.\n99\t\n100\t**Top 15 hidden names per library** (count; source and its member count in brackets):\n101\t- **shadcn:** lang 182, hidden 178, inert 178, translate 178, dir 174 (GlobalDOMAttributes [5], dom.d.ts); aria-describedby 149, aria-details 149, aria-labelledby 149, aria-label 146 (@types/react AriaAttributes [53]); onClick 139 (GlobalDOMEvents [64]); id 121 (DOMProps [1], dom.d.ts); rel 92 (HTMLAttributes [55]); aria-errormessage 83, aria-modal 79 (AriaAttributes); onTransitionCancel 79 (DOMAttributes [170]).\n102\t- **antd:** aria-label 26, aria-labelledby 25, then 13 more AriaAttributes at 23 each (aria-setsize, aria-rowcount, aria-grabbed, aria-posinset, aria-multiselectable, aria-autocomplete, aria-required, aria-colindextext, aria-checked, aria-keyshortcuts, aria-valuemax, aria-valuemin, aria-valuetext), all @types/react [53].\n103\t- **Spectrum:** id 868 (DOMProps [1]); aria-details 867, aria-describedby 866, aria-labelledby 847, aria-label 815 (AriaLabelingProps [4], dom.d.ts); then GlobalDOMEvents [64] at 223 each: onAnimationEnd, onMouseLeave, onTransitionCancelCapture, onMouseOverCapture, onScrollCapture, onMouseUp, onTouchEnd, onTransitionRunCapture, onTransitionStart, onPointerEnter.\n104\t- **Mantine:** ref 11 (RefAttributes [1], @types/react); then @types/react members at 2 each: onAnimationEndCapture, onSubmitCapture, about, onLoadedData, onDragEndCapture, title, aria-orientation, onAnimationIterationCapture, onTransitionRunCapture, unselectable, onTouchCancel, onTouchMove, prefix, onFocus.\n105\t- **Chakra:** @types/react DOM, ARIA and event members, 9 each: onTransitionCancel, aria-describedby, onLostPointerCapture, onLoadedData, onTransitionCancelCapture, aria-errormessage, part, onBeforeInputCapture, popoverTargetAction, onGotPointerCapture, onKeyDown, onScrollEnd, onTransitionStart, aria-valuemax, onDrop.\n106\t- **ark-ui and react-resizable-panels fixtures:** all @types/react DOMAttributes, AriaAttributes and HTMLAttributes (onStalled, aria-live, defaultChecked…).\n107\t- **Real-API names among them**, for the lead to eyeball:\n108\t  - `excludeFromTabOrder`, `routerOptions` (certain)\n109\t  - `id` and the four `aria-*` labelling props on React Aria and Spectrum (documented)\n110\t  - `ref` on Mantine (debatable)\n111\t- **Generated noise (b) that is listed, not hidden:** Chakra's own repo `Button` has 147 rows, of which 104 are `_*` conditions and 26 are breakpoints (`2xl`, `mdDown`…): only 17 are real API. The chakra fixture has about 864 rows. Cause: \"only sources outside the project are narrowed\", so the generated rule never applies to an in-repo style system.\n112\t\n113\t## Per pattern (all libraries)\n114\t\n115\tPatterns were assigned heuristically from `detectedBy`, the exports and a regex over the component's file. They are approximate. Each entry gives the component count, rows main → 490 as median, p95 and fell >90%, the hidden members, two examples, and a verdict.\n116\t\n117\t- **Own props type only:** 674 components.\n118\t  - Rows: median 2 → 2; p95 25 → 25; fell >90%: 0. Hidden: 0.\n119\t  - Examples: blueprint `Column` 7 → 7 (cellRenderer, className, …); day-picker `DayPicker` 68 → 68.\n120\t  - Verdict: **works.**\n121\t- **DOM-spread wrapper:** 1,397 components.\n122\t  - Rows: median 2 → 3; p95 280 → 27; fell >90%: 82. Hidden: 26,231.\n123\t  - Examples: shadcn `ChartLegend` 500 → 176, keeping align, content, formatter, iconType… and hiding SVG attributes (accentHeight…); a Spectrum icon `ForwardRef` 488 → 0, hiding only SVG attributes.\n124\t  - Verdict: **works.** The noise removed is DOM or SVG.\n125\t- **Polymorphic `as`:** 547 components.\n126\t  - Rows: median 139 → 139; p95 152 → 151; fell >90%: 0. Hidden: 564.\n127\t  - Examples: Chakra `ArkEditableTextarea` 429 → 140, still listing `2xl`, `_active`, `_after`…; headlessui `Listbox` 14 → 14.\n128\t  - Verdict: **works with caveat.** The generated rule is not applied to project sources.\n129\t- **forwardRef or memo wrapper:** 115 components.\n130\t  - Rows: median 16 → 14; p95 116 → 56; fell >90%: 7. Hidden: 2,133.\n131\t  - Examples: antd `OTPInput` 328 → 29, keeping addonAfter, allowClear, count…; Spectrum `CarouselNavButton` 114 → 39, hiding aria-label, id and `excludeFromTabOrder`.\n132\t  - Verdict: **works with caveat** (SharedDom API; Mantine `ref`).\n133\t- **Compound or namespace component:** 25 components.\n134\t  - Rows: median 28 → 27; p95 306 → 90; fell >90%: 1. Hidden: 1,014.\n135\t  - Examples: antd `Input.Password` 329 → 29, keeping action, addonAfter, allowClear…; base-ui `MenuRoot` 15 → 15.\n136\t  - Verdict: **works.**\n137\t- **Hook-driven (`useX(props)`):** 1,028 components, 1,019 of them Spectrum.\n138\t  - Rows: median 11 → 6; p95 103 → 58; fell >90%: 50. Hidden: 16,809.\n139\t  - Examples: Spectrum `Input` 313 → 8 (UNSAFE_className, placeholder, styles…); ariakit `MenuProvider` 7 → 7.\n140\t  - Verdict: **works with caveat, and it is the worst pattern.** Props handed to a hook promote nothing, so the API in SharedDom stays hidden.\n141\t- **Factory-built:** 71 components.\n142\t  - Rows: median 100 → 79; p95 143 → 143; fell >90%: 10. Hidden: 1,629.\n143\t  - Examples: react-aria-components `Tab` 100 → 19, hiding aria-label, href, download and routerOptions (`LinkDOMProps`); antd `Calendar` 25 → 24, hiding `ref`.\n144\t  - Verdict: **works with caveat** (SharedDom; Chakra factories still list conditions).\n145\t- **Generic or conditional props:** 62 components.\n146\t  - Rows: median 68.5 → 31.5; p95 313 → 122; fell >90%: 5. Hidden: 2,809.\n147\t  - Examples: antd `InternalInputNumber` 333 → 39, keeping changeOnWheel, controls…; shadcn `Accordion` 287 → 10, keeping collapsible, onValueChange, orientation…\n148\t  - Verdict: **works** (and the union probe passes).\n149\t- **Re-exporting a dependency component:** 0 components detected.\n150\t  - Verdict: **not measured.** My heuristic found none, so this pattern is unverified.\n151\t- **Other** (unclassified): 680 components.\n152\t  - Rows: median 12 → 9; p95 279 → 87; fell >90%: 36. Hidden: 13,526.\n153\t  - Examples: shadcn `Input` 314 → 12, keeping placeholder, render…; Spectrum `Add` icon 489 → 2.\n154\t  - Verdict: not judged as a pattern.\n155\t\n156\t## Failure-mode probes\n157\t\n158\tThe probe project is `oracle-run/pattern-eval/probes` (`src/probes*.tsx`, `src/anon.tsx`, a fake dependency `node_modules/fake-lib`, and @types/react linked from the repo). I ran both binaries, checker and `--no-checker`. **PR 490's two lanes agree on every probe.** Main's two lanes disagree: the checker lane lists 1 row and the structural lane 279 on the same DOM-spread components. Unless a line says otherwise, the output quoted is PR 490's, identical in both lanes.\n159\t\n160\t- **(i) Reads in nested code — PASS.** The DOM props read in a handler, a `useEffect`, a template literal and a nested function (title, tabIndex, lang, dir, plus a direct `hidden`) are all listed; the other 273 members stay a layer.\n161\t  - `P1Closures`: rows 6, `['dir','hidden','lang','tabIndex','title']`.\n162\t- **(ii) Rest spread onto a component vs onto a DOM tag — PASS.**\n163\t  - `{own2, ...rest}` → `<Inner {...rest}/>`, where `Inner` destructures `title` and `onFocus`: rows `onFocus`, `title`.\n164\t  - The same onto `<div {...rest}/>`: no DOM rows.\n165\t  - Onto the dependency `FakeButton` (Big40 & button attributes): all 40 `api*` listed and no DOM members, correctly.\n166\t- **(iii) Bracket and alias access — PARTIAL FAIL.**\n167\t  - `props['title']`: listed.\n168\t  - `const p = props; p.lang`: **not listed** (`Q2AliasMemberNoSpread`: 0 rows).\n169\t  - `const p = props; const {title} = p` with no spread: **55 rows**, the whole `@types/react` `HTMLAttributes` interface (about, accessKey, autoCapitalize…) instead of 1. The same code with `{...props}` added gives 0 rows. Alias handling is unsound in both directions.\n170\t- **(iv) Default-exported anonymous arrow — PASS.** `Anon`: rows `own4`, `title`.\n171\t- **(v) A body read of a member of a >200-member source — FAIL.**\n172\t  - A project interface of 210 members: `props.loc5` is read, yet loc5 stays in layer `HugeLocalProps` (210) with rows 1. It is the same on main.\n173\t  - A dependency interface of 210: `props.big5` is not listed either.\n174\t  - Collapsed or large layers are never promoted by reads, which contradicts \"a member from any source the body reads\".\n175\t- **(vi) A 40-member API in one dependency interface — PASS, with one FAIL.**\n176\t  - `extends`, the bare type, `Partial`, `Required` and `Omit`: all 40 (or 39) listed.\n177\t  - **FAIL:** a homomorphic mapped copy `{ [K in keyof Big40Props]?: boolean }` gives rows 1 (`api0`, read) and a layer `Big40Props` of 39. Main listed 40. The mapped-over-more-than-30-keys rule hides real API that has the same shape as Chakra's `Conditions`.\n178\t- **(vii) Discriminated union & DOM — PASS.** Rows `alpha`, `beta`, `kind`, `title` (title is read in one branch).\n179\t- **(viii) A wrapper that renames props — PASS.** `{label, press, lang: language, ...rest}` → rows label, lang, press. The renamed DOM destructure is listed.\n180\t- **Extra (ix): members of small dependency API interfaces that @types/react also declares — FAIL.** This is the shape of the shadcn aria `Item`.\n181\t  - Props: `FocusEventsApi`(onFocus, onBlur) & `SlotApi`(slot) & `HTMLAttributes`, with a DOM spread.\n182\t  - Rows 0; layers `FocusEventsApi` 2/2 and `SlotApi` 1/1.\n183\t  - The 1 to 2-member API sources are hidden, against rule 2.\n184\t- **Extra: forwardRef + memo — PASS.** Rows `ref`, `title`.\n185\t- **Extra: hook-driven — by design.** `useThing(props)` gives rows 1 (own only), so nothing is promoted.\n186\t\n187\t## Verdict per pattern\n188\t\n189\t- **Works:** own props only; DOM-spread wrapper; compound/namespace; generic or conditional (and unions).\n190\t- **Works with caveat:**\n191\t  - polymorphic `as`, and factory-built in an in-repo style system: generated noise is still listed;\n192\t  - forwardRef/memo: SharedDom API and `ref` are hidden;\n193\t  - factory-built: SharedDom API is hidden.\n194\t- **Works with caveat, and the worst:** hook-driven. Spectrum's 1,019 components lose `id`, `aria-label*`, `excludeFromTabOrder` and `routerOptions`.\n195\t- **Broken (probe-level, no corpus instance found):**\n196\t  - reads into large or collapsed sources;\n197\t  - mapped copies of a real API of more than 30 keys;\n198\t  - one-hop props aliases.\n199\t- **Not measured:** re-exported dependency components.\n200\t\n201\t## Proposed rule-level changes\n202\t\n203\t1. **Ambient by declaring interface, not by file.** Under `@react-types/shared/src/dom.d.ts`, only `GlobalDOMAttributes` and `GlobalDOMEvents` (and similar pure-DOM interfaces) should be ambient. Alternatively: ambient means declared by React's or the DOM lib's types, and an interface a library re-declares stays an API source when it is at most 200 members.\n204\t   - Effect: restores `excludeFromTabOrder` and `routerOptions` (136 component rows) and the documented `id` and `aria-label*` (about 5.1k component rows, about +4 to 5 rows per Spectrum component). The 64-member event lists stay hidden.\n205\t2. **A member is ambient only when every one of its declarations is ambient.**\n206\t   - Effect: fixes probe (ix) and the shadcn aria `Item` (8 rows). DOM-only members are unchanged.\n207\t3. **Apply \"generated\" (more than 200 members, or a mapped copy of large keys) to project sources too.** Keep \"a project source of at most 200 members is listed\".\n208\t   - Effect: Chakra's own repo `Button` goes from 147 to about 17 rows, and the chakra fixture from about 864 to tens. That fixes the polymorphic and factory caveat for in-repo design systems.\n209\t4. **Reads promote from layers.** A read, destructure or pass of a name that sits in a collapsed or >200-member layer of the same binding becomes a row (the per-component name lists already carry the names).\n210\t   - Effect: fixes probe (v), and keeps a recipe wrapper's `props.colorPalette` as a row.\n211\t5. **Mapped rule by the key interface's nature, not only its size.** Hide a mapped copy only when its key interface is itself generated or ambient (more than 200 members, collapsed, or ambient), or is a selector or token table (all members literal-string or non-callable values; this needs validating on `Conditions`).\n212\t   - Effect: fixes probe (vi-mapped). Whether `Conditions` (130 keys) is still caught must be checked first: as written, a size-only rule at 200 would not catch it.\n213\t6. **Follow one-hop aliases of the props binding** (`const p = props`) as the props binding, and fix the over-promotion. An aliased destructure with no spread lists the whole 55-member `HTMLAttributes`.\n214\t   - Effect: fixes probe (iii).\n215\t7. **Hook hand-off as forwarding.** Treat `useX(props)`, where the callee's parameter type resolves, like a spread onto a resolved component: the members the parameter type declares from non-ambient sources count as used.\n216\t   - Effect: after change 1, React Aria and Spectrum hook-driven components keep their API members without any per-component fixes.\n217\t\n218\t## Not run or not verified\n219\t\n220\t- I did not rebuild either binary. Main is identified by its build time (6 minutes after de016f69), and PR 490 by its worktree and build time (2 minutes after d884334e).\n221\t- PR 490's corpus runs were reused from `list-main-props/runs`, not re-run.\n222\t- The 13 non-corpus fixture libraries are vendored files whose dependencies mostly do not resolve. Their dependency-sourced patterns (Radix, MUI, ariakit generics…) are under-tested, and zendesk-garden matched no component.\n223\t- No large corpora were fetched (MUI, Radix, ariakit, ark-ui, base-ui, blueprint, fluentui, headlessui and panda as real installs).\n224\t- Pattern buckets are regex heuristics. Re-exported dependency components were not detected (0).\n225\t- The SharedDom split into API-named and DOM-named members is by interface name (`DOMProps`, `AriaLabelingProps`, `FocusableDOMProps`, `LinkDOMProps`…).\n226\t- I did not root-cause the 55-row over-promotion in probe (iii).\n227\t- No Storybook rendering was checked, and no oracle was run.\n228\t"}]},"uuid":"2e5c62bf-c65d-4cb5-a789-08d610dbda83","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:09:50.706Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval.md","content":"# Pattern evaluation: PR 490's listing rule (feat/list-props-by-usage, d884334e) vs main\n\nQuestion: does the rule (main props in full; any member the body reads, destructures or passes by name, but not through a DOM spread; generated or ambient sources stay layer names) work for other components and libraries as a pattern, not as a one-off?\n\nShort answer: **mostly yes.** It removes DOM, ARIA and event noise across every library, keeps every own-props component unchanged, and both lanes agree on every probe. It has five rule-level gaps, and four of them hide real API:\n1. Ambient is decided by file path. React Aria's API interfaces that live in `@react-types/shared/src/dom.d.ts` are therefore hidden.\n2. A member that @types/react also declares is hidden, even when a small API interface declares it.\n3. The generated rule does not apply to project sources, so Chakra's own repo still lists 130 condition names on Button.\n4. Reads do not promote members of collapsed or >200-member sources.\n5. The mapped-type rule hides a real 40-key API.\n\n## Setup\n\n- **Main:** `oracle-run/target/release/caliper-docgen`, built 2026-11-15 22:37, 6 minutes after de016f69 (the first-parent tip at the time). I took it to be de016f69 and did not re-verify it by rebuild.\n- **PR 490:** `shrink/list-main-props/target/release/caliper-docgen`. It was built 2026-11-16 11:36 from worktree `agent-af9171696…` at d884334e, 2 minutes after the commit. Note: `shrink/lpm` is the fix-list-props-memory build (PR 490's \"before\"), not d884334e, so I did not use it.\n- **Flags:** `extract --json --quiet --no-cache --load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies`, checker on.\n- **Runs reused:** the PR 490 listed and expanded (`none`) runs on the five corpora are reused from `oracle-run/list-main-props/runs/*.after.json` and `*.expanded.json`. That is the same binary with the same flags.\n- **Runs made here:**\n  - main on the five corpora\n  - main and PR 490 on the repo's `fixtures/`\n  - PR 490 expanded on `fixtures/`\n- **Libraries covered:**\n  - 5 installed corpora: Chakra (`packages/react/src`), Mantine (`@mantine/core`), antd (`components`), shadcn (`apps/v4`), React Spectrum (`packages`)\n  - 19 of the 20 `fixtures/` libraries (vendored files, @types/react resolved, other deps mostly unresolved): ariakit, ark-ui, base-ui, blueprint, chakra, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, mantine, mui, panda, radix, react-aria, react-final-form, react-resizable-panels, shadcn, storybook-emotion, tanstack-table, antd, plus rdt-compat\n- **Scratch** (not in the repo), under `oracle-run/pattern-eval/`:\n  - `run.sh` (runs)\n  - `eval.py` (rows, hidden classes, patterns)\n  - `mixed.py` (multi-declaration and SharedDom audit)\n  - `patterns.out`\n  - `probes/` (probe project, `run.sh`, `show.py`, `show.out`)\n  - `<lib>.out`\n\n**Definitions:**\n- **Rows:** `props` + `notableInherited`.\n- **Hidden members** are the union of two sets:\n  - members that are rows on main and not on PR 490;\n  - names in PR 490 layers whose source (from the expanded run) is non-ambient and has at most 200 members.\n- **Classes:**\n  - (a) DOM, ARIA or event, declared under @types/react or `@react-types/shared` `dom.d.ts`\n  - (b) generated: csstype, `_`-prefixed, a source over 200 members, or a System/Conditions-like source\n  - (c) real API, declared by the component's own type or by a small (≤200) non-ambient source\n  - (d) other\n\n## Per library (components present in both runs)\n\nEach entry gives rows main → 490 as median, p95 and total; how many components grew by more than 30 rows or fell by more than 90%; and the hidden members by class.\n\n**Corpora:**\n- **Chakra repo:** 629 components.\n  - Rows: median 139 → 139; p95 154 → 150; total 84,386 → 81,972\n  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 7\n  - Hidden: a 2,521, b 0, c 0, d 0\n- **Mantine:** 348 components.\n  - Rows: median 72 → 72; p95 107 → 106; total 20,873 → 20,348\n  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 1\n  - Hidden: a 592 (incl. `ref` ×11), b 0, c 0, d 0\n- **antd:** 254 components.\n  - Rows: median 14 → 13; p95 148 → 61; total 9,114 → 4,975\n  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 7\n  - Hidden: a 4,219, b 0, c 0, d 0\n- **shadcn:** 1,901 components.\n  - Rows: median 2 → 3; p95 51 → 19; total 33,249 → 11,142\n  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 75\n  - Hidden: a 23,527 (515 of them SharedDom API-named), b 0, c 34, d 0\n- **React Spectrum:** 1,415 components.\n  - Rows: median 11 → 6; p95 112 → 55; total 52,011 → 18,739\n  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 100\n  - Hidden: a 33,298 (4,584 of them SharedDom API-named), b 0, c 102, d 0\n\n**Fixtures:**\n- **ark-ui:** 2 components.\n  - Rows: median 174.5 → 37; p95 313 → 37; total 349 → 74\n  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 0\n  - Hidden: a 276, nothing in b, c or d\n- **react-resizable-panels:** 1 component.\n  - Rows: median 288 → 14; total 288 → 14\n  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 1\n  - Hidden: a 274, nothing in b, c or d\n- **chakra (vendored styled-system):** 8 components.\n  - Rows: median 863.5 → 864.5; p95 884 → 885; total 6,943 → 6,951\n  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 0\n  - Hidden: none (the project source is not narrowed)\n- **The 16 other fixture libraries:** ariakit, base-ui, blueprint, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, mantine, mui, panda, radix, rdt-compat, react-aria, react-final-form, shadcn, storybook-emotion, tanstack-table and antd, with 1 to 12 components each.\n  - Rows change by 0 to +3 per component.\n  - Grew >30: 0; fell >90%: 0\n  - Hidden: none\n- **zendesk-garden:** no component matched in both runs.\n\n**What the class (c) numbers contain:**\n- **shadcn (34):**\n  - The aria `Item` (`registry/bases/aria/ui/item.tsx`): 8 members (onBlur, onFocus, onKeyDown, onKeyUp, autoFocus, onClick, slot, style). They come from 1 to 3-member React Aria interfaces (`FocusEvents`, `KeyboardEvents`, `PressEvents`, `FocusableProps` in `@react-types/shared/src/events.d.ts`; `SlotProps`, `StyleRenderProps` in react-aria-components `utils.d.ts`). They are hidden on main too, so they break the \"API source in full\" rule rather than being a 490 regression.\n  - `excludeFromTabOrder` ×26.\n- **Spectrum (102):**\n  - `excludeFromTabOrder` ×55\n  - `routerOptions` ×47\n- **Where they are declared:** `excludeFromTabOrder` and `routerOptions` are not DOM attributes. They are React Aria API declared in `@react-types/shared/src/dom.d.ts` (`FocusableDOMProps`, `LinkDOMProps`), and that file is ambient by path. They were rows on main and are hidden by 490.\n- **Total:** 136 component rows across 10 distinct names.\n- **Debatable, counted in (a):** `id`, `aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`, `aria-describedby` and `aria-details` in React Aria's `DOMProps` and `AriaLabelingProps`. They are documented Spectrum API that happen to be DOM-named. 4,584 component rows on Spectrum and 515 on shadcn are hidden.\n\n**Top 15 hidden names per library** (count; source and its member count in brackets):\n- **shadcn:** lang 182, hidden 178, inert 178, translate 178, dir 174 (GlobalDOMAttributes [5], dom.d.ts); aria-describedby 149, aria-details 149, aria-labelledby 149, aria-label 146 (@types/react AriaAttributes [53]); onClick 139 (GlobalDOMEvents [64]); id 121 (DOMProps [1], dom.d.ts); rel 92 (HTMLAttributes [55]); aria-errormessage 83, aria-modal 79 (AriaAttributes); onTransitionCancel 79 (DOMAttributes [170]).\n- **antd:** aria-label 26, aria-labelledby 25, then 13 more AriaAttributes at 23 each (aria-setsize, aria-rowcount, aria-grabbed, aria-posinset, aria-multiselectable, aria-autocomplete, aria-required, aria-colindextext, aria-checked, aria-keyshortcuts, aria-valuemax, aria-valuemin, aria-valuetext), all @types/react [53].\n- **Spectrum:** id 868 (DOMProps [1]); aria-details 867, aria-describedby 866, aria-labelledby 847, aria-label 815 (AriaLabelingProps [4], dom.d.ts); then GlobalDOMEvents [64] at 223 each: onAnimationEnd, onMouseLeave, onTransitionCancelCapture, onMouseOverCapture, onScrollCapture, onMouseUp, onTouchEnd, onTransitionRunCapture, onTransitionStart, onPointerEnter.\n- **Mantine:** ref 11 (RefAttributes [1], @types/react); then @types/react members at 2 each: onAnimationEndCapture, onSubmitCapture, about, onLoadedData, onDragEndCapture, title, aria-orientation, onAnimationIterationCapture, onTransitionRunCapture, unselectable, onTouchCancel, onTouchMove, prefix, onFocus.\n- **Chakra:** @types/react DOM, ARIA and event members, 9 each: onTransitionCancel, aria-describedby, onLostPointerCapture, onLoadedData, onTransitionCancelCapture, aria-errormessage, part, onBeforeInputCapture, popoverTargetAction, onGotPointerCapture, onKeyDown, onScrollEnd, onTransitionStart, aria-valuemax, onDrop.\n- **ark-ui and react-resizable-panels fixtures:** all @types/react DOMAttributes, AriaAttributes and HTMLAttributes (onStalled, aria-live, defaultChecked…).\n- **Real-API names among them**, for the lead to eyeball:\n  - `excludeFromTabOrder`, `routerOptions` (certain)\n  - `id` and the four `aria-*` labelling props on React Aria and Spectrum (documented)\n  - `ref` on Mantine (debatable)\n- **Generated noise (b) that is listed, not hidden:** Chakra's own repo `Button` has 147 rows, of which 104 are `_*` conditions and 26 are breakpoints (`2xl`, `mdDown`…): only 17 are real API. The chakra fixture has about 864 rows. Cause: \"only sources outside the project are narrowed\", so the generated rule never applies to an in-repo style system.\n\n## Per pattern (all libraries)\n\nPatterns were assigned heuristically from `detectedBy`, the exports and a regex over the component's file. They are approximate. Each entry gives the component count, rows main → 490 as median, p95 and fell >90%, the hidden members, two examples, and a verdict.\n\n- **Own props type only:** 674 components.\n  - Rows: median 2 → 2; p95 25 → 25; fell >90%: 0. Hidden: 0.\n  - Examples: blueprint `Column` 7 → 7 (cellRenderer, className, …); day-picker `DayPicker` 68 → 68.\n  - Verdict: **works.**\n- **DOM-spread wrapper:** 1,397 components.\n  - Rows: median 2 → 3; p95 280 → 27; fell >90%: 82. Hidden: 26,231.\n  - Examples: shadcn `ChartLegend` 500 → 176, keeping align, content, formatter, iconType… and hiding SVG attributes (accentHeight…); a Spectrum icon `ForwardRef` 488 → 0, hiding only SVG attributes.\n  - Verdict: **works.** The noise removed is DOM or SVG.\n- **Polymorphic `as`:** 547 components.\n  - Rows: median 139 → 139; p95 152 → 151; fell >90%: 0. Hidden: 564.\n  - Examples: Chakra `ArkEditableTextarea` 429 → 140, still listing `2xl`, `_active`, `_after`…; headlessui `Listbox` 14 → 14.\n  - Verdict: **works with caveat.** The generated rule is not applied to project sources.\n- **forwardRef or memo wrapper:** 115 components.\n  - Rows: median 16 → 14; p95 116 → 56; fell >90%: 7. Hidden: 2,133.\n  - Examples: antd `OTPInput` 328 → 29, keeping addonAfter, allowClear, count…; Spectrum `CarouselNavButton` 114 → 39, hiding aria-label, id and `excludeFromTabOrder`.\n  - Verdict: **works with caveat** (SharedDom API; Mantine `ref`).\n- **Compound or namespace component:** 25 components.\n  - Rows: median 28 → 27; p95 306 → 90; fell >90%: 1. Hidden: 1,014.\n  - Examples: antd `Input.Password` 329 → 29, keeping action, addonAfter, allowClear…; base-ui `MenuRoot` 15 → 15.\n  - Verdict: **works.**\n- **Hook-driven (`useX(props)`):** 1,028 components, 1,019 of them Spectrum.\n  - Rows: median 11 → 6; p95 103 → 58; fell >90%: 50. Hidden: 16,809.\n  - Examples: Spectrum `Input` 313 → 8 (UNSAFE_className, placeholder, styles…); ariakit `MenuProvider` 7 → 7.\n  - Verdict: **works with caveat, and it is the worst pattern.** Props handed to a hook promote nothing, so the API in SharedDom stays hidden.\n- **Factory-built:** 71 components.\n  - Rows: median 100 → 79; p95 143 → 143; fell >90%: 10. Hidden: 1,629.\n  - Examples: react-aria-components `Tab` 100 → 19, hiding aria-label, href, download and routerOptions (`LinkDOMProps`); antd `Calendar` 25 → 24, hiding `ref`.\n  - Verdict: **works with caveat** (SharedDom; Chakra factories still list conditions).\n- **Generic or conditional props:** 62 components.\n  - Rows: median 68.5 → 31.5; p95 313 → 122; fell >90%: 5. Hidden: 2,809.\n  - Examples: antd `InternalInputNumber` 333 → 39, keeping changeOnWheel, controls…; shadcn `Accordion` 287 → 10, keeping collapsible, onValueChange, orientation…\n  - Verdict: **works** (and the union probe passes).\n- **Re-exporting a dependency component:** 0 components detected.\n  - Verdict: **not measured.** My heuristic found none, so this pattern is unverified.\n- **Other** (unclassified): 680 components.\n  - Rows: median 12 → 9; p95 279 → 87; fell >90%: 36. Hidden: 13,526.\n  - Examples: shadcn `Input` 314 → 12, keeping placeholder, render…; Spectrum `Add` icon 489 → 2.\n  - Verdict: not judged as a pattern.\n\n## Failure-mode probes\n\nThe probe project is `oracle-run/pattern-eval/probes` (`src/probes*.tsx`, `src/anon.tsx`, a fake dependency `node_modules/fake-lib`, and @types/react linked from the repo). I ran both binaries, checker and `--no-checker`. **PR 490's two lanes agree on every probe.** Main's two lanes disagree: the checker lane lists 1 row and the structural lane 279 on the same DOM-spread components. Unless a line says otherwise, the output quoted is PR 490's, identical in both lanes.\n\n- **(i) Reads in nested code — PASS.** The DOM props read in a handler, a `useEffect`, a template literal and a nested function (title, tabIndex, lang, dir, plus a direct `hidden`) are all listed; the other 273 members stay a layer.\n  - `P1Closures`: rows 6, `['dir','hidden','lang','tabIndex','title']`.\n- **(ii) Rest spread onto a component vs onto a DOM tag — PASS.**\n  - `{own2, ...rest}` → `<Inner {...rest}/>`, where `Inner` destructures `title` and `onFocus`: rows `onFocus`, `title`.\n  - The same onto `<div {...rest}/>`: no DOM rows.\n  - Onto the dependency `FakeButton` (Big40 & button attributes): all 40 `api*` listed and no DOM members, correctly.\n- **(iii) Bracket and alias access — PARTIAL FAIL.**\n  - `props['title']`: listed.\n  - `const p = props; p.lang`: **not listed** (`Q2AliasMemberNoSpread`: 0 rows).\n  - `const p = props; const {title} = p` with no spread: **55 rows**, the whole `@types/react` `HTMLAttributes` interface (about, accessKey, autoCapitalize…) instead of 1. The same code with `{...props}` added gives 0 rows. Alias handling is unsound in both directions.\n- **(iv) Default-exported anonymous arrow — PASS.** `Anon`: rows `own4`, `title`.\n- **(v) A body read of a member of a >200-member source — FAIL.**\n  - A project interface of 210 members: `props.loc5` is read, yet loc5 stays in layer `HugeLocalProps` (210) with rows 1. It is the same on main.\n  - A dependency interface of 210: `props.big5` is not listed either.\n  - Collapsed or large layers are never promoted by reads, which contradicts \"a member from any source the body reads\".\n- **(vi) A 40-member API in one dependency interface — PASS, with one FAIL.**\n  - `extends`, the bare type, `Partial`, `Required` and `Omit`: all 40 (or 39) listed.\n  - **FAIL:** a homomorphic mapped copy `{ [K in keyof Big40Props]?: boolean }` gives rows 1 (`api0`, read) and a layer `Big40Props` of 39. Main listed 40. The mapped-over-more-than-30-keys rule hides real API that has the same shape as Chakra's `Conditions`.\n- **(vii) Discriminated union & DOM — PASS.** Rows `alpha`, `beta`, `kind`, `title` (title is read in one branch).\n- **(viii) A wrapper that renames props — PASS.** `{label, press, lang: language, ...rest}` → rows label, lang, press. The renamed DOM destructure is listed.\n- **Extra (ix): members of small dependency API interfaces that @types/react also declares — FAIL.** This is the shape of the shadcn aria `Item`.\n  - Props: `FocusEventsApi`(onFocus, onBlur) & `SlotApi`(slot) & `HTMLAttributes`, with a DOM spread.\n  - Rows 0; layers `FocusEventsApi` 2/2 and `SlotApi` 1/1.\n  - The 1 to 2-member API sources are hidden, against rule 2.\n- **Extra: forwardRef + memo — PASS.** Rows `ref`, `title`.\n- **Extra: hook-driven — by design.** `useThing(props)` gives rows 1 (own only), so nothing is promoted.\n\n## Verdict per pattern\n\n- **Works:** own props only; DOM-spread wrapper; compound/namespace; generic or conditional (and unions).\n- **Works with caveat:**\n  - polymorphic `as`, and factory-built in an in-repo style system: generated noise is still listed;\n  - forwardRef/memo: SharedDom API and `ref` are hidden;\n  - factory-built: SharedDom API is hidden.\n- **Works with caveat, and the worst:** hook-driven. Spectrum's 1,019 components lose `id`, `aria-label*`, `excludeFromTabOrder` and `routerOptions`.\n- **Broken (probe-level, no corpus instance found):**\n  - reads into large or collapsed sources;\n  - mapped copies of a real API of more than 30 keys;\n  - one-hop props aliases.\n- **Not measured:** re-exported dependency components.\n\n## Proposed rule-level changes\n\n1. **Ambient by declaring interface, not by file.** Under `@react-types/shared/src/dom.d.ts`, only `GlobalDOMAttributes` and `GlobalDOMEvents` (and similar pure-DOM interfaces) should be ambient. Alternatively: ambient means declared by React's or the DOM lib's types, and an interface a library re-declares stays an API source when it is at most 200 members.\n   - Effect: restores `excludeFromTabOrder` and `routerOptions` (136 component rows) and the documented `id` and `aria-label*` (about 5.1k component rows, about +4 to 5 rows per Spectrum component). The 64-member event lists stay hidden.\n2. **A member is ambient only when every one of its declarations is ambient.**\n   - Effect: fixes probe (ix) and the shadcn aria `Item` (8 rows). DOM-only members are unchanged.\n3. **Apply \"generated\" (more than 200 members, or a mapped copy of large keys) to project sources too.** Keep \"a project source of at most 200 members is listed\".\n   - Effect: Chakra's own repo `Button` goes from 147 to about 17 rows, and the chakra fixture from about 864 to tens. That fixes the polymorphic and factory caveat for in-repo design systems.\n4. **Reads promote from layers.** A read, destructure or pass of a name that sits in a collapsed or >200-member layer of the same binding becomes a row (the per-component name lists already carry the names).\n   - Effect: fixes probe (v), and keeps a recipe wrapper's `props.colorPalette` as a row.\n5. **Mapped rule by the key interface's nature, not only its size.** Hide a mapped copy only when its key interface is itself generated or ambient (more than 200 members, collapsed, or ambient), or is a selector or token table (all members literal-string or non-callable values; this needs validating on `Conditions`).\n   - Effect: fixes probe (vi-mapped). Whether `Conditions` (130 keys) is still caught must be checked first: as written, a size-only rule at 200 would not catch it.\n6. **Follow one-hop aliases of the props binding** (`const p = props`) as the props binding, and fix the over-promotion. An aliased destructure with no spread lists the whole 55-member `HTMLAttributes`.\n   - Effect: fixes probe (iii).\n7. **Hook hand-off as forwarding.** Treat `useX(props)`, where the callee's parameter type resolves, like a spread onto a resolved component: the members the parameter type declares from non-ambient sources count as used.\n   - Effect: after change 1, React Aria and Spectrum hook-driven components keep their API members without any per-component fixes.\n\n## Not run or not verified\n\n- I did not rebuild either binary. Main is identified by its build time (6 minutes after de016f69), and PR 490 by its worktree and build time (2 minutes after d884334e).\n- PR 490's corpus runs were reused from `list-main-props/runs`, not re-run.\n- The 13 non-corpus fixture libraries are vendored files whose dependencies mostly do not resolve. Their dependency-sourced patterns (Radix, MUI, ariakit generics…) are under-tested, and zendesk-garden matched no component.\n- No large corpora were fetched (MUI, Radix, ariakit, ark-ui, base-ui, blueprint, fluentui, headlessui and panda as real installs).\n- Pattern buckets are regex heuristics. Re-exported dependency components were not detected (0).\n- The SharedDom split into API-named and DOM-named members is by interface name (`DOMProps`, `AriaLabelingProps`, `FocusableDOMProps`, `LinkDOMProps`…).\n- I did not root-cause the 55-row over-promotion in probe (iii).\n- No Storybook rendering was checked, and no oracle was run.\n","numLines":228,"startLine":1,"totalLines":228}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"603f3223-0805-4b37-96b4-457fc8721d58","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
