{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","prNumber":490,"prUrl":"https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/490","prRepository":"orin-dx/caliper","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:09:50.833Z"}
{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","bridgeSessionId":"cse_013R2ytvK9B32ZaSUaSe6aAZ","lastSequenceNum":15975,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"7d843298-0194-4a7a-9276-ea379685b42d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7DMEepy5tTRpQKDUhPd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The rule works for the common patterns and removes a lot of noise, but it isn't pattern-complete. The evaluation found five rule-level gaps, and four of them hide real API props. It covered the five corpora and 19 vendored fixture libraries. MUI, Radix and the other large libraries weren't real installs, so their patterns are under-tested. The report is at `~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval.md`.\n\n**What works**\n- Own-props-only components are unchanged: 674 components, 0 hidden.\n- DOM-spread wrappers, compound components and generic or union props work.\n- Both lanes agree on every probe. On `main` they disagreed (the checker lane gave 1 row where the structural lane gave 279).\n- No component grew by more than 30 rows. The medians barely move (Chakra 139 → 139, Mantine 72 → 72), and the p95 falls sharply on antd, shadcn and Spectrum.\n\n**Where it hides real API, by pattern**\n\n| Pattern | Problem | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Ambient decided by file path | React Aria's own API interfaces live in `@react-types/shared/src/dom.d.ts`, so they count as DOM | `excludeFromTabOrder`, `routerOptions` hidden on 136 component rows. Documented `id` and `aria-label*` hidden on about 5.1k rows (Spectrum, shadcn aria). |\n| Hook-driven `useX(props)` | Props handed to a hook count as no evidence, so nothing is promoted. This is the worst pattern. | About 1,019 Spectrum components. |\n| Members that `@types/react` also declares | A member is hidden even when a small API interface declares it too | shadcn aria `Item` loses `onFocus`, `onBlur`, `slot` and more (hidden on `main` too, so not a regression). |\n| In-repo style systems | The \"generated\" rule applies only to sources outside the project | Chakra's own repo `Button` still shows 147 rows, 130 of them `_*` conditions and breakpoints. Only 17 are real API. |\n| Reads into large sources | A prop the body reads from a source over 200 members stays hidden | Probe failure, also on `main`. No corpus instance found. |\n| Mapped copy of a real API over 30 keys | Treated as generated noise | Probe failure. No corpus instance found. |\n| Props aliases | `const p = props; p.lang` isn't followed. `const {title} = p` with no spread lists all 55 `HTMLAttributes` members. | Probe failure in both directions. |\n\n**Proposed rule-level fixes, not per-component**\n1. **Decide ambient by the declaring interface, not by file.** Only the pure DOM interfaces in `dom.d.ts` count. This restores the 136 `excludeFromTabOrder` and `routerOptions` rows and the documented `id` and `aria-label*` rows.\n2. **A member is ambient only when every declaration of it is ambient.** This fixes the shadcn aria `Item` shape.\n3. **Apply \"generated\" to project sources too.** A project source of 200 members or fewer stays listed. This takes Chakra's own `Button` from 147 to about 17 rows.\n4. **Reads promote members from collapsed or large layers.** This also keeps a recipe wrapper's `props.colorPalette` as a row.\n5. **Hide a mapped copy only when its key interface is itself generated, ambient or a token table.** This needs validating on `Conditions` first, since a size-only rule at 200 wouldn't catch its 130 keys.\n6. **Follow one-hop aliases of the props binding** and fix the over-promotion.\n7. **Treat a hook hand-off as forwarding** when the callee's parameter type resolves.\n\n**Not covered:** re-exported dependency components (the heuristic found none), Storybook rendering, and any oracle run. I'd also want a real MUI and Radix install before calling the patterns complete.\n\nI'd do all seven, with changes 1, 2 and 3 first, since those restore real API props and remove the generated noise on in-repo design systems. Changes 4 to 7 are the probe failures. Want me to start the worker on #490 with those seven?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13055,"cache_read_input_tokens":923887,"output_tokens":1416,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13055,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1416,"cache_read_input_tokens":923887,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13055,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13055},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"3ba369c0-0db1-41bc-a5c3-1b853ae7adff","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch7DMEQgs49H2xLbWrNBz","requestRef":"fb608591-0593-4e19-9254-3ab2f0dc09e1","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8a1219bc-1c01-4792-8365-14ff1d865866","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:10:00.522Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
