` (id), `AriaLabelingProps`, `FocusableDOMProps` (excludeFromTabOrder), `LinkDOMProps` (routerOptions)) are API sources when at most 200 members: define precisely and by structure (e.g. ambient = declared by React's or the DOM lib's types, or an interface whose members are all native DOM attribute/event names per the DOM/React typings themselves; derive the set from the typings, not a hand-written name list; if you must use a rule on the declaring file, justify and test it), and update crates/core/src/types/ambient.rs / `Origin` / `declaration_origin` accordingly; (2) A member is ambient only when EVERY one of its declarations is ambient (probe ix: `onFocus` declared by a small API interface AND by @types/react `DOMAttributes`; the shadcn aria `Item`); (3) apply the 'generated' rule (a source over 200 members, or a mapped copy of `keyof` a large key set) to PROJECT sources too, while a project source of at most 200 members stays listed (Chakra's own repo Button 147 rows -> about 17; the chakra fixture ~864 -> tens). STEP 2 (commit after Step 1 is green): (4) reads/destructures/passes of a name that sits in a collapsed or more-than-200-member layer of the same props binding promote it to a row (probe v; keep a recipe wrapper's `props.colorPalette`); (5) the mapped-copy rule by the key interface's NATURE: hide a mapped copy only when its key interface is itself generated or ambient (over 200 members, collapsed, ambient) or is a selector/token table (all members string-literal or non-callable values: validate on Chakra `Conditions` (130 keys): if a size-only 200 threshold does not catch Conditions, find the structural signal that does, e.g. every member's type is the same style-object type, and prove it on the corpus; a real 40-key API mapped copy (probe vi) must be listed; (6) follow one-hop aliases of the props binding (`const p = props; p.lang`; `const {title} = p`) as the props binding itself, and fix the over-promotion that lists the whole 55-member `HTMLAttributes` for an aliased destructure with no spread (root-cause it: the pattern-eval report did not); the alias analysis must stay an allow-list: anything not proven is `handed_on`/unknown, per the extractor rules (the T1 body facts in crates/core/src/extractor/body_facts.rs use oxc_semantic symbols: alias = a `const`/`let` initialised with the props identifier, never reassigned); (7) treat `useX(props)` hand-offs as forwarding when the callee's parameter type resolves (like a spread onto a resolved component, T3 forwarding in crates/core/src/relevance/forwarding.rs): the members that parameter type declares from non-ambient sources count as used; unresolved callee = unknown. ACCEPTANCE (re-measure with the evaluation harness in /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval/ (run.sh, eval.py, mixed.py, probes/ with run.sh and show.py): copy and adapt in scratch; do not commit it): (a) real-API rows hidden by mistake: 136 -> 0 on the corpora + fixtures (excludeFromTabOrder, routerOptions, the documented id/aria-label* on React Aria/Spectrum, the shadcn aria Item members); report class (c) counts per library before/after; (b) Spectrum and shadcn rows: report median/p95/total before/after (today Spectrum 11 -> 6 median, 52,011 -> 18,739 total): they will rise by about 4-5 rows per Spectrum component: report it and that no median exceeds a sensible bound (say Spectrum median <= 12); (c) Chakra's own repo Button ~17 rows, Chakra corpus median not above 139; (d) all probes (i)-(ix) PASS in BOTH lanes (checker and --no-checker) and add each probe as a regression test (relevance_model.rs / a new small test file next to it; model-based where it generates components); (e) the main-props differential (0 violations) from the previous round, re-run, and the demo sb-demo Button rows (20 today: as, asChild, css, extra, fresh, html*, kind, loading, loadingText, recipe, size, spinner, spinnerPlacement, tone, unstyled, variant) must not lose any and must not gain any of the 286/706/130 noise; (f) peak RSS shadcn/Chakra within 3% of PR 490's current (975 / 1,819 MiB); (g) CLI JSON still carries the layer names: no information lost. Pre-push gate: invariants in the PR note (unknown unless proven; by binding not spelling; every read recorded; one owner; wired or not defined), grammar sweep over the source/provenance/alias forms (interface, intersection, mapped-over-keyof, Pick/Omit, alias, generic instantiation, ComponentProps<'el'>, forwardRef/memo, factory, hook hand-off, alias chains, shadowing, reassignment), mutation proofs per new rule, ADR 0028 A2 amended via the adr skill (new ambient definition, project-source generated rule, layer promotion, alias and hook forwarding) and the changeset `list-props-by-usage` updated in the user-focused convention of AGENTS.md, `/code-review medium` on your explicit SHA range AWAITED with one fix round. Gates: `just lint doc-check machete typos`, `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` (run `pnpm install --offline --ignore-scripts --frozen-lockfile` first), `just test-checker-lane` (symlink target/release in the worktree to your CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release), `just test-ts`, `just semver`. NOT in scope: the Storybook browser check and the antd/shadcn oracle run (the lead does them after). Own CARGO_TARGET_DIR under /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/shrink/, rust 1.99.1 first on PATH (/Users/gabe/.rustup/toolchains/1.99.1-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin). Cap 130 tool calls; if you run out, stop at a green commit (Step 1 alone is a valid stopping point) and list what remains. Update /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/pr/feat-list-props-by-usage.md with the new rule and before/after tables (replace obsolete claims). Final message at most 100 words: SHA, which steps are done, the acceptance numbers (a) to (g), gates exit codes, what remains."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_toke