e by PROVENANCE and STRUCTURE, never by name lists; this is about patterns, not one-off components; 'produce the best results, not the overwhelming numbers'. STEP 1 (highest value, do first, commit): (1) Ambient by DECLARING INTERFACE, not by file: under `@react-types/shared/src/dom.d.ts` only the pure-DOM interfaces (`GlobalDOMAttributes`, `GlobalDOMEvents` and similar) are ambient; React Aria API interfaces declared in the same file (`DOMProps` (id), `AriaLabelingProps`, `FocusableDOMProps` (excludeFromTabOrder), `LinkDOMProps` (routerOptions)) are API sources when at most 200 members: define precisely and by structure (e.g. ambient = declared by React's or the DOM lib's types, or an interface whose members are all native DOM attribute/event names per the DOM/React typings themselves; derive the set from the typings, not a hand-written name list; if you must use a rule on the declaring file, justify and test it), and update crates/core/src/types/ambient.rs / `Origin` / `declaration_origin` accordingly; (2) A member is ambient only when EVERY one of its declarations is ambient (probe ix: `onFocus` declared by a small API interface AND by @types/react `DOMAttributes`; the shadcn aria `Item`); (3) apply the 'generated' rule (a source over 200 members, or a mapped copy of `keyof` a large key set) to PROJECT sources too, while a project source of at most 200 members stays listed (Chakra's own repo Button 147 rows -> about 17; the chakra fixture ~864 -> tens). STEP 2 (commit after Step 1 is green): (4) reads/destructures/passes of a name that sits in a collapsed or more-than-200-member layer of the same props binding promote it to a row (probe v; keep a recipe wrapper's `props.colorPalette`); (5) the mapped-copy rule by the key interface's NATURE: hide a mapped copy only when its key interface is itself generated or ambient (over 200 members, collapsed, ambient) or is a selector/token table (all members string-literal or non-callable values: validate on Chakra `Conditio