{"parentUuid":"5685e81d-4c16-4bb8-b512-9a7300f9d733","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Jv4bqahsxVv4Y2tyKQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Phase 1 has started. A worker (Opus, 130 calls) is making the seven rule-level changes on #490's branch, in two commit groups, and it won't push.\n\n**Step 1 comes first and is a valid stopping point on its own:**\n- Ambient decided by declaring interface, so React Aria's `excludeFromTabOrder`, `routerOptions` and documented `id` and `aria-label*` stop being treated as DOM.\n- A member is ambient only when every one of its declarations is.\n- The \"generated\" rule applies to project sources too, so Chakra's own-repo `Button` drops from 147 to about 17 rows.\n\n**Step 2:** reads promote members from large layers, the mapped-copy rule decided by the key interface's nature, one-hop alias following, and hook hand-offs treated as forwarding.\n\n**What I asked it to prove, with the evaluation harness**\n- Real-API rows hidden by mistake go from 136 to 0.\n- Spectrum's medians rise by about 4–5 rows per component, with no median above a sensible bound.\n- All the probes pass in both lanes, and each becomes a regression test.\n- The demo `Button` keeps its 20 rows and gains none of the 286, 706 or 130 noise members.\n- Memory stays within 3% of #490's current numbers.\n- It follows the pre-push gate, amends ADR 0028 and the changeset, and awaits `/code-review medium`.\n\n**Left for me afterwards:** the Storybook browser check, the antd and shadcn oracle run, and the memory check. I'll do those once it reports. In the meantime #491 and #489 are unaffected, and I'll check their CI and findings while I wait."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6887,"cache_read_input_tokens":940157,"output_tokens":557,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool