{"parentUuid":"9a121800-166b-4504-8bb9-2473809ea87e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KKGox3BrDeXNHaqCzY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LWNB8Hf2bxEKUvRsgumjGK","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Reusable listing acceptance run: Storybook rows, CLI rows, oracle on antd/shadcn","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"Build ONE reusable acceptance command and run it as a BASELINE; do not change repo files, do not push. Purpose: PR 490 (`origin/feat/list-props-by-usage`) is being reworked by another worker, and when it lands we must verify, in one command and without ceremony, that the Storybook Controls rows and the CLI rows are right and that the oracle does not regress. Read /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/worker-contract.md, /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/REPORT.md (Storybook dev-mode section), /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval.md and the scratch in /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/ (sb-demo/serve.sh, setup-stories.sh, first-second.sh, run-weekly.sh, counts.py, pattern-eval/eval.py, probes/). Deliverable: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/accept/accept.sh (+ helpers in the same dir): `accept.sh <caliper-docgen binary> <packages/storybook dir + napi build> <label>` that (1) CLI rows: runs `extract --json --quiet --no-cache --load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies` on the sb-demo (Button, Badge, Card, Input, Menu, Tabs components) and the five corpora (chakra-only, gate-large, mantine, antd, shadcn, spectrum; reuse oracle-run/work or corpora paths), decodes the interned JSON (write a small robust decoder: `props` / `propSets` / `nameLists` hash tables; verify it by checking a component's decoded row count equals the count in `--format rdt`'s props for the same component) and writes per component the row names, the layer names with sizes and `used`, and per corpus median/p95/total rows; (2) Storybook dev mode: starts the sb-demo dev server with the given addon/napi (see sb-demo/serve.sh; ports must be free: pick a free one and kill the server at the end), drives a real browser with the Playwright MCP tools (load with ToolSearch `select:mcp__playwright__browser_navigate,mcp__playwright__browser_evaluate,mcp__playwright__browser_wait_for,mcp__playwright__browser_close`; if MCP tools are unavailable to you, fall back to the npm `playwright` package under oracle-run/sb-demo if installed) and records, for Button, Badge, Card, Input: the rows in the Controls table (names), their count, time to structural and time to checker answer; asserts that Controls rows equal the CLI rows (+ `children`, which Storybook adds from args) and prints diffs; (3) oracle: `scripts/weekly.py --bin <binary> --oracle --corpus antd --corpus shadcn --corpora <dir> --work <dir> --runs 1 --out <file>` (see its usage; authorised, small) and prints the headline per corpus and compares with the baseline numbers (shadcn 98.7% correct / 0 wrong, antd 93.0% / 1 wrong); (4) a one-screen summary `accept-<label>.md` with pass/fail per check. Then run it with label `baseline-d884334e` using a binary built from the PR 490 head d884334e (reuse /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/shrink/list-main-props/target/release/caliper-docgen if present: check its build matches `git log` of the branch; the napi/addon build from the same worktree if present (find with `ls /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/` and shrink dirs); if none exists build into your own CARGO_TARGET_DIR under /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/accept/ with rust 1.99.1 first on PATH /Users/gabe/.rustup/toolchains/1.99.1-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin). Report any acceptance failure on the baseline plainly (e.g. Storybook rows differing from the CLI rows). The machine is shared (other workers build): do not report timings as official. Cap 60 tool calls; run long commands in the background and poll. Final message at most 70 words: the command, baseline pass/fail per check, Button/Badge Storybook rows, oracle headline."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":649,"cache_read_input_tokens":947044,"output_tokens":7694,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1163},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":649,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7694,"cache_read_input_tokens":947044,"cache_creation_input_tokens":649,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":649},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LWNB8Hf2bxEKUvRsgumjGK":{"description":"Reusable listing acceptance run: Storybook rows, CLI rows, oracle on antd/shadcn","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"Build ONE reusable acceptance command and run it as a BASELINE; do not change repo files, do not push. Purpose: PR 490 (`origin/feat/list-props-by-usage`) is being reworked by another worker, and when it lands we must verify, in one command and without ceremony, that the Storybook Controls rows and the CLI rows are right and that the oracle does not regress. Read /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/worker-contract.md, /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/REPORT.md (Storybook dev-mode section), /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval.md and the scratch in /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/ (sb-demo/serve.sh, setup-stories.sh, first-second.sh, run-weekly.sh, counts.py, pattern-eval/eval.py, probes/). Deliverable: /Users/gabe/Projec