erage = judged / total, and gate on both (the existing gate on wrong props stays; add a documented floor on coverage only if the data supports one: look at the stored records and the reports; if not, report it without a gate and say so). In headline.py keep the old fields so earlier records compare; bump UNIVERSE_VERSION or REFERENCE_VERSION only if the meaning of a stored field changes (see their comments), and say why. (3) the weekly's recall vs RDT counts `@types/react` props as 'recalled' by listed props, but with the checker on the whole-project merge keeps React's props in the element layer (and with PR 490 the layer carries the names): measured recall of `@types/react` props is 0.4% (Mantine), about 0% (Chakra), 4.9% (shadcn), 23.9% (antd), 86.8% (Spectrum) versus 99% on 0.10.0 (no checker). Count a React prop as recalled when it is listed OR named in an inheritance layer's members (the JSON carries `nameLists`; look at how recall reads `own_layers`/`react_layers` in weekly.py: the record already has `react_layers`), and report both the listed and the layered recall so the column measures information kept, not rows. Check docs/measurement.md's description of the column and update it. (4) the CI weekly of 2026-11-15 died with exit 143 on 'chakra: Caliper' (a kill; memory on 0.11.0); with the memory fixes in main this should pass: add nothing for it, but make sure STEP_TIMEOUT/failed handling reports a signal death clearly (read the code; fix only if unclear). Tests first: scripts/test_weekly.py / test_headline.py cases for each change (python3 -I -m unittest or the project's runner: see the justfile `test-py`), including a record with not_judged > 0 and a record from before (missing fields). Keep changes small and in the existing files. Gates: `just lint doc-check machete typos`, `just test-py`, `just semver` if a changeset is demanded (these are scripts: probably none; check the AGENTS.md changeset rule: only consumer-visible changes). Do NOT run the oracle itself (costs money; the lead runs it). Cap 50 tool calls. Notes to /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/pr/fix-weekly-oracle-measurement.md (## What, ## Evidence, ## Not verified, session URL line). Final message at most 60 words: SHA, exit codes, what the headline shows for a record with Chakra's numbers (16.7% / 75.5% not judged)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":649,"cache_read_input_tokens":947044,"output_tokens":7694,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1163},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":649,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7694,"cache_read_input_tokens":947044,"cache_creation_input_tokens":649,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":649},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QiP6rPNrjgHPKXDbcPiw3L":{"description":"Weekly oracle: Chakra heap, report not-judged separately, fix the recall metric","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"Fix the weekly record's measurement problems found by the 2026-11-15 oracle run. Start from `origin/main` (`git fetch origin` first; if blocked use existing refs); branch `fix/weekly-oracle-measurement`; commit locally; I push and open the PR. Read /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/worker-contract.md (incl. 'no new scripts/options/recipes unless wired into CI/weekly'), /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/REPORT.md (Quality and 'What failed' sections), docs/measurement.md, scripts/weekly.py, scripts/headline.py, scripts/oracle_data.py, scripts/test_weekly*.py, scripts/test_headline.py, .github/wor