d, Select, Autocomplete, Dialog, DataGrid-free set, plus the library's own source for `packages/mui-material/src` if the install is feasible; state what you did) and Radix (`radix-ui/primitives`: `packages/react/*/src`; similar). Use `ToolSearch`-free shell: `git clone --depth 1` and `pnpm install --ignore-scripts` (the sandbox may block the network: run with the sandbox disabled only for fetching and installing, using dangerouslyDisableSandbox; do not touch anything outside oracle-run/ and corpora/). If the network or install is impossible, say so and stop with what you have. (2) Run both binaries (main: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/target/release/caliper-docgen; PR 490's d884334e build: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/shrink/list-main-props/target/release/caliper-docgen, or whatever newest build of `origin/feat/list-props-by-usage` exists under shrink/ or oracle-run/accept/; the lead will rerun with the final build, so make it ONE command: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval/run-extra.sh <main-bin> <490-bin>) with `extract --json --quiet --no-cache --load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies` (checker on) on the new corpora, and use eval.py's classification to produce per library: rows main -> 490 (median, p95, total, grew >30, fell >90%), hidden members by class (a DOM/ARIA ambient, b generated, c REAL API hidden by mistake, d other) and the TOP 15 hidden names with declaring source; the pattern buckets (own props, DOM-spread wrapper, polymorphic as/OverridableComponent, forwardRef/memo, compound, hook-driven, factory, generic/conditional); and a list of every class (c) real-API hit with its declaring file. (3) Add to the existing report as a NEW file /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval-mui-radix.md: tables, patterns, the real-API hits, what MUI's `OverridableComponent` and Radix `asChild` components list (show Button, TextField, Select, Dialog.Root/Content and Radix Dialog/Tooltip/Popover/Tabs rows before/after), and whether anything in the 7 proposed rule changes of pattern-eval.md would change for these libraries. Cap 50 tool calls; run long commands in the background and poll. Final message at most 70 words: what was installed, real-API hits (count, names), worst pattern, path."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":649,"cache_read_input_tokens":947044,"output_tokens":7694,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1163},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":649,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7694,"cache_read_input_tokens":947044,"cache_creation_input_tokens":649,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":649},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SDNrQaE9UyUJdVpcfnfVDF":{"description":"Real MUI and Radix corpora for the pattern evaluation","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"Extend the pattern evaluation to real MUI and Radix installs; do not change repo files, do not push. Context: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval.md evaluated PR 490's listing rule (main props in full, what the body uses directly, big generated/ambient sources as layer names) on five installed corpora and 19 vendored fixture libraries, but MUI and Radix (and other big libraries) were never run as real installs, so their patterns (MUI's `OverridableComponent` / `ButtonProps` from `@mui/material` with `OverrideProps`, `styled`, Radix primitives with `asChild` and `React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<typeof Primitive.X>`, forwardRef every