 oracle does not regress. Read /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/worker-contract.md, /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/REPORT.md (Storybook dev-mode section), /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval.md and the scratch in /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/ (sb-demo/serve.sh, setup-stories.sh, first-second.sh, run-weekly.sh, counts.py, pattern-eval/eval.py, probes/). Deliverable: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/accept/accept.sh (+ helpers in the same dir): `accept.sh <caliper-docgen binary> <packages/storybook dir + napi build> <label>` that (1) CLI rows: runs `extract --json --quiet --no-cache --load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies` on the sb-demo (Button, Badge, Card, Input, Menu, Tabs components) and the five corpora (chakra-only, gate-large, mantine, antd, shadcn, spectrum; reuse oracle-run/work or corpora paths), decodes the interned JSON (write a small robust decoder: `props` / `propSets` / `nameLists` hash tables; verify it by checking a component's decoded row count equals the count in `--format rdt`'s props for the same component) and writes per component the row names, the layer names with sizes and `used`, and per corpus median/p95/total rows; (2) Storybook dev mode: starts the sb-demo dev server with the given addon/napi (see sb-demo/serve.sh; ports must be free: pick a free one and kill the server at the end), drives a real browser with the Playwright MCP tools (load with ToolSearch `select:mcp__playwright__browser_navigate,mcp__playwright__browser_evaluate,mcp__playwright__browser_wait_for,mcp__playwright__browser_close`; if MCP tools are unavailable to you, fall back to the npm `playwright` package under oracle-run/sb-demo if installed) and records, for Button, Badge, Card, Input: the rows in the Controls table (names), their count, time to structural and time to checker answer; asserts that Controls rows equal the CLI rows (+ `children`, which Storybook adds from args) and prints diffs; (3) oracle: `scripts/weekly.py --bin <binary> --oracle --corpus antd --corpus shadcn --corpora <dir> --work <dir> --runs 1 --out <file>` (see its usage; authorised, small) and prints the headline per corpus and compares with the baseline numbers (shadcn 98.7% correct / 0 wrong, antd 93.0% / 1 wrong); (4) a one-screen summary `accept-<label>.md` with pass/fail per check. Then run it with label `baseline-d884334e` using a binary built from the PR 490 head d884334e (reuse /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/shrink/list-main-props/target/release/caliper-docgen if present: check its build matches `git log` of the branch; the napi/addon build from the same worktree if present (find with `ls /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/` and shrink dirs); if none exists build into your own CARGO_TARGET_DIR under /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/accept/ with rust 1.99.1 first on PATH /Users/gabe/.rustup/toolchains/1.99.1-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin). Report any acceptance failure on the baseline plainly (e.g. Storybook rows differing from the CLI rows). The machine is shared (other workers build): do not report timings as official. Cap 60 tool calls; run long commands in the background and poll. Final message at most 70 words: the command, baseline pass/fail per check, Button/Badge Storybook rows, oracle headline.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper/ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba/tasks/a8d5d2d85bcab4a5b.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0f13e914-0f37-44fd-aa80-11bcfba661c8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","branch":"mf-t4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibili