/recipes unless wired into CI/weekly'), /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/REPORT.md (Quality and 'What failed' sections), docs/measurement.md, scripts/weekly.py, scripts/headline.py, scripts/oracle_data.py, scripts/test_weekly*.py, scripts/test_headline.py, .github/workflows/weekly.yml, apps/oracle/. Problems to fix: (1) the oracle step runs out of Node heap on Chakra (default ~4 GB: exit 134) and needs `REDACTED` (the rerun passed with it: 620 components, 486,834 props, exit 0); set it where the oracle is spawned (scripts/weekly.py / oracle_data.py, and any CI step), sized by a named constant with a comment on the measured need, and make a memory failure of a step a recorded `failed` entry with the log tail, not a silent absence. (2) the headline reads Chakra 16.7% and Mantine 32.7% correct because 75.5% / 62.9% of props are 'not judged' (0 wrong): the single 'correct %' hides that the oracle did not check most props. Report `not judged` as its own first-class column next to correct / less precise / wrong in the weekly markdown and the issue text, define the headline rate over JUDGED props (correct / (correct + less precise + wrong), with the denominator shown) AND show coverage = judged / total, and gate on both (the existing gate on wrong props stays; add a documented floor on coverage only if the data supports one: look at the stored records and the reports; if not, report it without a gate and say so). In headline.py keep the old fields so earlier records compare; bump UNIVERSE_VERSION or REFERENCE_VERSION only if the meaning of a stored field changes (see their comments), and say why. (3) the weekly's recall vs RDT counts `@types/react` props as 'recalled' by listed props, but with the checker on the whole-project merge keeps React's props in the element layer (and with PR 490 the layer carries the names): measured recall of `@types/react` props is 0.4% (Mantine), about 0% (Chakra), 4.9% (shadcn), 23.9% (antd), 86.8% (Spectrum) versus 99% on 0.10.0 (no checker). Count a React prop as recalled when it is listed OR named in an inheritance layer's members (the JSON carries `nameLists`; look at how recall reads `own_layers`/`react_layers` in weekly.py: the record already has `react_layers`), and report both the listed and the layered recall so the column measures information kept, not rows. Check docs/measurement.md's description of the column and update it. (4) the CI weekly of 2026-11-15 died with exit 143 on 'chakra: Caliper' (a kill; memory on 0.11.0); with the memory fixes in main this should pass: add nothing for it, but make sure STEP_TIMEOUT/failed handling reports a signal death clearly (read the code; fix only if unclear). Tests first: scripts/test_weekly.py / test_headline.py cases for each change (python3 -I -m unittest or the project's runner: see the justfile `test-py`), including a record with not_judged > 0 and a record from before (missing fields). Keep changes small and in the existing files. Gates: `just lint doc-check machete typos`, `just test-py`, `just semver` if a changeset is demanded (these are scripts: probably none; check the AGENTS.md changeset rule: only consumer-visible changes). Do NOT run the oracle itself (costs money; the lead runs it). Cap 50 tool calls. Notes to /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/pr/fix-weekly-oracle-measurement.md (## What, ## Evidence, ## Not verified, session URL line). Final message at most 60 words: SHA, exit codes, what the headline shows for a record with Chakra's numbers (16.7% / 75.5% not judged).","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper/ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba/tasks/a08b05225ee2a65e8.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0f13e914-0f37-44fd-aa80-11bcfba661c8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","branch":"