e memo with 812k hits vs 40k misses, `PropType` trees, session targets). This decides whether the next memory slice (sharing/`Arc`-ing the converter's memo results and cutting oversized types BEFORE expanding them: chakra-memory.md Part C) can reach Chakra under 1 GiB. Read /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/memory-profile.md (phase table, ranked saving #3 and 'Not measured'), /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/shrink/chakra-memory.md and tsrs-replacements.md, docs/type-checker-integration.md (converter on the checker's thread, memo, the ~3,200 requests for Chakra), crates/semantic/src/convert.rs (MAX_SIZE, past_size_budget, the memo), instantiate.rs, checker.rs, heap.rs. Method (scratch only under /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/mem2/; your own CARGO_TARGET_DIR there; rust 1.99.1 first on PATH /Users/gabe/.rustup/toolchains/1.99.1-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin; build from `origin/main`): add to a SCRATCH copy a counting global allocator (a tiny `#[global_allocator]` wrapper over mimalloc counting live bytes per tag, or per thread: the converter runs on the checker's own thread, so thread attribution is not enough: use a thread-local 'current tag' set by RAII guards around (a) the converter's work (`convert.rs` entry points), (b) the converter's memo inserts, (c) tsrs calls (the RPC client calls into the checker), and count live bytes by tag at the d1 marker (all components answered) and at the process peak; also try the cheaper alternative if the allocator is too invasive: measure the process RSS at the d1 marker with the memo cleared/disabled (a scratch env switch that bypasses memo insertion) and with the converter's output dropped immediately (convert then discard), and with the checker's own caches reduced via any tsrs option, to attribute by subtraction. Report: live bytes by tag (tsrs heap, memo, converted trees kept, session/targets, structural data) at d1 and at the peak on Chakra, shadcn and Mantine; the memo: entry count, bytes per entry, average subtree size, the share of memory in the 7 style-system components (about 4,000 requests each), and how many memo values are deep-cloned on hits (812k hits: what does a hit cost: clone of a `PropType` tree?). Then DESIGN the slice: what to change (e.g. `Arc<PropType>` subtrees in the memo, hash-consing, cut oversized types before expansion, lazily convert), the expected saving in MiB per project with the evidence behind it, the public type changes (semver: which pub types are touched; is `PropType` public output? what does the serializer need), the risk to output identity, the work split into at most 3 independent worker slices with files, and a go/no-go: 'Chakra can/cannot get under 1 GiB with this, because tsrs heap alone is X'. Deliverable: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/memory-split.md. Cap 60 tool calls; run long commands in the background and poll. Final message at most 80 words: the split of d1 memory (tsrs vs converter), the achievable Chakra peak, go/no-go, path.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper/ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba/tasks/a667c15e3f4e6d284.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0f13e914-0f37-44fd-aa80-11bcfba661c8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","branch":"mf-t4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.clau