, but MUI and Radix (and other big libraries) were never run as real installs, so their patterns (MUI's `OverridableComponent` / `ButtonProps` from `@mui/material` with `OverrideProps`, `styled`, Radix primitives with `asChild` and `React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<typeof Primitive.X>`, forwardRef everywhere) are under-tested. Read /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/worker-contract.md, pattern-eval.md and its scratch in /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval/ (run.sh, eval.py, mixed.py, probes/), scripts/corpora.py (how corpora are pinned, fetched and installed: the 5 pinned ones; follow its conventions: pinned commit, `INSTALL_NODE_DIR`, caches under .corpora/caches; install under /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/corpora/ like the others, never /tmp, never in the repo), docs/measurement.md. Steps: (1) Fetch and install two more corpora, shallow and pinned: MUI (`mui/material-ui`: the `packages/mui-material/src` tree with its dependencies installed enough for @types/react and @mui/types to resolve; `pnpm install --filter` may be large: prefer a minimal route, e.g. a small consumer project that depends on `@mui/material` and re-exports/wraps its Button, TextField, Select, Autocomplete, Dialog, DataGrid-free set, plus the library's own source for `packages/mui-material/src` if the install is feasible; state what you did) and Radix (`radix-ui/primitives`: `packages/react/*/src`; similar). Use `ToolSearch`-free shell: `git clone --depth 1` and `pnpm install --ignore-scripts` (the sandbox may block the network: run with the sandbox disabled only for fetching and installing, using dangerouslyDisableSandbox; do not touch anything outside oracle-run/ and corpora/). If the network or install is impossible, say so and stop with what you have. (2) Run both binaries (main: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/target/release/caliper-docgen; PR 490's d884334e build: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/shrink/list-main-props/target/release/caliper-docgen, or whatever newest build of `origin/feat/list-props-by-usage` exists under shrink/ or oracle-run/accept/; the lead will rerun with the final build, so make it ONE command: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval/run-extra.sh <main-bin> <490-bin>) with `extract --json --quiet --no-cache --load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies` (checker on) on the new corpora, and use eval.py's classification to produce per library: rows main -> 490 (median, p95, total, grew >30, fell >90%), hidden members by class (a DOM/ARIA ambient, b generated, c REAL API hidden by mistake, d other) and the TOP 15 hidden names with declaring source; the pattern buckets (own props, DOM-spread wrapper, polymorphic as/OverridableComponent, forwardRef/memo, compound, hook-driven, factory, generic/conditional); and a list of every class (c) real-API hit with its declaring file. (3) Add to the existing report as a NEW file /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval-mui-radix.md: tables, patterns, the real-API hits, what MUI's `OverridableComponent` and Radix `asChild` components list (show Button, TextField, Select, Dialog.Root/Content and Radix Dialog/Tooltip/Popover/Tabs rows before/after), and whether anything in the 7 proposed rule changes of pattern-eval.md would change for these libraries. Cap 50 tool calls; run long commands in the background and poll. Final message at most 70 words: what was installed, real-API hits (count, names), worst pattern, path.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper/ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba/tasks/a7d5c66a21e2ce1d3.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0f13e914-0f37-44fd-aa80-11bcfba661c8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","branch":"mf-t4","default_br