{"parentUuid":"52c1088e-14e9-4119-a713-e8d12446613a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KS17apmWZ2VP11u9WZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NZLew5BqrPyDBecWFZS2nF","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ace6850035594237c","summary":"two Entire findings on 490 to fold into your pass","message":"Two open Entire findings on PR 490 (change 288) in the files you are changing; fix them in your pass (with failing tests first) and cite them in the commit messages. (1) crates/core/src/relevance/mod.rs:84-90 (perf, Medium): when a complete body leaves a large collapsed source unused, `apply` passes every member (mod.rs:61-62) and `Vec::contains` rescans the layer per member: a 3,700-member layer = ~6.8M string comparisons per component, repeated when answers are published (pipeline/revision.rs:125-127), even for project sources `add` discards. Fix: index layer membership once (a set built per layer, or iterate layers against a set of wanted names), and skip sources `add` will discard before doing any work; add a test that pins complexity (e.g. a 4,000-member layer with 4,000 wanted names completes in a bounded number of comparisons: count via a counting wrapper or assert on a deterministic structure) and report the time on Chakra's SystemProperties layer before/after. (2) crates/core/src/react_types.rs:452 (correctness, Medium): this also restricts the EXPANDED on-demand view (`collapseInheritedProps: 'none'`): for props expressed as `ReturnType<typeof makeProps>` where `makeProps` returns React attributes, structural resolution produces no props (resolver/chain.rs:255), so it requests an empty React set and the checker then discards every React property (semantic/src/component.rs:161), whereas Full mode previously requested and merged them. Preserve checker discovery when collapse is disabled so the `none` option still returns these props: add a test with that exact shape in both lanes and assert `none` returns the React props (and `dependencies` stays narrowed). These are in addition to your seven changes; do them first (they are small), then continue.","type":"message","recipient":"ace6850035594237c","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Two open Entire findings on PR 490 (change 288) i…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":736,"cache_read_input_tokens":961947,"output_tokens":935,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":220},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":736,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":935,"cache_read_input_tokens":961947,"cache_creation_input_tokens":736,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":736},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NZLew5BqrPyDBecWFZS2nF":{"to":"ace6850035594237c","summary":"two Entire findings on 490 to fold into your pass","message":"Two open Entire findings on PR 490 (change 288) in the files you are changing; fix them in your pass (with failing tests first) and cite them in the commit messages. (1) crates/core/src/relevance/mod.rs:84-90 (perf, Medium): when a complete body leaves a large collapsed source unused, `apply` passes every member (mod.rs:61-62) and `Vec::contains` rescans the layer per member: a 3,700-member layer = ~6.8M string comparisons per component, repeated when answers are published (pipeline/revision.rs:125-127), even for project sources `add` discards. Fix: index layer membership once (a set built per layer, or iterate layers against a set of wanted names), and skip sources `add` will discard before doing any work; add a test that pins complexity (e.g. a 4,000-member layer with 4,000 wanted names completes in a bounded number of comparisons: count via a counting wrapper or assert on a deterministic structure) and report the time on Chakra's SystemProperties layer before/after. (2) crates/core/src/react_types.rs:452 (correctness, Medium): this also restricts the EXPANDED on-demand view (`collapseInheritedProps: 'none'`): for props expressed as `ReturnType<typeof makeProps>` where `makeProps` returns React attributes, structural resolution produces no props (resolver/chain.rs:255), so it requests an empty React set and the checker then discards every React property (semantic/src/component.rs:161), whereas Full mode previously requested and merged them. Preserve checker discovery when collapse is disabled so the `none` option still returns these props: add a test with that exact shape in both lanes and assert `none` returns the React props (and `dependencies` stays narrowed). These are in addition to your seven changes; do them first (they are small), then continue."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3a1b4c77-7327-4c03-bb1d-9b25970305bd","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch7KRznj7fKajfDrGTQW3","requestRef":"fc2c7761-9dc0-4e44-b2be-4f2da5645d7e","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"fcfa911a-bb24-4e48-85fc-0c74cfaf5264","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:29:43.244Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
