{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","id":"b1e11b14-19d8-4611-b857-5f1630fc922d","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:29:43.590Z","version":"2.1.311","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"9803daf85cbe48be5f6ca225f95dc13bf2e5a024e85e5325762dd209c1ad3e02","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"fc2c7761-9dc0-4e44-b2be-4f2da5645d7e","keep":1539,"tail":["ed465b092172a603fac5bebc7bbbc0c1c03fcb25e618efa45abdc24223ac3990","bd8cc8d3ce70217ea995fe583c43409a217725ea01258e4b0eb77a94db2204d1","9e672f737c8f0cb9ef2d69d7b889f682a5168366108db95c1e4e82ba37be477e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1541,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"a1be915599e1d9a446f7077a0e92e2b0906209d8e3fc504f1cb4fce11d927eea"}
{"parentUuid":"a30e83db-a21e-4148-b8f7-c19494cc79ea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KSY4fKRKmAvaC5PFKc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Five workers are now running in parallel, and #489 is already merged. I'm not waiting on anything of my own.\n\n| Worker | Model | What it's doing | Output |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Phase 1** | Opus | The seven rule-level changes on #490, plus the two new Entire findings (below) | A pushable branch |\n| **Acceptance command** | Sonnet | One reusable `accept.sh` that checks CLI rows, the Storybook rows in a real browser, and the antd and shadcn oracle, and runs it now as a baseline on #490's current head | The command and a baseline result |\n| **Weekly oracle fixes** | Sonnet | The Chakra Node heap, \"not judged\" as its own column with the headline rate over judged props, and the `@types/react` recall metric counting layer names | A small PR |\n| **Memory split** | Opus, read-only | Separates the tsrs heap from our converter's share of Chakra's 1.1 GiB component phase, and gives a go or no-go on getting Chakra under 1 GiB | `memory-split.md` |\n| **MUI and Radix** | Sonnet | Installs both for real and runs the pattern evaluation on them, as one re-runnable command | `pattern-eval-mui-radix.md` |\n\nI chose the model per task. Opus goes where design judgment or provenance logic is involved, and Sonnet where the work is mechanical with a clear spec, to save tokens.\n\n**New findings on #490 (change 288)**, both folded into the Phase 1 worker's brief, since a second worker would conflict:\n1. **Quadratic scan:** `relevance::apply` rescans a layer with `Vec::contains` per member. That's about 6.8 million comparisons per component on a 3,700-member layer, repeated when answers are published. It's fixed with a set, and the timing is reported.\n2. **A regression in the expanded view:** `collapseInheritedProps: 'none'` loses React props for components typed as `ReturnType<typeof makeProps>`, because the narrowed request asks the checker for an empty React set. The fix keeps checker discovery when collapse is off, with a test for that exact shape.\n\n**#491's Entire Gates** show failing after 2h21m, with no open finding in Entire's list. I'll look into it once its CI settles. #490 shows no failing checks right now, but its CI will rerun when the worker's push lands.\n\nWhen the Phase 1 worker pushes, I run the acceptance command on the new build, then the merged-`main` oracle and the `STATUS.md` refresh. The release recovery, the audience and the addon default flip still need your answers. They're the only items waiting on you."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1086,"cache_read_input_tokens":962683,"output_tokens":881,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1086,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":881,"cache_read_input_tokens":962683,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1086,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1086},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7bef35df-0ff0-43cc-9a2a-51d7f3e8a239","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch7KSXnJkM19yk1cbmTGx","requestRef":"b1e11b14-19d8-4611-b857-5f1630fc922d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b313f202-745f-460c-ae9f-61fb5a92a47c","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:29:50.780Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/