{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","bridgeSessionId":"cse_013R2ytvK9B32ZaSUaSe6aAZ","lastSequenceNum":15975,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"5c0cc40b-9aa2-4338-8619-7e20be9dace0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b190fb6e-60c6-4ad3-93ae-13b7eff3fc86","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TCUBRmja8HW8hkMethkguB","type":"tool_result","content":"# Pattern evaluation, extension: real MUI and Radix installs (PR 490 listing rule vs main)\n\nExtends `pattern-eval.md` (same flags, same classifier `pattern-eval/eval.py`). Question: do the polymorphic, `asChild`, forwardRef-everywhere and styled patterns of MUI and Radix break the rule (main props in full, what the body uses directly, big generated/ambient sources as layer names)?\n\nShort answer: **no 490 regression on either library, and zero class (c) real-API hits by the classifier.** Two things the five-corpus report could not show surfaced: (1) MUI's declaration-only components (`.d.ts` beside `.js`) have no body, so 490's usage signal is empty and `className`/`style`/`ref` are lost (debatable class (a\n\n## What was installed (pinned, shallow, under `corpora/`, nothing else touched)\n\n- **MUI:** `mui/material-ui` at `6a200b8e5966ad34f10c4e57d86c543280fe8b8d`, `git clone --depth 1` into `corpora/mui-material`. Source dir measured: `packages/mui-material/src`. Install: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --filter '@mui/material...' --ignore-scripts` (workspace deps only, 21.6s), store/cache under `corpora/caches/pn\n- **Radix:** `radix-ui/primitives` at `eb3a2b7091293e27df8f9ba906632d8daa3d81a3` into `corpora/radix-primitives`. Source dir measured: `packages/react` (each `*/src`). Install: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts` (pnpm 11.5.0, 70 workspace projects, 668 packages).\n- **Prune:** corpora.py's rule (tests, stories, demos, dist/build dirs, `*.test.*`/`*.spec.*`/`*.stories.*`; never `node_modules`) inside the two source dirs (`pattern-eval/prune-extra.sh`).\n- **Not added to `scripts/corpora.py`** (no repo changes). The sandbox blocked writes under `corpora/` and `oracle-run/`, so fetch, install, prune and the runs used the sandbox disabled.\n- **Binaries:** main `oracle-run/target/release/caliper-docgen`; PR 490 `shrink/list-main-props/target/release/caliper-docgen` (d884334e). I found no newer 490 build. Flags: `extract --src <dir> --json --quiet --no-cache --load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies`, checker on; 490 also run with `none` for declar\n- **Rerun (one command):** `pattern-eval/run-extra.sh <main-bin> <490-bin>` (run `prune-extra.sh` once first). Output `pattern-eval/runs-extra/*.json`, `pattern-eval/{mui,radix}.extra.out`; `show-extra.py <lib> '<regex on component name>'` prints per-component rows and layers.\n\n## Per library (components present in both runs)\n\n| Library | Components | Rows median main -> 490 | p95 | Total | Grew >30 | Fell >90% | Hidden a / b / c / d |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| MUI (`mui-material/src`) | 76 | 10.5 -> 9 | 38 -> 36 | 1,878 -> 994 | 0 | 1 | 890 / 0 / 0 / 0 |\n| Radix (`packages/react`) | 289 | 3 -> 3 | 18 -> 18 | 1,825 -> 1,570 | 0 | 1 | 277 / 0 / 0 / 0 |\n\n- MUI's \"fell >90%\" is `PopperTooltip` order of magnitude (290 -> 12 rows); `Autocomplete` goes 338 -> 64. MUI counts include one duplicate: `Autocomplete` appears twice (a second key with the `.d.ts` path), so subtract about 1% for unique components.\n- Radix: 284 of 289 components are identical on main and 490. The 277 hidden members are one component, `ToastAnnounce` (279 -> 2 rows, all @types/react DOM/ARIA). Four grow slightly because reads promote members: `OneTimePasswordField` 18 -> 20, `OneTimePasswordFieldInput` 3 -> 9, `PasswordToggleFieldInput` 2 -> 6, `PasswordTog\n- Main already lists Radix at about 3 rows because the `ComponentPropsWithoutRef<typeof Primitive.x>` spread is already collapsed there; 490's rule has almost nothing left to remove.\n\n### Top 15 hidden names with declaring source\n\n- **MUI (all @types/react):** `style` x32 (HTMLAttributes [55]); `className` x27 (HTMLAttributes [55]); `ref` x14 (RefAttributes [1]); then 3 each (Autocomplete x2 keys + PopperTooltip): `onAbort`, `onSeekingCapture`, `onCompositionStartCapture`, `onCanPlayThroughCapture`, `onDragOver`, `onKeyUpCapture`, `onLoadCapture`, `onTouc\n- **Radix (all @types/react, one component):** `onCanPlayThrough`, `onPointerMove`, `onCompositionEnd`, `onPointerUp`, `onWheelCapture`, `onPointerOver`, `onStalled`, `onDropCapture`, `onLoadStartCapture` (DOMAttributes [169]); `title`, `lang` (HTMLAttributes [55]); `aria-grabbed`, `aria-details`, `aria-labelledby`, `aria-readon\n\n## Class (c) real-API hits\n\n**None by the classifier (0 on MUI, 0 on Radix).** Every hidden member is declared in `@types/react`. Debatable, counted in (a) like Mantine's `ref` in the first report, for the lead to judge:\n\n- `className` (27 MUI components), `style` (32) and `ref` (14): MUI documents `className`, `sx`, `ref` as part of every component's API. They are hidden because the `.d.ts` component has no body to read them (see below), not because of a rule choice. Examples: Dialog loses `ref`, `style`; Popover `ref`, `style`; Tooltip `classNa\n- In Radix nothing real is hidden: `asChild`, `ref`, `forceMount` and `aria-label` (TooltipContent, an own declaration) stay in 490.\n\n## Patterns\n\nBuckets from `eval.py` (regex heuristic); counts are components, rows main -> 490 median.\n\n| Pattern | MUI | Radix | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Own props only | 11; 3 -> 3 | 40; 3.5 -> 3.5 | works |\n| DOM-spread wrapper | 1; 3 -> 8 | 3; 3 -> 9 | works (reads promote DOM props that are used) |\n| Polymorphic `as` / OverridableComponent | 0 detected (17 comps list `component`) | 0 detected (187 comps list `asChild`) | heuristic only knows `as`; see below |\n| forwardRef / memo | 3; 4 -> 4 | 217; 3 -> 3 | works |\n| Compound / namespace (`Dialog.Root`) | 0 | 0 | not detected; Radix exports namespaced `Root = Dialog` aliases as separate components |\n| Hook-driven | 3; 14 -> 12 | 22; 3 -> 3.5 | works |\n| Factory-built | 0 | 0 | n/a |\n| Generic / conditional | 16; 0 -> 0 | 7; 3 -> 3 | MUI: 0 rows on both binaries, see below |\n| Other | 42; 16.5 -> 15 | 0 | not judged |\n\n- **Worst pattern: MUI `OverridableComponent` / `ExtendButtonBase` (polymorphic).** `declare const Button: ExtendButtonBase<ButtonTypeMap>` (`Button/Button.d.ts`), and the same for Chip, IconButton, Typography and friends, produces **no component at all** on either binary. `Select` (`declare const Select: (<Value>(props: SelectP\n- **Zero-row components (both binaries):** 12 MUI slot roots (`BackdropRoot`, `BadgeMark`, `BadgeRoot`, `ModalRoot`, `PopoverPaper`, `PopoverRoot`, `SliderMark`, `SliderMarkLabel`, `SliderRail`, `SliderRoot`, `SliderThumb`, `SliderTrack`) and 1 Radix (`OneTimePasswordFieldHiddenInput`). These are `styled(...)` factory results wi\n- **Declaration-only components.** MUI's `.js` bodies are not parsed (the extractor reads the `.d.ts`), so \"what the body uses\" is empty and 490 reduces to \"main props only\". Main's notable-inherited rows (`className`, `style`, `ref`) disappear with nothing to promote them.\n- **Radix `asChild`:** the Slot behaviour needs no rule; `asChild` is an own prop in all 187 components that have it and stays in both runs.\n\n## Before and after (rows, main -> 490; 490 layers in brackets)\n\n| Component | Main -> 490 | Lost | 490 layer |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| MUI Button | not extracted (both) | n/a | n/a |\n| MUI Select | not extracted (both) | n/a | n/a |\n| MUI TextField | 38 -> 37 | `ref` | React.ComponentPropsWithRef [269] |\n| MUI Dialog | 32 -> 30 | `ref`, `style` | React.ComponentPropsWithRef [273] |\n| MUI Popover | 31 -> 29 | `ref`, `style` | React.ComponentPropsWithRef [277] |\n| MUI Tooltip | 26 -> 24 | `className`, `style` | React.HTMLAttributes [275] |\n| MUI Autocomplete | 338 -> 64 | 274 DOM/ARIA incl. `className`, `style` | React.HTMLAttributes [274] |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a16f4ee4-e6c2-49a3-86ac-06de78599d35","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:34:24.658Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Pattern evaluation, extension: real MUI and Radix installs (PR 490 listing rule vs main)\n\nExtends `pattern-eval.md` (same flags, same classifier `pattern-eval/eval.py`). Question: do the polymorphic, `asChild`, forwardRef-everywhere and styled patterns of MUI and Radix break the rule (main props in full, what the body uses directly, big generated/ambient sources as layer names)?\n\nShort answer: **no 490 regression on either library, and zero class (c) real-API hits by the classifier.** Two things the five-corpus report could not show surfaced: (1) MUI's declaration-only components (`.d.ts` beside `.js`) have no body, so 490's usage signal is empty and `className`/`style`/`ref` are lost (debatable class (a\n\n## What was installed (pinned, shallow, under `corpora/`, nothing else touched)\n\n- **MUI:** `mui/material-ui` at `6a200b8e5966ad34f10c4e57d86c543280fe8b8d`, `git clone --depth 1` into `corpora/mui-material`. Source dir measured: `packages/mui-material/src`. Install: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --filter '@mui/material...' --ignore-scripts` (workspace deps only, 21.6s), store/cache under `corpora/caches/pn\n- **Radix:** `radix-ui/primitives` at `eb3a2b7091293e27df8f9ba906632d8daa3d81a3` into `corpora/radix-primitives`. Source dir measured: `packages/react` (each `*/src`). Install: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts` (pnpm 11.5.0, 70 workspace projects, 668 packages).\n- **Prune:** corpora.py's rule (tests, stories, demos, dist/build dirs, `*.test.*`/`*.spec.*`/`*.stories.*`; never `node_modules`) inside the two source dirs (`pattern-eval/prune-extra.sh`).\n- **Not added to `scripts/corpora.py`** (no repo changes). The sandbox blocked writes under `corpora/` and `oracle-run/`, so fetch, install, prune and the runs used the sandbox disabled.\n- **Binaries:** main `oracle-run/target/release/caliper-docgen`; PR 490 `shrink/list-main-props/target/release/caliper-docgen` (d884334e). I found no newer 490 build. Flags: `extract --src <dir> --json --quiet --no-cache --load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies`, checker on; 490 also run with `none` for declar\n- **Rerun (one command):** `pattern-eval/run-extra.sh <main-bin> <490-bin>` (run `prune-extra.sh` once first). Output `pattern-eval/runs-extra/*.json`, `pattern-eval/{mui,radix}.extra.out`; `show-extra.py <lib> '<regex on component name>'` prints per-component rows and layers.\n\n## Per library (components present in both runs)\n\n| Library | Components | Rows median main -> 490 | p95 | Total | Grew >30 | Fell >90% | Hidden a / b / c / d |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| MUI (`mui-material/src`) | 76 | 10.5 -> 9 | 38 -> 36 | 1,878 -> 994 | 0 | 1 | 890 / 0 / 0 / 0 |\n| Radix (`packages/react`) | 289 | 3 -> 3 | 18 -> 18 | 1,825 -> 1,570 | 0 | 1 | 277 / 0 / 0 / 0 |\n\n- MUI's \"fell >90%\" is `PopperTooltip` order of magnitude (290 -> 12 rows); `Autocomplete` goes 338 -> 64. MUI counts include one duplicate: `Autocomplete` appears twice (a second key with the `.d.ts` path), so subtract about 1% for unique components.\n- Radix: 284 of 289 components are identical on main and 490. The 277 hidden members are one component, `ToastAnnounce` (279 -> 2 rows, all @types/react DOM/ARIA). Four grow slightly because reads promote members: `OneTimePasswordField` 18 -> 20, `OneTimePasswordFieldInput` 3 -> 9, `PasswordToggleFieldInput` 2 -> 6, `PasswordTog\n- Main already lists Radix at about 3 rows because the `ComponentPropsWithoutRef<typeof Primitive.x>` spread is already collapsed there; 490's rule has almost nothing left to remove.\n\n### Top 15 hidden names with declaring source\n\n- **MUI (all @types/react):** `style` x32 (HTMLAttributes [55]); `className` x27 (HTMLAttributes [55]); `ref` x14 (RefAttributes [1]); then 3 each (Autocomplete x2 keys + PopperTooltip): `onAbort`, `onSeekingCapture`, `onCompositionStartCapture`, `onCanPlayThroughCapture`, `onDragOver`, `onKeyUpCapture`, `onLoadCapture`, `onTouc\n- **Radix (all @types/react, one component):** `onCanPlayThrough`, `onPointerMove`, `onCompositionEnd`, `onPointerUp`, `onWheelCapture`, `onPointerOver`, `onStalled`, `onDropCapture`, `onLoadStartCapture` (DOMAttributes [169]); `title`, `lang` (HTMLAttributes [55]); `aria-grabbed`, `aria-details`, `aria-labelledby`, `aria-readon\n\n## Class (c) real-API hits\n\n**None by the classifier (0 on MUI, 0 on Radix).** Every hidden member is declared in `@types/react`. Debatable, counted in (a) like Mantine's `ref` in the first report, for the lead to judge:\n\n- `className` (27 MUI components), `style` (32) and `ref` (14): MUI documents `className`, `sx`, `ref` as part of every component's API. They are hidden because the `.d.ts` component has no body to read them (see below), not because of a rule choice. Examples: Dialog loses `ref`, `style`; Popover `ref`, `style`; Tooltip `classNa\n- In Radix nothing real is hidden: `asChild`, `ref`, `forceMount` and `aria-label` (TooltipContent, an own declaration) stay in 490.\n\n## Patterns\n\nBuckets from `eval.py` (regex heuristic); counts are components, rows main -> 490 median.\n\n| Pattern | MUI | Radix | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Own props only | 11; 3 -> 3 | 40; 3.5 -> 3.5 | works |\n| DOM-spread wrapper | 1; 3 -> 8 | 3; 3 -> 9 | works (reads promote DOM props that are used) |\n| Polymorphic `as` / OverridableComponent | 0 detected (17 comps list `component`) | 0 detected (187 comps list `asChild`) | heuristic only knows `as`; see below |\n| forwardRef / memo | 3; 4 -> 4 | 217; 3 -> 3 | works |\n| Compound / namespace (`Dialog.Root`) | 0 | 0 | not detected; Radix exports namespaced `Root = Dialog` aliases as separate components |\n| Hook-driven | 3; 14 -> 12 | 22; 3 -> 3.5 | works |\n| Factory-built | 0 | 0 | n/a |\n| Generic / conditional | 16; 0 -> 0 | 7; 3 -> 3 | MUI: 0 rows on both binaries, see below |\n| Other | 42; 16.5 -> 15 | 0 | not judged |\n\n- **Worst pattern: MUI `OverridableComponent` / `ExtendButtonBase` (polymorphic).** `declare const Button: ExtendButtonBase<ButtonTypeMap>` (`Button/Button.d.ts`), and the same for Chip, IconButton, Typography and friends, produces **no component at all** on either binary. `Select` (`declare const Select: (<Value>(props: SelectP\n- **Zero-row components (both binaries):** 12 MUI slot roots (`BackdropRoot`, `BadgeMark`, `BadgeRoot`, `ModalRoot`, `PopoverPaper`, `PopoverRoot`, `SliderMark`, `SliderMarkLabel`, `SliderRail`, `SliderRoot`, `SliderThumb`, `SliderTrack`) and 1 Radix (`OneTimePasswordFieldHiddenInput`). These are `styled(...)` factory results wi\n- **Declaration-only components.** MUI's `.js` bodies are not parsed (the extractor reads the `.d.ts`), so \"what the body uses\" is empty and 490 reduces to \"main props only\". Main's notable-inherited rows (`className`, `style`, `ref`) disappear with nothing to promote them.\n- **Radix `asChild`:** the Slot behaviour needs no rule; `asChild` is an own prop in all 187 components that have it and stays in both runs.\n\n## Before and after (rows, main -> 490; 490 layers in brackets)\n\n| Component | Main -> 490 | Lost | 490 layer |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| MUI Button | not extracted (both) | n/a | n/a |\n| MUI Select | not extracted (both) | n/a | n/a |\n| MUI TextField | 38 -> 37 | `ref` | React.ComponentPropsWithRef [269] |\n| MUI Dialog | 32 -> 30 | `ref`, `style` | React.ComponentPropsWithRef [273] |\n| MUI Popover | 31 -> 29 | `ref`, `style` | React.ComponentPropsWithRef [277] |\n| MUI Tooltip | 26 -> 24 | `className`, `style` | React.HTMLAttributes [275] |\n| MUI Autocomplete | 338 -> 64 | 274 DOM/ARIA incl. `className`, `style` | React.HTMLAttributes [274] |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a4f6ea03-3157-4ee4-817d-f45ac7070ff8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8