{"parentUuid":"431b4457-0175-440b-8304-ff1189c9902c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b190fb6e-60c6-4ad3-93ae-13b7eff3fc86","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Bash, Edit, EnterWorktree, ExitWorktree, Grep, ListAgents, Monitor, Read, SendMessage, Skill, StructuredOutput, SubagentHandback, TaskCreate, TaskStop, TaskUpdate, ToolSearch, WebFetch, WebSearch, Workflow, Write, bash, mcp__playwright__browser_close, mcp__playwright__browser_console_messages, mcp__playwright__browser_evaluate, mcp__playwright__browser_navigate, mcp__playwright__browser_run_code_unsafe, mcp__playwright__browser_take_screenshot, mcp__playwright__browser_wait_for</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Role: lead/coordinator for caliper's roadmap (Storybook integration is the product's purpose). Plan work as trails (404 = Chakra 42 GB regression, 405 = relevance/collapse/Storybook usefulness), run workers in isolated worktrees, push their branches, link with `entire trail link 405 --branch <b> --base main --repo gh/orin-dx/caliper` (Entire opens the PR), publish bodies with `gh pr edit N --title ... --body-file ~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/pr/<name>.md`, resolve Entire findings with commit and test citations (the user said \"Make sure you dismiss the fixed findings please\"). The user approves and merges PRs.\n   - The user's product goal, in their words:\n     - \"produce the best results, not the overwhelming massive numbers that are not useful to anyone\"\n     - \"We want to make sure we're providing everything in the main props even if the story doesn't use them. And anything that the actual Button component uses directly. ... It seems like you understood the use to mean used in the story but that is not what I meant.\"\n     - \"colorPalette seems to be fine. Would this change work well for other components too? We're not trying to one-off this work. We want to address the patterns\" (LATEST, unanswered)\n   - Process feedback to honor:\n     - stop spot-fixing; fix classes of problems; no push/fix loops\n     - be thorough before pushing, and check CI/conflicts proactively\n     - avoid ceremony and wasted tokens\n     - no over-engineering\n     - \"Let's not convert to drafts, let's just fix it promptly\"\n     - stop calling the TypeScript checker an \"add-on\": it is the default engine, so say \"the TypeScript checker (on by default)\". I have not yet swept docs/changesets for this and had not confirmed what exactly they meant.\n   - Alpha: the user said my definition matches theirs. Definition: someone installs the Storybook addon on a real design system and gets correct Controls fast on first and second start, with plain statements of what's missing; stability and API freeze are not required.\n   - Standing constraints (still in force): oracle/corpus runs cost money (only when asked; the user explicitly asked for the oracle run from main and authorised `scripts/weekly.py --oracle --corpus antd --corpus shadcn` for workers; no `--agent-eval`); no files in /tmp (use ~/Projects/caliper-fixtures or $TMPDIR); no new scripts/options without CI/weekly value; token budget for workers (caps, targeted checks); don't poll CI; release actions (rerun, delete assets, re-dispatch, RELEASE_PENDING_FROM) need the user's say-so; the classifier blocked `gh pr ready --undo` (converting PRs to draft) because the user had not asked; dismiss findings only when verified fixed (user later told me to dismiss fixed ones); memory rule: measure peak RSS and time for resolver/checker changes.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Entire trails/changes. Change numbers map: 267=#469, 268=#470, 270=#472, 271=#473, 272=#474, 273=#475, 274=#476, 275=#477, 276=#478, 277=#479, 278=#480, 279=#481, 280=#482, 281=#483, 283=#485. The user asked for merge order given as \"trail and change number\".\n   - ADR 0026 (checker is the type authority), ADR 0028 (relevance evidence and checker scheduler; A2 section added by #490), ADR 0023 (htmlAttributes full default, cited but not in docs/adr).\n   - Collapse by default: `collapseInheritedProps` default `'dependencies'` (was `'none'`) in the addon; thresholds 200 (other) and 30 (ambient); notable props; layers of names.\n   - Relevance/T4: `relevance::decide`, `Placement`, `narrow`, `apply` (the one sink); `InheritedLayer::used`; provenance, never names (\"narrow by provenance, never by name\"); declined key sets (Pick/Omit); body facts (T1) with `handed_on`; forwarding (T3); call sites (T6).\n   - Findings classes C1–C8 (silence-as-evidence, lossy model asserting exactness, spelling vs binding, derived state outside the dependency model, two owners, host assumptions, hand-tuned policy without a reference model, contract drift). Guards must be ALLOW-lists (exhaustive matches, no `_ =>`). Pre-push gate (invariants, grammar sweep with TS API/checker as oracle, mutation proof, adversarial pass, `/code-review` awaited) is in `~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/worker-contract.md`.\n   - `htmlAttributes` modes: curated (default 2026-07-15 to 2026-10-26), full (default since 2026-10-26 for RDT parity), none. T4 reinterprets it as \"which DOM attributes are KNOWN as data\", not which become rows.\n   - Memory: checker session working set (not the loaded files) dominates; tsrs arena small; peak lands in generic instantiation; mimalloc; heap budget (60% of memory, at most 8 GiB, cgroup-aware incl. v1 mountinfo parsing).\n   - Release: Callisto; \"Execute approved release\" fails with E167 (ArtifactAssetDiffers) on the unfinished 0.11.0 release; docs/releasing.md recovery: delete the mismatched asset and `gh workflow run callisto-release.yml --ref main -f release_source_sha=<sha>`, or skip by moving `RELEASE_PENDING_FROM`.\n   - Stacked PRs duplicate findings; merge in order and merge `main` forward.\n   - Sandbox quirks: git commands inside compound `$(...)`/pipes get refused in worktree sessions (run plain separate commands); `$TMPDIR` differs between sandboxed and `dangerouslyDisableSandbox` runs; pre-commit hook runs lint/deny; worker worktrees need `pnpm install --offline --ignore-scripts --frozen-lockfile` and a `target/release` symlink for `just test-checker-lane`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/worker-contract.md`: appended \"Pre-push gate\" section (ALLOW-lists, invariants in PR body, grammar sweep, mutation proof, `/code-review` before reporting).\n   - `~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/shrink/findings-synthesis.md`: C1–C8 table and the pre-push gate.\n   - `~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/shrink/architecture-review.md`, `redteam-structural.md` (548 wrong answers, 12 classes), `redteam-collapse.md` (9 classes, D1–D9): evidence behind deleting structural expansion and the #485 fixes.\n   - `crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs` `add_absent`: edited (change 278) to keep `other.discriminant_prop` when self has none:\n     ```rust\n     if self.discriminant_prop.is_none() {\n         self.discriminant_prop = other.discriminant_prop;\n     }\n     ```\n     plus test `a_render_callbacks_discriminated_union_keeps_its_discriminant` in `crates/core/src/extractor/factory_props/tests.rs` (mutation-checked).\n   - `crates/core/src/dependency_types.rs` `mapping_refs`: edited to include `mapping.factory_props` in the dependency scan; test `a_package_type_named_only_by_a_factory_callback_annotation_is_loaded` in `crates/core/src/dependency_types/tests.rs`.\n   - `crates/core/src/cache.rs`: resolved merge conflict, `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION = 43` (note 43: `ComponentMapping::factory_type_params`); golden snapshot regenerated. T4 later moved the parse cache to 44.\n   - `crates/semantic/src/component.rs` `is_react_declared`: combined #483 and #485 rules:\n     ```rust\n     let files = || property.declarations.iter().map(|declaration| declared_in(declaration));\n     files().any(|file| declaration_origin(file) == Origin::React) && files().all(|file| file.contains(\"/node_modules/\"))\n     ```\n   - `crates/core/tests/relevance_props_type.rs`: test renamed to `a_redeclared_member_is_listed_and_not_held_by_its_collapsed_base` (#486; main later contained the same contract).\n   - `.changeset/*.md`: rewritten by a worker (#488 merged); new `keep-own-props-beside-collapsed-sources.md` (patch); T4 adds `list-props-by-usage` (minor). `docs/storybook-parity.md` default row fixed. #489 adds `MIGRATING.md` \"Upgrading the Storybook addon\" section and the addon README \"Known limits (alpha)\" (six limits).\n   - `~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/REPORT.md` (written by me from the worker's text; Chakra oracle row added), `diagnosis.md`, `memory-profile.md`; raw data in the same directory (weekly.json, fs/, work/, sb-demo/, mem/).\n   - `~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/pr/feat-list-props-by-usage.md`, `fix-list-props-memory.md`, `perf-instantiation-without-second-program.md`: PR bodies.\n   - Branch heads: `feat/list-props-by-usage` (PR #490) at d884334e; `perf/instantiation-without-second-program` (PR #491) at 466a71b1; `docs/alpha-limits-and-upgrade` (PR #489); `docs/user-focused-changesets` (#488 merged).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Mistakes the user called out, owned and corrected:\n     - holding finished fixes for extra verification (267's collapse fix sat unpushed)\n     - pushing worker fixes with their own caveats, causing push/fix loops\n     - building the relevance stack before any consumer existed\n     - T4 first treated as optional for the alpha\n     - misreading \"used\" as story/call-site use\n     - recommending a fixed notable-name list\n     - saying \"nothing own was lost\" from a differential that excluded dependency-declared props\n     - missing that #485 broke #477's test, which caused CI failures on #479, #480, #481 and #483\n   - Structural utility expansion: red-team found 548 wrong answers in 12 classes → expansion deleted (PR 475, −560 net lines) instead of patching an allow-list.\n   - T7b parked (`used` empty after dedupe, spectrum 30 props differed, watch model failed); later T4 delivered a working producer.\n   - Fixed-in-flight findings: 268 `arguments` in nested non-arrow functions, writes to props binding; 278 callback generics scope, defaults, dependency scan, discriminant; 279 cancel while converting and starvation; 281 lazy delta, destructuring defaults; 267 `Pick` alias via \"proven whole\" rule; #474 cgroup v1 comounted mounts.\n   - A conflict-merge snag: `$TMPDIR` mismatch lost an edit backup (restored by re-applying the edit); `git checkout` on mf branches needed `--no-track`; the pre-commit hook reformatted an array (`cargo fmt` style) once.\n   - Classifier denied: `gh pr ready --undo` (draft conversion; not asked) and earlier `gh run rerun` (release action).\n   - Entire Gates sometimes show failures/awaiting approval; handled by checking CI, not by working around.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved/merged: Chakra 42 GB regression (heap budget, size bound, collapse), collapse by default, JSX evidence, scheduler S1/S2, factory own props, relevance output (schema 8, `used`), checker memory fixes (cgroup), user-focused changesets, #485 own-props fix, #486 test contract.\n   - Oracle results (main de016f69, load 5–10 so times inflated): first run Chakra 3.50 s/1,908 MiB, Mantine 1.06 s/857, antd 1.49 s/1,072, shadcn 1.41 s/981, Spectrum 1.56 s/840; second run Chakra 0.77 s/476 MiB, Mantine 0.27 s, antd 0.08 s, shadcn 0.42 s, Spectrum 0.23 s; all within BUDGETS. Quality: shadcn 98.7%, antd 93.0%, Spectrum 88.4% right; Mantine 32.7% (62.9% not judged), Chakra 16.7% right/75.5% not judged (0 wrong; cause likely types cut by the size bound; unverified); oracle needs `REDACTED` for Chakra. Storybook dev cold: structural rows +891 ms after render, checker +134 ms; warm 128–156 ms; live edit 172 ms; 893 MiB server. Not measured: prefetch, antd in Storybook (Vite `./version`), quiet machine.\n   - Diagnosis of 437 rows: intended-by-default (`htmlAttributes: full`, React never collapses, Conditions 130 under threshold); CLI checker lane dropping React props is documented (type-checker-integration.md) but the layer carried no names.\n   - Memory profile: peak on Chakra lands in generic instantiation; loaded program is small (Chakra 2,291 files, 6.6 MiB); narrowing `types`, batching, allocator settings and streaming give little or reject (batching 4/8 changes output). #490 memory fix: shadcn 1,191→976, Chakra 2,009→1,825 MiB (output identical); #491: Chakra 1,886→1,690, shadcn 961→867 (output identical on six projects).\n   - T4 reworked rule (d884334e): main props listed in full (props type's own members, project sources, API-sized dependency sources), plus members the component body reads/destructures/passes explicitly (never via DOM spread), big generated/ambient sources stay as layer names. \"Generated\" = source over 200 members, or a mapped copy of `keyof` over 30 (changed from the brief's plain size 30 because that hid real APIs). Results: demo Button CLI rows 9→20 (as, asChild, css, extra, fresh, htmlContent/Height/Size/Translate/Width, kind, loading, loadingText, recipe, size, spinner, spinnerPlacement, tone, unstyled, variant); 286/706/130 stay names; colorPalette stays hidden (declared in SystemProperties in the installed types) — the user said this is fine; main-props differential 0 violations on seven corpora; RSS shadcn 972→975, Chakra 1,815→1,819.\n   - Open: Spectrum `aria-*`/`id` hiding (SharedDom ambient by path; 972 components) was a pending user decision under the old rule and may look different under the new rule (worker did not say).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   (In this stretch, in order; abbreviated where long.)\n   - \"change #270 has findings to address\"; \"So do #267 and #268\"\n   - \"You need to consider all of the findings together, architecturally and semantically. Also consider the patterns and make sure the agents won't find even more things\"\n   - \"I think we still have a lot of changes in entire with findings that need to be addressed. Look at all of them. Consider the patterns and see if we need to adjust our architecture and models to better address the issues.\" and \"We also have conflicts in some branches that need fixing\"\n   - \"Please also consider all the changes we made and see if we should refactor or adjust anything to better fit the architecture, model, best practices and things like traits\"\n   - \"Keep moving forward and set up the branches appropriately. When telling me when to merge, use the trait and change number for the order\" (read as trail and change number)\n   - \"272 has a finding still: [cgroup v1 finding]\"; \"Looks like we still have lots of findings\"\n   - \"Doesn't look like you've fixed the finding for #267 at all have you? Why is it taking hours???? ... ridiculously slow.\"\n   - \"Are we done? Everything that is open still have findings... I can't believe you're stuck in this loop of push, fix, push, fix without really looking into what might fail like I asked.\"\n   - \"Merged 267 but all other open changes still have unresolved findings so I can't approve and merge\"\n   - \"Waiting on what?\"; \"Are we spinning cycles and wasting tokens with human ceremony?\"; \"Are we wasting time and tokens in other ones too? How do we keep making these mistakes?\"\n   - \"Let's not convert to drafts, let's just fix is promptly and without wasting time/tokens\"; \"But without rushing, we can take a step back, consider all of it and move foward without over-engineering\"\n   - \"Make sure you dismiss the fixed findings please\"; \"You're not being thorough, ci failed for change #277\"; \"And the other changes don't seem to have been addressed\"; \"And a conflict\"; \"What is the merge order to avoid conflicts?\"; \"Merged some more but now we have a conflict for feat/relevance-forwarding\"; \"feat/factory-own-props and feat/scheduler-priority-and-cancel have findings... Same for feat/relevance-output along with failing CI\"; \"Change 278 has a finding...\"; \"We have two open changes with findings we need to address\"; \"#278 has another fingind...\" (dependency scan); \"and #281 has two findings\"\n   - \"FYI from michi: ...\" (informational about michi 0.9/0.10 TOON/response contract; Caliper keeps canonical JSON as source of truth; no action)\n   - \"Did we not add appropriate changesets, user-focused, scannable, etc to get a new caliper version?\"; \"Also, with everything merged are we ready for a fresh oracle run from latest main?\"; \"Prior to a release?\"\n   - \"Start the oracle please, I want to get a sense of our state now... performance, quality of output for both the overall CLI as well as storybook. First run, second run as well as storybook dev mode.\"\n   - \"We want to consider what we need to wrap up for an alpha\"; \"Your definition is pretty aligned with my thinking for alpha\"; \"How's the oracle?\"\n   - \"We should stop calling it an add-on, ts checker is more accurate since it's on by default now. And before we didn't do full-HTML, right? So why is that the default now. Didn't we agree that we would produce the best results, not the overwelming, massive numbers that are not useful to anyone?\"; \"That we would narraw it down by usage? WTF\"\n   - \"Where are we on this?\"; \"That is a very large amount of memory to use. How can we cut down our memory usage significantly? Where can we find improvements?\"; \"Is there a way to narrow down what the checker loads for us?\"; \"Let's tackle these please\"\n   - \"What's the next highest priorities to tackle?\"; \"Does this include the optimizations to avoid massive number of props, most of which are not quite relevant??\"\n   - \"Does the chakra button's 10 props include all of the ones defined in the button itself and any inherited that are used?\"\n   - \"We want to make sure we're providing Everything in the main props even if the story doesn't use them. And anything that the actual Button component uses directly, does that make sense? It seems like you understood the use to mean used in the story but that is not what I meant.\"\n   - \"colorPalette seems to be fine. Would this change work well for other components too? We're not trying to one-off this work. We want to address the patterns\" (LATEST; unanswered)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Answer the latest question: does the main-props + body-use rule generalize across components/design systems (evidence to gather/present: the seven-corpora differential, row counts for Button on Chakra demo/Mantine/antd/shadcn new-york and aria/Spectrum/react-aria-components, five-corpora medians; show the 20 most common names hidden by the noise rule; what's unverified).\n   - Finish verifying #490 before merge: the real Storybook browser check of the 20 rows; oracle on antd and shadcn (`scripts/weekly.py --oracle --corpus antd --corpus shadcn`, authorised) for the rework; the `/code-review` result of the rework round; read the diff; re-check the Spectrum `aria-*`/`id` question under the new rule; confirm CI/Entire findings on #490, #491, #489.\n   - Merge order and blockers: #490, #491, #489 pending the user's approval; #487 (Wisp v5 chore) untouched.\n   - Release pipeline: 0.11.0 recovery (E167): user's choice needed between deleting the mismatched asset and re-dispatching, or skipping via `RELEASE_PENDING_FROM`; corpora budget gate has never run on a real release PR (the new dispatch step in `callisto-release.yml` is untested).\n   - Other alpha items: weekly oracle needs the Node heap setting for Chakra and a split of \"not judged\" (Chakra 75.5%, Mantine 63%); the weekly's @types/react recall column is stale; a clean re-timing on an idle machine; refresh `docs/STATUS.md` speed numbers and re-run the oracle on merged main; sweep docs/changesets for \"add-on\" wording (confirm meaning first); remaining alpha decisions: audience, and whether the addon default flip ships in the first alpha.\n   - Later/optional: converter memo sharing (memory ranked saving #3, Chakra under 1 GiB; large, public type change); Storybook measurements not done (prefetch, antd `./version`, head-to-head vs react-docgen-typescript); unfixed review items from #490's earlier round (`key` in the CLI for unlayered components, allocations in `narrow`, unused `_mode` parameter (semver break), double alias walk).\n   - Task list (TaskCreate): #8 T4 in progress; #10 scheduler slices in progress (S3–S5 not started); #11 Storybook head-to-head pending; #12 pending (stale).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before the summary request: T4 rework on #490. Worker `af9171696a52d8df2` reported `fix/list-main-props` at d884334e (committed locally); I verified it contains the remote head and pushed it to `feat/list-props-by-usage` as d884334e. I reported Button rows 9→20, differential 0 violations on seven corpora, RSS unchanged, gates exit 0, and the not-done items (Storybook browser check, antd/shadcn oracle, review result not seen), and asked whether to do the Storybook check and oracle myself. The user replied: colorPalette is fine, and asked whether this change works well for other components too, because they want the patterns addressed and not a one-off. No answer has been given yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Answer the user's latest message: \"Would this change work well for other components too? We're not trying to one-off this work. We want to address the patterns\". Concretely: give a pattern-level assessment from evidence, and have a worker (or me) run the remaining verification on #490 (the Storybook browser check, the antd/shadcn oracle, the `/code-review` result, row counts for `Button`-like components across Chakra demo, Mantine, antd, shadcn new-york/aria, Spectrum, react-aria-components, plus the 20 most common hidden names), then report whether the rule (main props in full, plus what the body uses directly, with large generated/ambient sources as layer names, decided by provenance and structure, not names) holds across design systems, and what patterns still fail (for example, props declared in a big style source like colorPalette, and the Spectrum shared-DOM decision). Do not merge or release anything without the user's approval.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8/ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"b98bf20b-caea-4b80-88d9-afa81d87a168","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:03:04.785Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":377,"turnIndex":829},"turnOrigin":"peer","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
{"parentUuid":"b98bf20b-caea-4b80-88d9-afa81d87a168","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/memory-profile.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/memory-profile.md","content":"# Memory profile: first run with the checker (2026-11-16)\n\nThese are scratch measurements only. Nothing was committed or pushed. Binaries:\n- origin/main de016f69: `oracle-run/target/release/caliper-docgen`.\n- Instrumented builds of de016f69 (`mem/target-main`) and of the PR 490 head 3eb7ec26 (`mem/target-pr490`).\n\nInstrumentation (`mem/instrument.pl`, scratch copy only):\n- `PHASE` markers print mimalloc `mi_process_info` (current RSS, peak RSS, commit) and the tsrs arena's resident MiB (`checker::arena_mib`).\n- Environment switches: `CAL_PROGRAMS` (lanes), `CAL_TYPES` (compiler `types`), `CAL_BATCHES` (sequential root batches) and `CAL_READS_OUT` (dumps the kept answer's `reads`).\n\nCommand: `extract --json --load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies --cache-dir <empty>`. Harness:\n- `mem/prof.sh` runs it under `/usr/bin/time -l` and samples `ps` RSS every 50 ms.\n- `mem/exp.sh` runs the experiments.\n- Raw files are in `mem/runs/`, and `mem/exp.txt` and `mem/base.txt` hold the summaries.\n\nLoad was 8 to 20 throughout. Times are noisy; RSS is not. The uninstrumented and instrumented peaks agree within 2%: Chakra 1,866 to 1,910 MiB across 4 runs, shadcn 980 to 991, Mantine 860 to 871, sb-demo 230.\n\n## 1. Peak RSS by phase (instrumented main, MiB = mimalloc current RSS at the marker)\n\n| Phase (end of) | Chakra | shadcn | Mantine | sb-demo |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| (a)+(b) structural pass incl. dependency declarations, `--no-checker` alone | 364* | 357 | 181* | n/a |\n| (c) same point with the early checker program loading in parallel | 490 (arena 48) | 690 (arena 166) | 280 (arena 48) | 185 (arena 31) |\n| (d1) all components answered and converted | 1,604 (arena 155) | 751 (arena 196) | 672 (arena 87) | 199 |\n| (d2) generic instantiation (`instantiate::answer`): **the process peak is here in all four** | **1,866** | **982** | **868** | **230** |\n| checker released, kept answer saved | 1,704 | 757 | 832 | 219 |\n| (e) merge (`merge_semantic_in`: apply_props, relevance, layers) | 1,705 | 758 | 836 | 220 |\n| (f) JSON written (streamed, 64 KiB BufWriter) | 1,715 (+10) | 760 (+2) | 869 (+33) | 222 |\n| Peak (`time -l`) | 1,866 | 982 | 871 | 230 |\n\n\\* From REPORT.md (structural run).\n\nWhat the checker loads (E1, from the kept answer's `reads`):\n- Chakra: 2,291 files, 6.6 MiB. Of that, `@types/node` is 70 files and 2.4 MiB, csstype 0.86 MiB, and @ark-ui 918 files but 0.53 MiB. Project files are 226 (0.7 MiB). There were 3,748 failed lookups.\n- shadcn: 5,165 files, 25.8 MiB. Project 1,231 files (6.2 MiB); lucide-react 1.9 MiB, next 363 files (1.7 MiB), @tabler/icons 1.3 MiB, date-fns 1.2 MiB, `@types/node` 2.2 MiB. There were 8,830 failed lookups.\n- Mantine: 1,393 files, 6.3 MiB, of which `@types/node` is 2.4 MiB.\n- sb-demo: 1,895 files, 3.1 MiB.\n- No TypeScript `lib.*.d.ts` is read from disk: tsrs embeds them, so their size is not in these counts.\n- The tsrs arena (nodes, symbols, types) is only 87 to 206 MiB at its peak.\n\nConclusion: the program that gets loaded (phase c) is small. The memory is the checker session's working set. That is the tsrs heap (type and relation caches, which live on mimalloc, not in the arena) plus the converter's memo and trees, all built in phase d.\n- On Chakra, d1 adds 1,114 MiB. Most of it, 530 to 1,402 MiB, comes in the first second, while the 7 style-system components each make about 4,000 requests.\n- The result is small by comparison. The kept answer (the serialized semantic outcome) is 32.5 / 9.0 / 23.4 / 1.9 MiB, and the second run peaks at 476 MiB on Chakra.\n- So about 1.4 GiB of Chakra's peak is session state that the output does not need.\n- Not separated: how much of d1 is tsrs heap and how much is converter heap. Both are mimalloc; there is no dhat feature or counting allocator.\n\n## 2. PR 490 on shadcn (+22%): measured\n\n| shadcn | main | PR 490 | Δ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `--no-checker` peak | 357 | 463 | **+106 (+30%)**, structural time 0.32 → 0.49 s |\n| structural marker (checker run) | 690 (commit 863) | 810 (commit 990) | +120 |\n| components answered (d1) | 751 | 999 | +248 |\n| peak (d2) | 982 | 1,195 | +213 (+22%) |\n| checker `batchRequests` / memo hits / misses | 4,265 / 17,076 / 8,060 | 4,087 / 10,909 / 6,959 | the checker does **less** work |\n| `heap_peak_mib` (backend log) | 859 | 1,114 | +255 |\n\nCause:\n- Caliper-side data, not checker work.\n- About half (+106 MiB) is already in the structural pass. PR 490 adds `relevance: Option<Arc<Placement>>` to every component (`types/output.rs:143`, kept across merges) and the element layers' member lists. `InheritedLayer.members` is `Vec<String>` per component, not interned; only the JSON's `nameLists` are interned.\n- The rest (about +130 MiB) appears during the component phase although checker requests fell. Likely cause: those placements and listings ride along in the targets that `session` clones per file. Not proven: no allocation profile.\n- Chakra grows the same way, 1,866 → 2,030 (+164, +9%); Mantine 871 → 894.\n\n## 3. Ranked savings (measured)\n\n| # | Change | Chakra | shadcn | Effort / files | Risk | Dev server? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Generic instantiation builds a **second whole program**. `Rpc::layered` (rpc.rs:548) creates a fresh snapshot rooted at every root file plus the synthetic files, while both lane programs and their caches are still alive, and the peak lands there in all four. Fix: derive it from the live snapshot (`updateSnapshot`, as `beside` does), root it only at the generic components' files, or release lane 2 and its converter first. | bound **−262 (−14%)** | bound **−231 (−24%)** (Mantine −196, −23%; sb-demo −31) | M; lib.rs `session`, rpc.rs `layered`, instantiate.rs | Output-preserving by design; check with an identity diff | Likely yes, where a session answers a generic component (not measured) |\n| 2 | Undo PR 490's retained data: no per-component `Arc<Placement>` after merge, interned or shared layer member lists | PR 490 −164 (−8%) | PR 490 **−213 (−18%)**; structural −106 | M; core relevance, output.rs, semantic targets | None to output if only storage changes | Yes: structural data lives in the session |\n| 3 | Converter working set: share memo results (`Arc` subtrees, no deep clone on 812k memo hits vs 40k misses), and cut oversized types before expanding them, not after (chakra-memory.md Part C) | not measured; d1 is +1,114 MiB, about 870 of it in the first 1 s | d1 +61 | L; convert.rs, core `PropType`, serializers | Public type change (semver); output identical if done right | Yes |\n| 4 | One checker lane (`CHECKER_PROGRAMS` 2 → 1) | −15 (−1%), time 3.8 → 6.3 s | −58 (−6%), 1.55 → 4.95 s | S; lib.rs | Identical output; much slower | Minor |\n| 5 | Sequential root batches. 2 batches (b2) | −41 (−2%) | −6 | M (~60 lines; scratch `batched`) | b2 identical | No |\n|   | b2 with one lane | −101 (−5%), 5.6 s | −50 (−5%) | | identical | |\n|   | 4 or 8 batches | b4 −96 (−5%), 10.8 s; b8 +31 | b4 +8, b8 −20 | | **Output changes** (Chakra OPAQUE_TYPE 8 → 69, JSON 49.6 → 46.8 MB): a batch's program misses declarations other roots bring | rejected |\n| 6 | E2 `types: [\"react\"]` | −12 (noise); reads 2,291 → 2,076 files, 6.6 → 3.6 MiB | +5 (noise); reads unchanged at 5,165 | S; rpc.rs `default_options` | Output identical on all three (0 changed props, so there are no examples) | No |\n|   | Mantine with the same `types` setting | −13; reads 1,393 → 1,017 files, 6.3 → 3.4 MiB | | | | |\n| 7 | mimalloc: `MIMALLOC_PURGE_DELAY=0`; `ARENA_EAGER_COMMIT=0` with a 64 MiB reserve | 1,887 / 1,867 vs 1,866 to 1,910 (0%) | 980 vs 982 (0%) | S | None | No |\n| 8 | Streaming output: already streamed (`write_extraction_output_json` into a BufWriter) | written +10 | +2 (Mantine +33) | n/a | n/a | n/a |\n| 9 | Free data before the next phase | Useless for the peak: the peak is before the merge and the process exits after writing | | | | |\n| 10 | Early program reopened (\"not the request's\", 116 vs 113 roots) on Chakra and Mantine | memory not separated; about 70 ms | not seen | S | None | No |\n\nE1 and E2 answer \"can we narrow what the checker loads\":\n- The program is already only the roots' closure.\n- Disk input is 3 to 26 MiB, and the TypeScript libs are embedded.\n- Narrowing `types` drops `@types/node` (about 2.4 MiB of text) with no RSS or output change.\n- Loading less is not where the memory is.\n\n## 4. Recommendation\n\n1. **#1, share or narrow the generic-instantiation program.** Measured bound: Chakra 1,866 → about 1,604 MiB; shadcn 982 → about 751; Mantine 868 → about 672.\n2. **#2, before merging PR 490.** Its +164 to +213 MiB is all Caliper-side retained data. With #1, PR 490's shadcn goes from 1,195 to about 750 to 800 MiB.\n3. **#3, shared memo results and an early size cut.** This is the only lever on Chakra's +1.1 GiB component phase. Its saving is not measured.\n\nExpected with #1 and #2:\n- Chakra 1.87 GiB (2.03 with PR 490) → about 1.6 GiB.\n- shadcn 0.98 (1.2) → about 0.75 GiB.\n- Getting below 1 GiB on Chakra needs #3.\n\nNot measured:\n- How d1 splits between the tsrs heap and the converter (no allocation profiler).\n- The fix for #1 itself: the number above is a bound, peak minus the d1 marker.\n- The Storybook dev server's 893 MiB.\n- antd and Spectrum.\n- `--collapse-inherited-props all`: a harness flag clash, so it was not run.\n- A quiet machine (load 8 to 20; RSS is unaffected).\n","numLines":106,"startLine":1,"totalLines":106}},"displayPath":"../../../../caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/memory-profile.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"403639cf-ed25-4e6f-80c3-4768eb741173","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:34:25.563Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/memory-profile.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t# Memory profile: first run with the checker (2026-11-16)\n2\t\n3\tThese are scratch measurements only. Nothing was committed or pushed. Binaries:\n4\t- origin/main de016f69: `oracle-run/target/release/caliper-docgen`.\n5\t- Instrumented builds of de016f69 (`mem/target-main`) and of the PR 490 head 3eb7ec26 (`mem/target-pr490`).\n6\t\n7\tInstrumentation (`mem/instrument.pl`, scratch copy only):\n8\t- `PHASE` markers print mimalloc `mi_process_info` (current RSS, peak RSS, commit) and the tsrs arena's resident MiB (`checker::arena_mib`).\n9\t- Environment switches: `CAL_PROGRAMS` (lanes), `CAL_TYPES` (compiler `types`), `CAL_BATCHES` (sequential root batches) and `CAL_READS_OUT` (dumps the kept answer's `reads`).\n10\t\n11\tCommand: `extract --json --load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies --cache-dir <empty>`. Harness:\n12\t- `mem/prof.sh` runs it under `/usr/bin/time -l` and samples `ps` RSS every 50 ms.\n13\t- `mem/exp.sh` runs the experiments.\n14\t- Raw files are in `mem/runs/`, and `mem/exp.txt` and `mem/base.txt` hold the summaries.\n15\t\n16\tLoad was 8 to 20 throughout. Times are noisy; RSS is not. The uninstrumented and instrumented peaks agree within 2%: Chakra 1,866 to 1,910 MiB across 4 runs, shadcn 980 to 991, Mantine 860 to 871, sb-demo 230.\n17\t\n18\t## 1. Peak RSS by phase (instrumented main, MiB = mimalloc current RSS at the marker)\n19\t\n20\t| Phase (end of) | Chakra | shadcn | Mantine | sb-demo |\n21\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n22\t| (a)+(b) structural pass incl. dependency declarations, `--no-checker` alone | 364* | 357 | 181* | n/a |\n23\t| (c) same point with the early checker program loading in parallel | 490 (arena 48) | 690 (arena 166) | 280 (arena 48) | 185 (arena 31) |\n24\t| (d1) all components answered and converted | 1,604 (arena 155) | 751 (arena 196) | 672 (arena 87) | 199 |\n25\t| (d2) generic instantiation (`instantiate::answer`): **the process peak is here in all four** | **1,866** | **982** | **868** | **230** |\n26\t| checker released, kept answer saved | 1,704 | 757 | 832 | 219 |\n27\t| (e) merge (`merge_semantic_in`: apply_props, relevance, layers) | 1,705 | 758 | 836 | 220 |\n28\t| (f) JSON written (streamed, 64 KiB BufWriter) | 1,715 (+10) | 760 (+2) | 869 (+33) | 222 |\n29\t| Peak (`time -l`) | 1,866 | 982 | 871 | 230 |\n30\t\n31\t\\* From REPORT.md (structural run).\n32\t\n33\tWhat the checker loads (E1, from the kept answer's `reads`):\n34\t- Chakra: 2,291 files, 6.6 MiB. Of that, `@types/node` is 70 files and 2.4 MiB, csstype 0.86 MiB, and @ark-ui 918 files but 0.53 MiB. Project files are 226 (0.7 MiB). There were 3,748 failed lookups.\n35\t- shadcn: 5,165 files, 25.8 MiB. Project 1,231 files (6.2 MiB); lucide-react 1.9 MiB, next 363 files (1.7 MiB), @tabler/icons 1.3 MiB, date-fns 1.2 MiB, `@types/node` 2.2 MiB. There were 8,830 failed lookups.\n36\t- Mantine: 1,393 files, 6.3 MiB, of which `@types/node` is 2.4 MiB.\n37\t- sb-demo: 1,895 files, 3.1 MiB.\n38\t- No TypeScript `lib.*.d.ts` is read from disk: tsrs embeds them, so their size is not in these counts.\n39\t- The tsrs arena (nodes, symbols, types) is only 87 to 206 MiB at its peak.\n40\t\n41\tConclusion: the program that gets loaded (phase c) is small. The memory is the checker session's working set. That is the tsrs heap (type and relation caches, which live on mimalloc, not in the arena) plus the converter's memo and trees, all built in phase d.\n42\t- On Chakra, d1 adds 1,114 MiB. Most of it, 530 to 1,402 MiB, comes in the first second, while the 7 style-system components each make about 4,000 requests.\n43\t- The result is small by comparison. The kept answer (the serialized semantic outcome) is 32.5 / 9.0 / 23.4 / 1.9 MiB, and the second run peaks at 476 MiB on Chakra.\n44\t- So about 1.4 GiB of Chakra's peak is session state that the output does not need.\n45\t- Not separated: how much of d1 is tsrs heap and how much is converter heap. Both are mimalloc; there is no dhat feature or counting allocator.\n46\t\n47\t## 2. PR 490 on shadcn (+22%): measured\n48\t\n49\t| shadcn | main | PR 490 | Δ |\n50\t|---|---|---|---|\n51\t| `--no-checker` peak | 357 | 463 | **+106 (+30%)**, structural time 0.32 → 0.49 s |\n52\t| structural marker (checker run) | 690 (commit 863) | 810 (commit 990) | +120 |\n53\t| components answered (d1) | 751 | 999 | +248 |\n54\t| peak (d2) | 982 | 1,195 | +213 (+22%) |\n55\t| checker `batchRequests` / memo hits / misses | 4,265 / 17,076 / 8,060 | 4,087 / 10,909 / 6,959 | the checker does **less** work |\n56\t| `heap_peak_mib` (backend log) | 859 | 1,114 | +255 |\n57\t\n58\tCause:\n59\t- Caliper-side data, not checker work.\n60\t- About half (+106 MiB) is already in the structural pass. PR 490 adds `relevance: Option<Arc<Placement>>` to every component (`types/output.rs:143`, kept across merges) and the element layers' member lists. `InheritedLayer.members` is `Vec<String>` per component, not interned; only the JSON's `nameLists` are interned.\n61\t- The rest (about +130 MiB) appears during the component phase although checker requests fell. Likely cause: those placements and listings ride along in the targets that `session` clones per file. Not proven: no allocation profile.\n62\t- Chakra grows the same way, 1,866 → 2,030 (+164, +9%); Mantine 871 → 894.\n63\t\n64\t## 3. Ranked savings (measured)\n65\t\n66\t| # | Change | Chakra | shadcn | Effort / files | Risk | Dev server? |\n67\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n68\t| 1 | Generic instantiation builds a **second whole program**. `Rpc::layered` (rpc.rs:548) creates a fresh snapshot rooted at every root file plus the synthetic files, while both lane programs and their caches are still alive, and the peak lands there in all four. Fix: derive it from the live snapshot (`updateSnapshot`, as `beside` does), root it only at the generic components' files, or release lane 2 and its converter first. | bound **−262 (−14%)** | bound **−231 (−24%)** (Mantine −196, −23%; sb-demo −31) | M; lib.rs `session`, rpc.rs `layered`, instantiate.rs | Output-preserving by design; check with an identity diff | Likely yes, where a session answers a generic component (not measured) |\n69\t| 2 | Undo PR 490's retained data: no per-component `Arc<Placement>` after merge, interned or shared layer member lists | PR 490 −164 (−8%) | PR 490 **−213 (−18%)**; structural −106 | M; core relevance, output.rs, semantic targets | None to output if only storage changes | Yes: structural data lives in the session |\n70\t| 3 | Converter working set: share memo results (`Arc` subtrees, no deep clone on 812k memo hits vs 40k misses), and cut oversized types before expanding them, not after (chakra-memory.md Part C) | not measured; d1 is +1,114 MiB, about 870 of it in the first 1 s | d1 +61 | L; convert.rs, core `PropType`, serializers | Public type change (semver); output identical if done right | Yes |\n71\t| 4 | One checker lane (`CHECKER_PROGRAMS` 2 → 1) | −15 (−1%), time 3.8 → 6.3 s | −58 (−6%), 1.55 → 4.95 s | S; lib.rs | Identical output; much slower | Minor |\n72\t| 5 | Sequential root batches. 2 batches (b2) | −41 (−2%) | −6 | M (~60 lines; scratch `batched`) | b2 identical | No |\n73\t|   | b2 with one lane | −101 (−5%), 5.6 s | −50 (−5%) | | identical | |\n74\t|   | 4 or 8 batches | b4 −96 (−5%), 10.8 s; b8 +31 | b4 +8, b8 −20 | | **Output changes** (Chakra OPAQUE_TYPE 8 → 69, JSON 49.6 → 46.8 MB): a batch's program misses declarations other roots bring | rejected |\n75\t| 6 | E2 `types: [\"react\"]` | −12 (noise); reads 2,291 → 2,076 files, 6.6 → 3.6 MiB | +5 (noise); reads unchanged at 5,165 | S; rpc.rs `default_options` | Output identical on all three (0 changed props, so there are no examples) | No |\n76\t|   | Mantine with the same `types` setting | −13; reads 1,393 → 1,017 files, 6.3 → 3.4 MiB | | | | |\n77\t| 7 | mimalloc: `MIMALLOC_PURGE_DELAY=0`; `ARENA_EAGER_COMMIT=0` with a 64 MiB reserve | 1,887 / 1,867 vs 1,866 to 1,910 (0%) | 980 vs 982 (0%) | S | None | No |\n78\t| 8 | Streaming output: already streamed (`write_extraction_output_json` into a BufWriter) | written +10 | +2 (Mantine +33) | n/a | n/a | n/a |\n79\t| 9 | Free data before the next phase | Useless for the peak: the peak is before the merge and the process exits after writing | | | | |\n80\t| 10 | Early program reopened (\"not the request's\", 116 vs 113 roots) on Chakra and Mantine | memory not separated; about 70 ms | not seen | S | None | No |\n81\t\n82\tE1 and E2 answer \"can we narrow what the checker loads\":\n83\t- The program is already only the roots' closure.\n84\t- Disk input is 3 to 26 MiB, and the TypeScript libs are embedded.\n85\t- Narrowing `types` drops `@types/node` (about 2.4 MiB of text) with no RSS or output change.\n86\t- Loading less is not where the memory is.\n87\t\n88\t## 4. Recommendation\n89\t\n90\t1. **#1, share or narrow the generic-instantiation program.** Measured bound: Chakra 1,866 → about 1,604 MiB; shadcn 982 → about 751; Mantine 868 → about 672.\n91\t2. **#2, before merging PR 490.** Its +164 to +213 MiB is all Caliper-side retained data. With #1, PR 490's shadcn goes from 1,195 to about 750 to 800 MiB.\n92\t3. **#3, shared memo results and an early size cut.** This is the only lever on Chakra's +1.1 GiB component phase. Its saving is not measured.\n93\t\n94\tExpected with #1 and #2:\n95\t- Chakra 1.87 GiB (2.03 with PR 490) → about 1.6 GiB.\n96\t- shadcn 0.98 (1.2) → about 0.75 GiB.\n97\t- Getting below 1 GiB on Chakra needs #3.\n98\t\n99\tNot measured:\n100\t- How d1 splits between the tsrs heap and the converter (no allocation profiler).\n101\t- The fix for #1 itself: the number above is a bound, peak minus the d1 marker.\n102\t- The Storybook dev server's 893 MiB.\n103\t- antd and Spectrum.\n104\t- `--collapse-inherited-props all`: a harness flag clash, so it was not run.\n105\t- A quiet machine (load 8 to 20; RSS is unaffected).\n106\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
{"parentUuid":"403639cf-ed25-4e6f-80c3-4768eb741173","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/REPORT.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/REPORT.md","content":"# caliper measurement at origin/main de016f69 (2026-11-15)\n\nSHA `de016f69c3b021aaf3223420faf7866087ded864` (merge of #483; binary reports 0.11.0, unreleased main). `git fetch` was blocked in the worker's sandbox, so this is the last fetched origin/main. The machine was shared with other agents: the 1-minute load average stayed 5 to 10 during every timed step, so every timing is inflated. Memory and sizes are not affected. Written by the lead from the measurement worker's report; the raw files are in this directory (`weekly.json`, `weekly.md`, `issue.md`, `logs/`, `fs/`, `work/`, `sb-demo/`).\n\n## Summary\n\n- First run (empty cache, checker on, addon config): Chakra 3.50 s / 1,908 MiB, Mantine 1.06 s / 857 MiB, antd 1.49 s / 1,072 MiB, shadcn 1.41 s / 981 MiB, Spectrum 1.56 s / 840 MiB. 1.4x (Mantine, Spectrum) to 6.4x (Chakra) faster than react-docgen-typescript (RDT). All five within the budgets (`weekly.py --enforce-budgets` exit 0).\n- Second run (kept checker answer): Chakra 0.77 s / 476 MiB, Mantine 0.27 s, antd 0.08 s, shadcn 0.42 s, Spectrum 0.23 s: 5.6x to 29x faster than RDT. Structural floor (`--no-checker`) 0.07 to 0.49 s.\n- Quality (share of the props of reported components the checker confirms): shadcn 98.7%, antd 93.0%, Spectrum 88.4%, Mantine 32.7% (62.9% not judged, 0 wrong). Wrong props: shadcn 0, antd 1, Spectrum 7, Mantine 0. Chakra: not measured, the oracle died of a Node heap OOM.\n- Storybook dev mode, cold (browser, demo Button over Chakra ButtonProps): structural Controls 891 ms after the story renders, the checker replaces them in place 134 ms later. Warm: 128 to 156 ms after render, already the checker's answer. A live props edit shows its row in 172 ms. Dev-server node process 893 MiB.\n- Worse than expected: (1) the demo Button shows 437 Controls rows, not about 146: about 300 are @types/react DOM, ARIA and event props and about 130 are Chakra condition props (`_active`, `2xl`...); a plain `ComponentProps<'span'>` component shows 280 rows. (2) RDT recall of @types/react props in the CLI output is very low with the checker on: Mantine 0.4%, Chakra about 0%, shadcn 4.9%, antd 23.9% (0.10.0 without the checker: 99% or more). (3) The weekly oracle cannot run Chakra on Node's default heap. (4) 63% of Mantine's oracle verdicts are \"not judged\".\n\n## CLI per corpus: first vs second run (Caliper alone)\n\nMedian of 3 runs under `/usr/bin/time -l`. Command: `extract --src SRC --json --load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies --cache-dir DIR`; first run with an empty DIR, second with DIR kept; structural adds `--no-checker` with an empty DIR. RDT is the weekly's single run (it keeps no cache). Load was 5.7 to 9.1.\n\n| Corpus | First | Second | Structural | RDT | Ratio first / second | JSON size (structural) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Chakra (`packages/react/src`) | 3.50 s / 1,908 MiB | 0.77 s / 476 MiB | 0.49 s / 364 MiB | 22.5 s / 2,847 MiB | 6.4x / 29x | 49.6 MB (6.9 MB) |\n| Mantine core | 1.06 s / 857 MiB | 0.27 s / 370 MiB | 0.11 s / 181 MiB | 1.50 s / 549 MiB | 1.4x / 5.6x | 57.2 MB (6.1 MB) |\n| antd | 1.49 s / 1,072 MiB | 0.08 s / 129 MiB | 0.07 s / 143 MiB | 2.21 s / 1,056 MiB | 1.5x / 28x | 4.6 MB (3.7 MB) |\n| shadcn (`apps/v4`) | 1.41 s / 981 MiB | 0.42 s / 308 MiB | 0.29 s / 351 MiB | 3.83 s / 1,593 MiB | 2.7x / 9.1x | 5.5 MB (8.0 MB) |\n| Spectrum (`packages`) | 1.56 s / 840 MiB | 0.23 s / 207 MiB | 0.16 s / 238 MiB | 2.21 s / 867 MiB | 1.4x / 9.6x | 13.4 MB (7.3 MB) |\n\nThe weekly's own numbers agree (parse caches warm, only the kept answer removed): Chakra 3,497 ms / 1,876 MiB and 761 ms; Mantine 1,069 ms / 853 MiB and 266 ms; antd 1,447 ms / 1,060 MiB and 93 ms; shadcn 1,427 ms / 954 MiB and 430 ms; Spectrum 1,562 ms / 820 MiB and 232 ms. react-docgen took 0.7 to 2.4 s and 209 to 617 MiB.\n\nBudgets (time, memory), all pass: Chakra 3.5 of 18 s and 1,876 of 14,336 MiB; Mantine 1.07 of 4 s and 853 of 2,048 MiB; antd 1.45 of 6 s and 1,060 of 2,048 MiB; shadcn 1.43 of 5.6 s and 954 of 2,048 MiB; Spectrum 1.56 of 6.8 s and 820 of 2,048 MiB.\n\n## Quality\n\nHeadline from the oracle (universe v5, checker on):\n\n| Corpus | Components / props | Correct | Less precise | Wrong | No checker type | Not judged |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Mantine | 332 / 20,148 | 32.7% | 4.3% | 0 | 8 | 62.9% |\n| shadcn | 1,552 / 13,932 | 98.7% | 37 | 0 | 54 | 0.7% |\n| antd | 210 / 4,127 | 93.0% | 2.1% | 1 | 0 | 4.9% |\n| Spectrum | 1,032 / 17,016 | 88.4% | 20 | 7 | 238 | 10.1% |\n| Chakra (rerun with a 16 GB Node heap, exit 0) | 620 / 486,834 | 16.7% (81,451) | 7.8% (37,951) | 0 | n/a | 75.5% (367,432) |\n\nOn the same Chakra props RDT has 10 wrong and 96.8% of the props it lists agree with the checker. Chakra's share confirmed correct was 99.995% on 0.10.0 (no checker): the drop is almost all \"not judged\" (as on Mantine, 0 wrong both times). Cause not found; a likely one is that types cut to their name by the size bound (PR 468) cannot be compared. The weekly's oracle step needs `REDACTED` for Chakra (it dies at about 4 GB).\n\nAgainst the same checker, RDT's wrong count is 9 props on shadcn and 0 elsewhere.\n\nRecall vs RDT (collapse `none`, as the weekly measures it):\n\n| Corpus | Components | Own props | @types/react props |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Mantine | 328/368 (89.1%) | 19,756/19,756 | 283/70,665 (0.4%) |\n| Chakra | 614/664 (92.5%) | 485,975/485,975 | 1/167,353 |\n| shadcn | 1,527/1,573 (97.1%) | 13,567/13,677 (99.2%) | 16,042/330,268 (4.9%) |\n| antd | 188/202 (93.1%) | 3,432/3,455 (99.3%) | 2,658/11,100 (23.9%) |\n| Spectrum | 1,080/1,105 (97.7%) | 16,357/16,359 | 12,973/14,940 (86.8%) |\n\nCollapse, `dependencies` (the addon default) vs `none`: Chakra median props per component 139 vs 844; Chakra's own `Button` lists 146 props plus one `SystemProperties` layer of 705 names, vs 851 props with `none`. Mantine (72), antd (14), shadcn (2) and Spectrum (11) have the same median either way. With `--no-checker` the medians are larger (Chakra 415, Mantine 348, shadcn 280): the checker output drops the DOM props the structural pass lists, which is the same recall drop as above.\n\n## Storybook dev mode\n\nSetup: the harness copies live-demo (storybook 11.0.0-beta.0, vite 8.3.8) into `sb-demo/`; `caliper-docgen-storybook` symlinked to this SHA's `packages/storybook`; napi binding built from this SHA. Options: `semanticWaitMs: 1`, `prefetchStories: 0`. A Playwright sampler polls the Controls rows every 10 ms; times are ms after navigation start. Load 5 to 8, and the Chakra oracle rerun was using one core throughout. Server start to ready 4.93 s (including npx and Vite re-optimizing).\n\n| Case | Story rendered | Controls | Checker answer |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Cold server and cache, Button first visit | 889 ms | 1,780 ms, 437 rows, structural (+891 ms after render) | 1,914 ms in place (+134 ms) |\n| Same server, Button second visit | 828 ms | 956 ms, checker's answer directly (+128 ms) | n/a |\n| Same server, Badge first visit | 834 ms | 971 ms (+137 ms), 280 rows | n/a |\n| Same server, Card first visit | 909 ms | 1,065 ms (+156 ms), 418 rows | n/a |\n| Restart with cache kept, Button (edited before the restart: not a pure cache hit) | 889 ms | 1,264 ms, structural (+375 ms) | 1,370 ms (+106 ms) |\n| Restart with cache kept, Input first visit | 895 ms | 1,040 ms (+145 ms), 445 rows | n/a |\n\nLive edit: adding `fresh?: 'x' | 'y'` to Button's props with the page open showed the new radio row 172 ms after the file write. Memory: the Storybook node process 893 MiB RSS, plus esbuild 16 + 61 MiB and the npm wrapper 92 MiB; no separate checker process. Row content: the collapsed `SystemProperties` layer does not appear as rows (no `bg`, `p`, `m`), but the DOM and condition props do. The roughly 146 figure was not reproduced. Versus the earlier 0.11.0 demo: rows 1,141 to 437; structural-to-checker swap 154 ms to 134 ms.\n\n## vs 0.11.0\n\nNo stored 0.11.0 weekly record exists (the CI weekly of 2026-11-15, run 43686845177, died with exit 143 on \"chakra: Caliper\"; the last green record is 2026-11-09, 0.10.0 with `--no-checker` on a GitHub runner, not comparable). From docs/measurement.md (0.11 plus the PR 468 fix): Chakra then 4.5 s / 6.9 GB, now 3.5 s / 1.9 GB (time -22%, memory -72%); the other four within 0.1 s and 0.05 GB. 0.11.0 as released needed 42 GB on Chakra. Headline vs 0.10.0 (older universe, no checker): Mantine 93.6% to 32.7% (the gap is \"not judged\"; 0 wrong both times), shadcn 94.2% to 98.7%, antd 94.2% to 93.0%, Spectrum 83.8% to 88.4% (1,032 components vs 454).\n\n## What failed or was not measured\n\n- Chakra oracle: OOM at the default Node heap (log tail in `logs/weekly.log`); a rerun with `REDACTED` was unfinished at hand-back.\n- A quiet machine was never reached (load 5 to 10).\n- Neighbour vs distant story with prefetch: not measured. antd in Storybook: Vite fails with `Failed to resolve import \"./version\"` (generated file). No big Mantine or antd story measured. Not recorded: warm-restart ready time, RDT's dev-server cost, a Badge screenshot.\n- Cold run clears only Caliper's cache directory; the OS file cache was warm.\n- Not diagnosed: the @types/react recall drop and the 437 rows. Both look like checker-mode output omitting or not collapsing DOM props (ADR 0028 \"ambient\" props); not checked whether that is intended.\n\n## Commands\n\nBuild (Rust 1.99.1 first on PATH): `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=oracle-run/target cargo build --release --locked -p caliper-docgen`; `pnpm install --offline --ignore-scripts --frozen-lockfile`; napi: `pnpm --filter caliper-docgen-napi build:napi` with `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=oracle-run/target-napi`, then `pnpm --filter caliper-docgen-storybook build`. Weekly (`run-weekly.sh`, load 8.59 at start): `scripts/weekly.py --bin oracle-run/target/release/caliper-docgen --corpora caliper-fixtures/corpora --work oracle-run/work --runs 2 --oracle --enforce-budgets --previous weekly-2026-11-09/weekly/weekly.json --out oracle-run/weekly.json --markdown oracle-run/weekly.md --issue oracle-run/issue.md`. First/second runs: `run-fs.sh` calling `first-second.sh BIN 3 chakra mantine antd shadcn spectrum`. Storybook: `sb-demo/serve.sh LOG cold`; setup in `sb-demo/setup-stories.sh`.\n","numLines":87,"startLine":1,"totalLines":87}},"displayPath":"../../../../caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/REPORT.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"afe02cfc-bf25-419d-b0be-56b7bf2c8f06","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:34:25.563Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/REPORT.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t# caliper measurement at origin/main de016f69 (2026-11-15)\n2\t\n3\tSHA `de016f69c3b021aaf3223420faf7866087ded864` (merge of #483; binary reports 0.11.0, unreleased main). `git fetch` was blocked in the worker's sandbox, so this is the last fetched origin/main. The machine was shared with other agents: the 1-minute load average stayed 5 to 10 during every timed step, so every timing is inflated. Memory and sizes are not affected. Written by the lead from the measurement worker's report; the raw files are in this directory (`weekly.json`, `weekly.md`, `issue.md`, `logs/`, `fs/`, `work/`, `sb-demo/`).\n4\t\n5\t## Summary\n6\t\n7\t- First run (empty cache, checker on, addon config): Chakra 3.50 s / 1,908 MiB, Mantine 1.06 s / 857 MiB, antd 1.49 s / 1,072 MiB, shadcn 1.41 s / 981 MiB, Spectrum 1.56 s / 840 MiB. 1.4x (Mantine, Spectrum) to 6.4x (Chakra) faster than react-docgen-typescript (RDT). All five within the budgets (`weekly.py --enforce-budgets` exit 0).\n8\t- Second run (kept checker answer): Chakra 0.77 s / 476 MiB, Mantine 0.27 s, antd 0.08 s, shadcn 0.42 s, Spectrum 0.23 s: 5.6x to 29x faster than RDT. Structural floor (`--no-checker`) 0.07 to 0.49 s.\n9\t- Quality (share of the props of reported components the checker confirms): shadcn 98.7%, antd 93.0%, Spectrum 88.4%, Mantine 32.7% (62.9% not judged, 0 wrong). Wrong props: shadcn 0, antd 1, Spectrum 7, Mantine 0. Chakra: not measured, the oracle died of a Node heap OOM.\n10\t- Storybook dev mode, cold (browser, demo Button over Chakra ButtonProps): structural Controls 891 ms after the story renders, the checker replaces them in place 134 ms later. Warm: 128 to 156 ms after render, already the checker's answer. A live props edit shows its row in 172 ms. Dev-server node process 893 MiB.\n11\t- Worse than expected: (1) the demo Button shows 437 Controls rows, not about 146: about 300 are @types/react DOM, ARIA and event props and about 130 are Chakra condition props (`_active`, `2xl`...); a plain `ComponentProps<'span'>` component shows 280 rows. (2) RDT recall of @types/react props in the CLI output is very low with the checker on: Mantine 0.4%, Chakra about 0%, shadcn 4.9%, antd 23.9% (0.10.0 without the checker: 99% or more). (3) The weekly oracle cannot run Chakra on Node's default heap. (4) 63% of Mantine's oracle verdicts are \"not judged\".\n12\t\n13\t## CLI per corpus: first vs second run (Caliper alone)\n14\t\n15\tMedian of 3 runs under `/usr/bin/time -l`. Command: `extract --src SRC --json --load-dependencies --collapse-inherited-props dependencies --cache-dir DIR`; first run with an empty DIR, second with DIR kept; structural adds `--no-checker` with an empty DIR. RDT is the weekly's single run (it keeps no cache). Load was 5.7 to 9.1.\n16\t\n17\t| Corpus | First | Second | Structural | RDT | Ratio first / second | JSON size (structural) |\n18\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n19\t| Chakra (`packages/react/src`) | 3.50 s / 1,908 MiB | 0.77 s / 476 MiB | 0.4