{"parentUuid":"8ec1671a-9f47-4ab3-b5eb-902ab3fad496","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KoMWkTUyKNzi9qewFT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DxjjM3rS4gpfVd6LivDwdE","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ace6850035594237c","summary":"add change 8: no body means unknown, not nothing used","message":"Add rule-level change 8 (do it after Step 1, with Step 2). Evidence: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/pattern-eval-mui-radix.md. MUI's components are declaration-only (`.d.ts` beside `.js`; the extractor reads the `.d.ts`), so there is NO body. Today the usage signal is empty, which 490 treats as 'nothing used', so main's notable-inherited rows `className`, `style`, `ref` vanish on 27/32/14 MUI components (Dialog loses ref+style, Popover ref+style, Tooltip className+style, TextField ref). This is silence-as-evidence (class C1): absence of a body is UNKNOWN, not 'uses nothing'. Rule: when a component has no analysable body (declaration-only, `declare const X: ...`, `.d.ts`, type-only export, unresolved body), the relevance decision must not narrow by usage: keep exactly what main listed for that component (main props in full plus the notable inherited set for its element), and say so in the placement (an explicit 'body unknown' state, not an empty used set). Encode it in the same decision function as the other cases (no special case at the call site; an exhaustive match, no `_ =>`), with a test that a `.d.ts` component keeps className/style/ref and a model test over {body: analysed-complete, analysed-handed-on, absent}. Also record in the PR note (not for you to fix): MUI `Button`/`Select` (`declare const Button: ExtendButtonBase<ButtonTypeMap>`, `OverridableComponent`) are not extracted at all by either binary; that is an extraction gap outside this PR; tell me the root cause in one line if you see it while in the code. Re-run the MUI/Radix harness at the end: `/Users/gabe/