{"parentUuid":"6c7fde80-2431-4dd4-8e53-57f78dd45047","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7L2FyjP9RKDPBtoq7vW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The weekly-oracle fix is pushed as `fix/weekly-oracle-measurement` at 21320206, and linked to trail 405. Entire will open the PR, and I'll publish its body from `~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/pr/fix-weekly-oracle-measurement.md` once it exists.\n\nI reran the checks the worker couldn't: `just lint` exits 0 (the worker's exit 1 was only the sandbox blocking the npm registry). The worker reported `test-py`, `doc-check`, `machete` and `typos` at exit 0, and I did not rerun those. I did not run the oracle itself, and I checked the diff only through the worker's summary.\n\nFor a record with Chakra's numbers, the weekly now shows:\n- **Headline:** 68.2% correct among judged props (81,451 of 119,402).\n- **Coverage:** 24.5% of props judged.\n- **Not judged:** 75.5%, now its own column.\n- **Floor:** a coverage floor at 50% that fires on that record.\n\nThe coverage floor is new gating, so you should decide whether it stays. It would flag Chakra and Mantine on every weekly until the cause of \"not judged\" is found. The Node heap for Chakra and the clearer handling of signal deaths are in the same change. The worker found the layered-recall metric already existed, so that part needed no change.\n\nThe acceptance command, the Chakra memory split and the Phase 1 rule changes are still running."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":423,"cache_read_input_tokens":149775,"output_tokens":482,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":423,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"o