{"parentUuid":"eb812b40-c3f3-4f20-a4bf-20065c74c505","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7L8FpjPXB7Bc3AfW2fU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The acceptance command works, and #490's current head (d884334e) passes all five of its checks.\n\n- **The command:** `zsh ~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/accept/accept.sh <binary> <addon packages/storybook dir> <label>`. It runs a CLI exit check, a decoder check against `--format rdt`, the Storybook rows in a real browser against the CLI rows, and the antd and shadcn oracle.\n- **Storybook Button** shows 21 rows in the browser: `children`, `as`, `asChild`, `css`, `extra`, `fresh`, `html*`, `kind`, `loading`, `loadingText`, `recipe`, `size`, `spinner`, `spinnerPlacement`, `tone`, `unstyled` and `variant`. That matches the 20 rows I verified in the CLI, plus `children`, which Storybook adds from args. The 286 / 706 / 130 noise members stay out.\n- **Badge** shows `children`, `asChild` and `variant`.\n- **Oracle:** shadcn 98.7% correct with 0 wrong, antd 93.0% with 1 wrong. Both are unchanged from the baseline.\n\nThe timings in the report are not official, since the machine is shared with the other workers.\n\nWhen the Phase 1 worker lands, I run the same command on its build, so Storybook rows, CLI rows and the oracle are re-checked without further setup. Only the Phase 1 worker and the Chakra memory split are still running."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1091,"cache_read_input_tokens":150198,"output_tokens":500,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1091,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":500,"cache_read_input_tokens":150198