{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","bridgeSessionId":"cse_013R2ytvK9B32ZaSUaSe6aAZ","lastSequenceNum":15975,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"29d1fece-807b-4a25-b2ec-165816855c80","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7LsouDn2xNxQfeQa7rC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Chakra memory split is in, and I've started the memory slice it recommends.\n\n**Where Chakra's memory goes** (1,604 MiB when all components are answered):\n\n| Share | MiB |\n|---|---|\n| tsrs checker | about 320 (heap 162, arenas 159) |\n| Our converter | about 570, of which the memo is 480 and is never freed |\n| Structural data | about 200 |\n| Allocator slack | about 510 |\n\nThe memo holds 3.6M type nodes but only about 7.5k distinct ones, so it is mostly duplicated copies. Interning them is a go, with an estimated saving of 330 to 410 MiB.\n\n**Under 1 GiB is not reachable with this alone.** Even combined with the #491 instantiation fix, the report puts Chakra's peak at about 1.05 to 1.1 GiB. Getting below 1 GiB needs further work on the converter (the report's other parts) or on the allocator slack. Chakra is the extreme case. shadcn and the others are already near 0.9 to 1 GiB.\n\n**The worker** (Opus, 90 calls):\n- **Scope:** only the shared memo values in `crates/semantic/src/convert.rs`. It makes no public type changes, and it stops and reports if that turns out to be impossible.\n- **Output check:** output must stay byte-identical on Chakra, Mantine, antd, shadcn, Spectrum and the demo.\n- **Memory check:** it reports peak RSS before and after on Chakra, shadcn and Mantine, and aims for Chakra at least 300 MiB lower.\n- **Time and gates:** time must not regress by more than 5%. It runs the memory and determinism gates and an awaited `/code-review medium`.\n\n**Running now:** the Phase 1 rule-change worker and this memory slice. They touch different crates (`core` and `semantic`), so they won't collide. The report is at `~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/memory-split.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5547,"cache_read_input_tokens":160063,"output_tokens":663,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5547,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":663,"cache_read_input_tokens":160063,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5547,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5547},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"83aaa7f1-d973-4209-b601-e8bd66505ec8","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch7Lsok4LdPrUxvPmeXSD","requestRef":"a81eaa33-a2a7-49ab-b08c-9c0ce3957bb3","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5f97ccb5-ccd6-4f5d-acdb-fa4ebbea55e3","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:48:38.388Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
