every call. It runs once per member inside the per-layer loop, even though the layer's answer is the same for all its members.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A Chakra component with a `SystemProperties` layer of thousands of members makes thousands of String pairs plus a path scan per component on each `apply`. Compute `ambient` once per layer before the member loop, and key `private` so a borrowed `(&amp;str, &amp;str)` can look it up.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/core/src/relevance/mod.rs\",\n    \"line\": 146,\n    \"summary\": \"`narrow` now clones every layer member name into a `BTreeSet&lt;String&gt;` on every call, including when no prop is left out. Before, it allocated nothing in that case.\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"`narrow` runs on `apply` and again at the end of every checker merge (session and CLI). A component with a 4,000-member layer pays about 4,000 String allocations and a tree build per call. Build the set lazily on the first left-out prop, or use borrowed keys or indices.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/core/src/react_types.rs\",\n    \"line\": 455,\n    \"summary\": \"The doc comment on `react_prop_listed` still reads \\\"[`checker_prop_used`] without the mode it no longer reads\\\". This change makes `checker_prop_used` read `mode` again (`Full` takes every React prop).\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"A maintainer reading this doc will assume mode is ignored and keep both merges on `react_prop_listed`, which is how the CLI/session split in finding 1 happened.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"crates/core/src/relevance/mod.rs\",\n    \"line\": 137,\n    \"summary\": \"This breaks /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8/AGENTS.md: \\\"Comments: only the non-obvious why, no history (the commit records it). Fill to 120 columns\\\". The rewritten doc line is 139 columns, and line 90 adds history: \\\"(Entire finding on change 288)\\\".\",\n    \"failure_scenario\": \"Other added lines also exceed 120 col