{"parentUuid":"c60f7f12-0126-4c21-abee-0a1defcc766d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7MPfDSFaF29dcLi3bhP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Step 1 of the #490 rule fixes is committed locally and green. It is not pushed. The Phase 1 worker's first run has finished and I've resumed it for the remainder.\n\n**Done, at 4c22b134 on `fix/list-rule-patterns`**\n- **Ambient:** it now means React's own types, or an interface its library marks `@private` or `@internal`. This restores `excludeFromTabOrder` and `routerOptions` (146 hidden rows → 0), and Spectrum gains `id` and `aria-label*`.\n- **Spectrum:** median 6 → 11, total 18,739 → 23,761.\n- **shadcn:** total 11,142 → 11,700, median unchanged at 3.\n- **Chakra's own repo `Button`:** 147 → 17 rows, and the corpus median 139 → 9.\n- **Gates:** all exit 0. That covers nextest (1,654 passed), lint, doc-check, machete, typos, the checker lane, test-ts and semver.\n- **Memory:** shadcn 970 and Chakra 1,820 MiB, unchanged.\n- **Layer names:** kept.\n- **Probes:** both lanes agree on all of them. Pass: i, ii, iv, vii, viii, ix. Still failing, and Step 2 fixes them: iii (aliases), v (reads into large layers), the mapped-copy case in vi, and hook hand-offs.\n\n**Findings on #490**\n- `relevance/mod.rs:84-90` (the quadratic scan) is fixed.\n- `react_types.rs:452` (`none` losing React props) is fixed only in the session lane. The CLI merge still has it, and the review caught that.\n\n**Still open, now in the resumed worker's brief:**\n- The 10 review findings, including the CLI-merge half above.\n- Step 2.\n- Change 8 (MUI `.d.ts` components with no body).\n- The Chakra fixture, still about 865 rows: the worker must say why change 3 didn't reduce it and fix it if that's a rule gap.\n- The main-props differential and the demo `Button` rows, which weren't re-run.\n- ADR and changeset, plus a full awaited `/code-review`.\n\nI won't push until all of that is green, and then I run the acceptance command on the final build. The converter-memo worker is also running."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4843,"cache_read_input_tokens":167143,"output_tokens":772,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4843,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":772,"cache_read_input_tokens":167143,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4843,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4843},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.13.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.16.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.22.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.28.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.31.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.31.content.1","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"},{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.36.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"14f54291-0e19-4e55-bf23-dbe2145d7189","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch7MPf2WeVxzTzDCAH3C9","requestRef":"7724b862-b03a-4873-b577-b54c82afb32b","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2141823e-2e23-4170-b92a-ce65323e852a","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:55:23.847Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort"