{"parentUuid":"4b1cc941-4af9-4fd4-8fb2-9f20bcc51cb5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7evoeH8UUqqm71qzAvF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't removed anything, because the subagents themselves need no cleanup and the real clutter is worktrees that another session is already handling.\n\n**Subagents:** six of the seven are finished and hold nothing. The only live one is the #490 rule-change worker (`ace6850…`), and it must keep running.\n\n**Worktrees:** `git worktree list` shows about 60 worktrees under `.claude/worktrees/`, around 25 of them locked. Most belong to PRs that already merged (the factory, collapse, jsx, scheduler and relevance branches).\n\nThe peer session `cleanup-merged-branches-worktrees` is busy right now and has been running for 5 days, so it is probably already doing this. A second sweep from me could race it, so I'd leave the merged ones to it.\n\n**What I should not touch:**\n- `agent-ace6850…` (`fix/list-rule-patterns`) is live, and its commit 53d45655 is local only. Removing it would lose work.\n- Worktrees for the weekly-oracle and converter-memo branches are pushed, but their PRs aren't open yet.\n- `agent-a8954…` (#491) and `docs/*` are tied to open PRs.\n\nI can do either of these:\n1. Message the cleanup session to ask for its status and pass it my keep-list.\n2. Remove only the worktrees I created in this stretch, once their branches are pushed and their PRs merged. That means the pattern-eval, MUI/Radix, acceptance, weekly-oracle and memory-split workers' worktrees.\n\nWhich do you want? I recommend the first, since it avoids any race."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5316,"cache_read_input_tokens":188566,"output_tokens":848,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":323},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"serv