{"parentUuid":"4a1c7d4b-580a-4a89-a109-75baef6be4ed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7gJ8oQPcnS3mVV6HKEX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KZY3MgpoaTUrUMcDPspS1r","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ace6850035594237c","summary":"2 new 490 findings (one class): fix first, then C/7/D","message":"Pushed cf51133b to PR 490 (CI pending, acceptance all pass). Two NEW Entire findings on that head; they are ONE CLASS: a prop is explicitly selected or read but one owner does not see it as listed. (1) crates/core/src/resolver/chain.rs:597-599 (Medium, 0.94): reading a non-curated member of a collapsed source now exposes it through `notable_inherited`, but the checker still treats it as layer-only: `LayerFacts::of` lists only `entry.props`, and `layer_notable` recognizes only curated names (types/semantic.rs:578-588, 623-628), so checker conversion/merging skips this visible prop, leaving its structural approximation even for checker-resolvable types such as `ReturnType<typeof makeValue>`. Fix: the checker's keep-and-merge decision must include body-promoted notable props (one owner for 'which names are visible rows': the checker must consume the same decision, not re-derive from curated names). (2) crates/core/src/relevance/props_type.rs:164-165 (Medium, 0.93): `type Select<T, K extends keyof T> = Pick<T, K>` with a component taking `Select<React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>, 'id'>`: the default view collapses the explicitly selected `id` unless usage promotes it; the resolver substitutes the arguments (resolver/chain.rs:272) but this branch skips generic aliases and `read` examines the unsubstituted `K` (props_type.rs:79); ambient members stay eligible for narrowing despite the `declined` flag (relevance/mod.rs:58). Fix: substitute alias arguments when collecting picked keys (and any other declined-key-set form: Omit through a generic alias, nested aliases, `keyof` of an argument, intersections of such aliases) so deliberately selected props stay listed. Do the class, not the two cases: (a) a grammar sweep over every way a key set can be explicit (Pick/Omit direct, through generic alias with arguments, alias of alias, mapped over a literal union, keyof an instantiated argument, indexed access, ComponentProps wrappers) with the TypeScript checker/API as the oracle for what the set is, a model test over the generated forms comparing the structural lane's listing against the checker lane's, mutation proofs, and (b) a model test that every name that is a visible row in the structural output is kept by the checker merge, for body-promoted names of every source kind. Failing-first tests, guards as ALLOW-lists. Commit on fix/list-rule-patterns (merge, never rebase). Then, in SEPARATE later commits: C (no analysable body = unknown, keep what main listed: MUI .d.ts components), change 7 (hook hand-off as forwarding), D (Chakra fixture rule gap: why the `declined` guard blocks it and whether the guard is right). Do the two findings FIRST and tell me as soon as that commit is green (message me with the SHA and the gate results: nextest, lint, doc-check, machete, typos, test-checker-lane, differential 0 violations, demo Button 20 names); I push it, then you continue with C/7/D. Run `/code-review medium` on the SHA range (awaited) before each hand-off. Budget 110 tool calls. Final message at most 80 words.","type":"message","recipient":"ace6850035594237c","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Pushed cf51133b to PR 490 (CI pending, acceptance…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1411,"cache_read_input_tokens":215253,"output_tokens":1544,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":319},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1411,"ephe