te alias arguments when collecting picked keys (and any other declined-key-set form: Omit through a generic alias, nested aliases, `keyof` of an argument, intersections of such aliases) so deliberately selected props stay listed. Do the class, not the two cases: (a) a grammar sweep over every way a key set can be explicit (Pick/Omit direct, through generic alias with arguments, alias of alias, mapped over a literal union, keyof an instantiated argument, indexed access, ComponentProps wrappers) with the TypeScript checker/API as the oracle for what the set is, a model test over the generated forms comparing the structural lane's listing against the checker lane's, mutation proofs, and (b) a model test that every name that is a visible row in the structural output is kept by the checker merge, for body-promoted names of every source kind. Failing-first tests, guards as ALLOW-lists. Commit on fix/list-rule-patterns (merge, never rebase). Then, in SEPARATE later commits: C (no analysable body = unknown, keep what main listed: MUI .d.ts components), change 7 (hook hand-off as forwarding), D (Chakra fixture rule gap: why the `declined` guard blocks it and whether the guard is right). Do the two findings FIRST and tell me as soon as that commit is green (message me with the SHA and the gate results: nextest, lint, doc-check, machete, typos, test-checker-lane, differential 0 violations, demo Button 20 names); I push it, then you continue with C/7/D. Run `/code-review medium` on the SHA range (awaited) before each hand-off. Budget 110 tool calls. Final message at most 80 words."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"86cd0dc3-cbcb-4614-8bbb-8f89efc9c94c","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch7gJ8SppegCJ7MSte1Fx","requestRef":"97e4bdb2-628f-4e4c-90db-ade6ccf825c8","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a6d4897f-f418-441c-9c01-bfa7a08c678f","timestamp":"2026-11-17T02:03:24.651Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessi