{"parentUuid":"71b0a513-6123-4d06-a554-9716f0b660ee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7jSLtzxYm57pc8BtEDj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Paste this into a fresh session at `~/Projects/caliper`:\n\n````\nYou are the lead/coordinator for caliper's road to v1 alpha (Storybook integration is the product's purpose). Read first: ~/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper/memory/MEMORY.md (and the memories it links), ~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/worker-contract.md (workers' rules and the pre-push gate), AGENTS.md, and ~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/{REPORT,pattern-eval,pattern-eval-mui-radix,memory-split,memory-profile}.md. Date of this handoff: 2026-11-16.\n\n## Product rule (the user's, non-negotiable)\nStorybook Controls must list EVERYTHING in the component's main props even if no story uses it, plus whatever the component body itself uses directly (reads, destructures, passes explicitly; never through a DOM spread). Big generated/ambient sources (DOM/ARIA/event attributes, style-system props) stay as names in a layer. Decide by provenance and structure, never by name lists. Fix classes of problems and patterns, not one-off components (\"produce the best results, not overwhelming numbers\"). colorPalette staying hidden is fine. Say \"the TypeScript checker (on by default)\", not \"add-on\" (the exact wording sweep of docs/changesets is not done; confirm meaning first).\nAlpha = someone installs the Storybook addon on a real design system and gets correct Controls fast on first and second start, with plain statements of what's missing; no stability/API freeze needed.\n\n## Process rules\n- Workers run in isolated worktrees; the lead pushes their branches (`git push origin <sha>:<branch>`, never force, merge main in rather than rebase), then `entire trail link 405 --branch <b> --base main --repo gh/orin-dx/caliper` (Entire opens the PR; don't `gh pr create` unless the user approves the shim/Touch ID). Publish bodies with `gh pr edit N --title ... --body-file ~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/pr/<name>.md`. Trail 404 = Chakra memory regression, 405 = relevance/collapse/Storybook usefulness.\n- Pre-push gate for workers: invariants in PR body, grammar sweep with the TS checker as oracle, mutation proofs, ALLOW-list guards, `/code-review medium` awaited, `just lint doc-check machete typos`, nextest, test-checker-lane when checker code changes. Lead reruns `just lint` itself (workers' sandbox blocks pnpm).\n- After a verified fix, resolve the Entire finding yourself citing commit + test: `entire trail finding list caliper/<change> --freshness=any ...`. Findings for the same class: fix the class, not the case.\n- Constraints: oracle/corpus runs cost money (only when asked; `scripts/weekly.py --oracle --corpus antd --corpus shadcn` is authorized for acceptance; never --agent-eval); no files in /tmp (use ~/Projects/caliper-fixtures or $TMPDIR); no new scripts/options without CI/weekly value; workers: Sonnet for mechanical, Opus for provenance/design, caps on tool calls, no polling CI, max 3 parallel workers; release actions (rerun, delete assets, re-dispatch, RELEASE_PENDING_FROM) need the user's say-so; measure peak RSS and time for resolver/checker changes; git inside worktree sessions: plain single commands, no `cd` to other worktrees, no compound `$(...)`.\n- Never merge or release anything without the user's approval; the user approves/merges PRs.\n\n## State\nMerged on main: Chakra 42 GB fix, collapse default 'dependencies', scheduler S1/S2, factory own props, relevance output, #491 (instantiation memory), #489 (alpha limits docs), #487 (Wisp v5).\nOpen PRs (all BLOCKED on CI/approval at last look): \n- #490 `feat/list-props-by-usage` (change 288, trail 405): T4 listing rule (main props + body use). Remote head cf51133b. Acceptance (oracle-run/accept/accept.sh) passed 5/5 on it: Storybook Button 21 rows (20 + children), Badge children/asChild/variant, shadcn 98.7%/0 wrong, antd 93.0%/1 wrong; differential 0 violations on 7 corpora; peak RSS shadcn 879 / Chakra 1,627 MiB. TWO OPEN ENTIRE FINDINGS (one class: explicit selection not seen by both owners): chain.rs:597-599 (checker keep-and-merge must include body-promoted notable props; types/semantic.rs LayerFacts::of / layer_notable) and relevance/props_type.rs:164-165 (substitute generic-alias args when collecting picked keys). A worker (agent ace6850035594237c, worktree .claude/worktrees/agent-ace6850035594237c, branch fix/list-rule-patterns) was mid-fix when the session ended; check its worktree (`git status`, `git log`), finish or restart: class fix with grammar sweep + model test that every visible structural row survives the checker merge + mutation proofs, then push to feat/list-props-by-usage and resolve both findings. Afterwards, separate commits: change 8 (no analysable body = unknown, keep what main listed: MUI .d.ts components lose className/style/ref), change 7 (hook hand-off useX(props) as forwarding), D (Chakra fixture still ~865 rows: the `declined` guard blocks the generated rule; decide if the guard is right). Evidence: pattern-eval.md lists 7 rule-level changes (1-6 done in #490: ambient by declaring interface, member ambient only if all declarations ambient, generated rule for project sources, reads promote from large layers, mapped-copy by key interface nature, one-hop aliases).\n- #492 `fix/weekly-oracle-measurement` (change 290): Node heap 16 GB for Chakra oracle, \"not judged\" as its own column, headline over judged props, coverage floor 50% (new gate: ask the user whether it stays), recall counts layer names.\n- Change 291 `perf/converter-memo-interning` (HEAD 1335c3d2 pushed, linked to trail 405): converter memo interning, Chakra peak 1,690 -> 1,366 MiB, output identical. NO PR was opened by Entire yet; check `gh pr list --head perf/converter-memo-interning --state all`; if still none ask the user (shim needs Touch ID). Publish body from ~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/pr/perf-converter-memo-interning.md.\n- #497 callisto/version-packages (release PR, not reviewed), #493-#496 dependabot.\n\n## Next\n1. Land #490's findings fix (above), push, check CI/Entire, resolve findings, rerun accept.sh on the new head: `zsh ~/Projects/caliper-fixtures/oracle-run/accept/accept.sh <bin> <packages/storybook dir with napi build> <label>`; MUI/Radix: `oracle-run/pattern-eval/run-extra.sh <main-bin> <490-bin>`.\n2. Chakra memory: ~1.1-1.2 GiB expected after #491 + memo interning; under 1 GiB needs more converter work (memory-split.md parts), not required for alpha.\n3. Weekly: merge #492 then run the oracle once on merged main (idle machine), refresh docs/STATUS.md speed numbers; weekly \"not judged\" cause (Chakra 75.5%, Mantine 62.9%) undiagnosed.\n4. Unmeasured: Storybook prefetch, antd in Storybook (Vite `./version` import fails), head-to-head vs react-docgen-typescript.\n5. MUI `Button`/`Select` (OverridableComponent/ExtendButtonBase declare const) aren't extracted by either binary: separate extraction gap, ask the user if it should be a slice.\n\n## Needs the user's decision (ask early)\n- 0.11.0 release recovery (E167 ArtifactAssetDiffers): delete mismatched asset + `gh workflow run callisto-release.yml --ref main -f release_source_sha=<sha>`, or skip via RELEASE_PENDING_FROM; is #497 the vehicle? (corpora budget gate never ran on a real release PR.)\n- Should the addon default flip (collapseInheritedProps 'dependencies') ship in the first alpha? Alpha audience? Coverage floor on the weekly (#492)? Worktree cleanup: ~60 stale worktrees under .claude/worktrees (peer session cleanup-merged-branches-worktrees did a sweep; don't remove live ones).\n\nStart by checking `gh pr list`, `gh pr checks 490`, Entire findings for caliper/288, 290, 291, and the worker worktree state, then continue with step 1 and report.\n````"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":61,"cache_read_input_tokens":244364,"output_tokens":3129,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":54},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":61,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3129,"cache_read_input_tokens":244364,"cache_creation_input_tokens":61,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":61},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e9e9c411-d790-48b6-a0e9-5052a46f4a29","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch7jSLYfZNPcEAkCqyfW3","requestRef":"24c479b7-6986-4c57-881c-205dd8c98051","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"aa794f82-bd5d-4760-8386-3010525e9a21","timestamp":"2026-11-17T02:44:46.302Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
