{"parentUuid":"9f255a5e-5b6a-4625-81f8-9f1d5e80f517","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7k5foL9mjH9mczMqi6G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing is downloading or extracting right now, and I can't pin down what opened the windows.\n\n- **Current activity:** the other lead is running `cargo nextest` (1 minute old) and a `ccstatusline` npm check just started. Neither opens windows. No curl, tar, unzip or Archive Utility process is running.\n- **Apple's asset downloader:** `MobileAssetDaemon` has been up for 23 minutes. It's a normal macOS background service and not one of ours.\n- **Playwright browsers:** the Playwright cache (`~/Library/Caches/ms-playwright`) already has Chromium 1248, the headless shell and ffmpeg, so a fresh Playwright launch wouldn't need to download anything.\n\nThe most likely source is the Playwright MCP servers starting up (`npx @playwright/mcp@latest` re-resolves on each new session, which can show an npm download) and opening browser windows when workers drove the Storybook checks. That would match the little windows appearing while several agents and the new lead session started at once. It's a guess, not something I observed.\n\nIf it happens again, tell me roughly what the window showed (a progress bar, a browser page or a Finder window) and I'll check what is running at that moment."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1242,"cache_read_input_tokens":261877,"output_tokens":402,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1242,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":402,"cache_read_input_tokens":261877,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1242,"cache_creation":{"e