{"parentUuid":"dbed565a-f16b-43b3-adbe-a09f48833cda","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch97zBXQLE5dPVxUzPZxu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not everything is done, but the main blocker has moved. The other lead pushed #490's findings fix, so its head is now 453f2aea. Entire shows no open findings on change 288, and no check on #490 is failing. #490 is open and waiting for your approval.\n\n**Where things stand**\n- **#490:** the findings fix is pushed and Entire shows nothing open. It is ready for your review and merge. I haven't looked at the diff of that push or the new CI results myself, because the other lead did that work.\n- **#492 (weekly-oracle fix):** open and waiting on you.\n- **Change 291 (converter memo):** the branch is pushed at 1335c3d2, but there is still no PR. That needs your go-ahead to open through the shim, with Touch ID.\n- **#497 (release PR):** open and unreviewed, with four dependabot PRs. #491 and an Entire hook fix (#498) have merged.\n\n**Still undone**\n- **Change 8:** MUI's `.d.ts` components still lose `className`, `style` and `ref`.\n- **Change 7:** hook hand-offs as forwarding.\n- **Chakra fixture:** still about 865 rows.\n- **0.11.0 release recovery:** needs your decision.\n- **After merges:** a fresh oracle run on the merged `main` and the `STATUS.md` speed numbers.\n- **Alpha decisions:** audience, whether the addon default flip ships, and whether the 50% coverage floor in #492 stays.\n\nThe code work for this round is finished. What's left is your merges and decisions, then the pattern gaps above as follow-up slices."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":839,"cache_read_input_tokens":271502,"output_tokens":531,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","ca