{"parentUuid":"dc03b479-2cc4-453a-9cb3-3fb3c1dabbaf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch984psKJsBmxC4R5sbJE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Change 291 now has the real work on it. `perf/converter-memo-interning` is at 06f6eccf, and the remote head matches. It's a fast-forward push, with no force.\n\n**What went wrong:** I told you the converter-memo branch was pushed with a 324 MiB saving. It wasn't. My first push sent a local branch that sat at a `main` commit (1335c3d2) and not the worker's commit. The branch therefore had no diff against `main`, and that is why Entire never opened a PR. I saw the SHA mismatch when the worker reported and didn't verify it. The worker's measurement was real, but the branch you saw contained none of it.\n\n**What's on the branch now:** 3 files, +242 and −39 lines: `convert.rs` (the interning), a one-line change in `lib.rs`, and a changeset.\n\n**The finding on change 291:** `resolver/named.rs:609-614`, where `enum Level { Low = 1 << 2 }` with `--no-checker` produces the string `\"Low\"` instead of the number `4`. That file isn't in this diff, and the finding was raised against the empty branch. It is probably a bug in code already on `main`, and it may be real. I haven't confirmed that, and I haven't touched it. Entire will rerun its review on the new push. If it stays open, the fix is separate from the memory change, and I'd send it to a worker as its own slice.\n\n**What happens next:**\n- Entire should now open the PR for change 291, since there's a diff. I'll check shortly and report if it doesn't.\n- CI will run on the real code. The worker skipped some gates after its last review fix, so CI is the first run of those."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":406,"cache_read_input_tokens":278865,"output_tokens":679,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":139},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":406,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":679,"cache_read_input_tokens":278865,"cache_creation_input_tokens":406,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":406},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f973903a-52b5-4c6f-aab0-0f0cfdda6f4f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch984pahuyihR37XG5skZ","requestRef":"ddc6b722-f297-464c-9389-1ca16037ab02","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ae5e8480-cc62-452d-8511-179d309c7f4c","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:21:51.660Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
