{"parentUuid":"d8ee568a-721a-40db-a223-5d551e5a3e53","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch98mvVZFwZ7S8eJYX8PC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, the Audit check fails on every open PR, and a worker is now fixing it on `main`.\n\n**Open PRs with a failing check**\n- **Audit** (`cargo deny`) fails on #493, #499, #500, #501 and #502. #499 is the converter-memo PR for change 291, which now exists since I pushed the right commit. #499's only failing check is Audit, and its code wasn't causing it.\n- **#497** (the release PR) fails only on Entire Gates.\n\n**The fix.** The worker (Sonnet, 40 calls) runs `cargo deny` itself and lists every failing advisory with the dependency path that pulls it in. For each one it first tries a real upgrade, then reruns the tests. It adds an ignore entry to `deny.toml` only where no safe upgrade exists and our code can't hit the problem the advisory describes. Each ignore carries a written reason and a review-by date 30 days out, and no other `deny` setting is weakened. Its report names each advisory and says whether it was upgraded or ignored.\n\n**Next steps.** When it reports, I push, link and merge `main` into the open PRs so their Audit reruns. That should turn #493, #499, #500, #501 and #502 green, except where a PR has its own failures. #496 had real npm failures, so it may still fail on those.\n\nMerged since the last check: #490 (20:21 UTC) and #492 (the weekly-oracle fix). I haven't looked at the post-merge CI results."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4862,"cache_read_input_tokens":292305,"output_tokens":485,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4862,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":485,"cache_read_input_tokens":292305,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4862,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4862},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"9c137631-9382-4da6-acd1-35d3821897cf","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch98mvDg7cEg8aUJsBkzR","requestRef":"9e03f354-d347-4dc0-a030-a23df9405ec4","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c6b0b0a4-0b5a-47b4-bf19-66823feed02b","timestamp":"2026-11-17T20:31:07.448Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf-t4","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
